// Generated by tools/build_library.py: do not edit by hand.
window.F3_LIBRARY = {"source":"F3 Nation Exicon (https://f3nation.com/exicon)","builtAt":"2026-10-16","count":977,"items":[{"id":"x-0-50-500","name":"0-50-500","text":"Partner Field Progression\n• Partner up with each PAX starting on opposite goal lines of a football field.\n• One side is designated to start as runners, the other for the called exercise. Each partner will switch (run/exercise) throughout.\nRound Flow:\nAt “Go”, PAX runners run to the opposite 5-yard line (= 95 yards) while other side does called exercise.\n• Once running partner arrives to stated yard line, he begins called exercise, while other partner then switches to run to opposite 5-yard line (also 95 yards). When arrives, he calls his partner’s name to begin his next run while he then switches back to called exercise.\n• For the second “leg”, Pax runner then goes back to 10-yard line on the opposite side, while the other partner is doing the exercise\n• Continue this pattern, increasing by 5 yards each direction of the field, which will get shorter with every switch. (15, 20, 25, etc.).\n• Continue until both partners meet at the 50-yard line (500 total yards each).\nBetween Rounds:\n• Reset to goal lines and repeat. Can vary called exercise for each round or keep the same. Can do 5 -8 rounds in a workout.\n• Add Mary between rounds as desired.\nCreated by Anchorman out of F3 Twin Cities","kind":"thang","emphasis":["cardio","lower","run"],"equipment":["field"],"tags":["mary","partner","routine"]},{"id":"x-1775","name":"1775","text":"The 1775 is a three round workout with 17 burpees followed by 75 prayer squats followed by a run (distance can vary by AO). Complete at least 3 rounds.","kind":"thang","emphasis":["cardio","lower","run"],"equipment":[],"tags":["routine"]},{"id":"x-1984","name":"1984","text":"Done to Van Halen’s Jump from the 1984 album. Pax will hold an air chair. Every time you hear “jump” you complete one jump squat.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["lower"],"equipment":[],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-1st-10","name":"1st & 10","text":"100 yard field marked at 10 yard increments. Perform 10 @Merkin , 1 @Burpee (11's) at the 10, sprint the remaining 90 yards. Recover jog back to the 20. Perform 9 Merkins , 2 @Burpee , sprint the remaining 80 yards, recover jog to the 30. Repeat until all 100 yards and 11's have been completed. Plank/core exercise until remaining PAX complete","kind":"thang","emphasis":["cardio","core","run","upper"],"equipment":["field"],"tags":["routine"]},{"id":"x-20-bert-variation","name":"20% Bert Variation","text":"This is a variation on the iconic Bert WOD. The reps and distances have been reduced. It is executed repeatedly as a ladder/pyramid to time. The routine works best with either a 100m or 300m out and back course. 10x Burpees 100m Run 20x @Merkin 100m Run 30x Lunges or Spartan Hammers or Sit-ups 100m Run 40x Squats 100m Run 30x Lunges or Spartan Hammers or Sit-ups 100m Run 20x Merkins 100m Run (Repeat to time) The following is a cinderblock variant. It works on a 100m out and back course. pick-up cinderblock 10x Blockees 100m Rifle Carry Drop cinderblock 20x Merkins 100m Run 30x Lunges or Spartan Hammers or Sit-ups 100m Run pick-up cinderblock 40x Goblet Squats 100m Rifle Carry Drop cinderblock 30x Lunges or Spartan Hammers or Sit-ups 100m Run 20x Merkins 100m Run (Repeat to time)","kind":"thang","emphasis":["cardio","core","heavy","lower","run","upper"],"equipment":["coupon"],"tags":["routine"]},{"id":"x-21s","name":"21s","text":"21s In unison PAX does 2-count side straddle hop and counts reps 1-5 out loud. Reps 6-21 are all mental and everyone must stop together at 21. If anyone stops early or goes over Q has PAX perform penalty workout of Q''s choice. Legs Routine","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["lower"],"equipment":[],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-4-square-death-dance","name":"4 Square Death Dance","text":"It’s Dancing time in the gloom! With your upright coupon as your center-point, PAX quick step runs in place for one minute. The Q yells out “rapid run” and counts down last 10 seconds of each minute. Do a quick 3 count to re-set to next side. Repeat process around all 4 sides of coupon to complete the square.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["cardio","heavy"],"equipment":["coupon"],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-4x4s","name":"4x4s","text":"Start with arms raised in a standing position, burpee into plank followed by four Merkins followed by four mountain climbers with each leg. \"One\" is completed when returning to the standing position with arms raised. Wash, rinse, repeat. Recommended to do OYO while waiting for the 6 or waiting for a partner during a group exercise.","kind":"thang","emphasis":["cardio","core","lower","upper"],"equipment":[],"tags":["partner","routine"]},{"id":"x-5-alive","name":"5 Alive","text":"5 Alive: BD Structure\nHere's a structure or format for organizing a BD:\n5 exercises, 25 stations with mozy:\n• Do 1 rep of first exercise at first station\n• Mozy to next station\n• Increase rep count by 1\n• At 6th station do\n• 5 reps of first exercise\n• 1 rep of 2nd\n• Continue as before until 5x, 5x\n• At 11th station, do 5x, 5x, 1x (3 exercises)\n• Continue in like fashion\n• At final (25th) station, will do 5 reps of each exercise (5 Alive!).\nIn the end you do:\n• 115 reps of 1st exercise\n• 90x of 2nd\n• 65x of 3rd\n• 40x of 4th\n• 15x of 5th exericse\nTo adapt UP, put burpees earlier in the queue.\nDepending on distance and cadence, may fill Da Thang time; if not, Ring of Fire PAX-choice is a great way to finish.\nSample recipes:\n5 Alive with:\n• Merkin\n• BBS\n• Burpee\n• Plank Jack\n• Shoulder Tap\nAnother set:\n• Plank Jack\n• Merkin\n• Mt. Climber\n• Absolution\n• Burpee\nCredit to F3 Wheaton where I learned it. It's my go-to BD structure. -What?","kind":"thang","emphasis":["cardio","core","upper"],"equipment":[],"tags":["finisher","routine"]},{"id":"x-5-minute-miracle","name":"5-minute miracle","text":"1 minute divided into 3 x 20 second rounds.\nRound 1: 20 seconds of Merkins\nRound 2: 20 seconds of abs (dictated by the Q)\nRound 3: 20 seconds of legs (dictated by the Q)\nRepeated 5 times = 5 minutes\nAll exercises are performed OYO; may be used as a warm-up or a finisher.\nExample: 1st minute is standard traditional moves- merkins, sit-ups, squats. 2nd minute is wide arm merkins, flutter kicks, Bonnie Blaires. 3rd minute is staggered merkins, imperial walkers, Cusack squats. 4th minute is diamond merkins, LBC, Bobby Hurley’s (jump shots). 5th minute is standard merkins, side bends, pulse squats.","kind":"thang","emphasis":["core","lower","upper"],"equipment":[],"tags":["finisher","mary","routine","warmup"]},{"id":"x-6-in-the-air-tonight","name":"6\" In the Air Tonight","text":"On your six. Hold a 6-inch Leg Hold for the entire slow build-up (approx 3.5 mins). When the famous drum fill hits, switch to max effort Flutter Kicks until the end.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["core","lower","mobility"],"equipment":[],"tags":["mary"]},{"id":"x-7-of-diamonds","name":"7 of Diamonds","text":"Performed on a large diamond (i.e. a square); we use the outside of a baseball field, but any large area will work. For the first round, do 7 reps of an exercise (burpees) at each of the 4 corners with a mosey (or sprint) in between corners. Each round, increase by 7 reps with a different exercise each round, for a total of 4 rounds. Round 2, 14 four count flutter kicks at each of the 4 corners. Round 3, 21 merkins at each of the 4 corners. Round 4, 28 squats at each of the 4 corners. If time allows, continue for a total of 7 rounds, decreasing the reps by 7 for each of the last 3 rounds with exercises of the Q''s choice. We will do some rounds on your own, then wait for the six each round; and some rounds we do as a group. Q''s choice.","kind":"thang","emphasis":["cardio","core","lower","run","upper"],"equipment":["field"],"tags":["mary","routine"]},{"id":"x-7220","name":"7220","text":"Using an elevated terrain feature (hill preferred, but stair set or bleachers will work), PAX begin at the bottom and complete 7 Merkins, run to the top of the hill and complete 2 Burpees, then return to the bottom of the hill to complete 20 squats. 7-2-20 reps represents the elevation in feet of F3 Laramie (Wyoming), the highest elevation Region and workout AO's in F3 Nation where the air is thin. Rinse and repeat as many times as the Q desires. Can be done repeatedly for an entire workout, or can be done as a closer to another routine (recommended pairing with the LARAMIE circuit listed elsewhere in the Exicon). Steep hill is preferred to spur heavy breathing to simulate workouts in the thin air of higher elevations with PAX running up the hill and fast mosey back down to reduce the chance of trips/falls.","kind":"thang","emphasis":["cardio","lower","run","upper"],"equipment":["stairs"],"tags":["competitive","game","routine"]},{"id":"x-abs-are-all-you-need","name":"Abs Are All You Need","text":"The Q plays \"Love is All You Need\" by The Beatles. Hold crunch position (supine with elbows and knees touching) throughout the song. Perform Big Boy Sit Up for every \"Love\" in the song.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["cardio","core"],"equipment":["speaker"],"tags":["mary"]},{"id":"x-absolution","name":"Absolution","text":"Combination of a Groiner, Mahktar N' Diayes, and Chilly Jack, done on an 8-count cadence. An awesome core and upper body workout that is both the solution to flabby abs, and a reason to beg absolution for your sins. Start in plank position and perform a single Groiner (cadence \"1\" jump feet forward, \"2\" jump feet back), then Mahktar N' Diayes to Chillcut position (cadence \"3\" & \"4\" with drop to each elbow), then Chilly Jack (cadence \"5\" feet out, \"6\" feet together), and finally Mahktar N' Diayes to plank starting position (cadence \"7\" and \"ONE, TWO, etc.\" with rise on each hand). Best done in mulch, dirt or at edge of grass and asphalt/concrete so hands/elbows can be on grass while feet have traction. Also works well in parking lot conveyer belts when PAX are provided with small squares of cardboard left at Absolution station to protect elbows. Smart Q's will introduce this with the cadence, but then instruct PAX to do sets of 15-30 OYO (as the Q will suffer too and should avoid giving the impression of weakness to the PAX, lest he suffer insufferable mumble chatter).","kind":"thang","emphasis":["core","lower","upper"],"equipment":[],"tags":["routine"]},{"id":"x-absolutions-for-my-way","name":"Absolutions for My Way","text":"Done as a Mary, Q will deliver short Moleskin referencing the importance of community in the lives of men and the pitfalls of thinking you can do it all on your own. Pax then hold plank while listening to the song “My Way” by Frank Sinatra. Each time there’s a reference to I, me, my, he, man, etc do an @Absolution. Approx 36-40 reps depending on the version of the song played.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["core"],"equipment":["speaker"],"tags":["mary"]},{"id":"x-abyss-merkin","name":"Abyss Merkin","text":"Abyss Merkin Perform merkins on two parallel benches, right hand and foot on one bench, and left hand and foot on the other bench, letting your body lower into the space between the benches as far a possible. Works best if done slowly, holding at the lowest point and imagining a bottomless abyss below you.\nMay also be performed between two coupons. Pax line up and place coupons on ground then shift 1/2 a position so that pax are in the “window” of two coupons. Each pax places his left hand on the coupon to his left, his right hand on the coupon to his right. Perform merkins into the abyss. The number of coupons should be the number of pax +1 to allow each pax the opportunity stare into the unblinking abyss.","kind":"thang","emphasis":["heavy","upper"],"equipment":["bench_wall","coupon"],"tags":["routine"]},{"id":"x-acey-doucey","name":"Acey Doucey","text":"Acey Doucey: A routine that starts with a single round of an exercise like a ladder or 1:4 routine, then at the next location, two reps of something, then four reps... By this point, you are calling out single-rep or 2x1 exercises. The reps keep doubling each round 8...16...32...64...128...256...etc. At any point, head back down the other side.","kind":"thang","emphasis":[],"equipment":[],"tags":["routine"]},{"id":"x-agassis","name":"Agassis","text":"Agassis Tennis court suicide drills. (Agassi has had many comebacks, aye.)","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["cardio"],"equipment":[],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-aiken-legs","name":"Aiken Legs","text":"Aiken Legs Done in succession with no rest -- 20 Squats, 20 Box Jumps, 20 Lunges (10 each leg), 20 Split Jacks (10 each leg forward). Rinse and Repeated as many times as you can.","kind":"thang","emphasis":["lower"],"equipment":[],"tags":["routine"]},{"id":"x-air-drama","name":"Air Drama","text":"Air Drama A continuation of the Johnny Drama, adding an Air (Bodyweight) Squat. Begin from a standing position, move your hips back, and lower your torso to \"sit\" as deeply as possible while maintaining an upright position. Upon returning to a full standing position, execute a calf raise. Can also be done as a negative calf raise by standing on a stair or curb.\nAlso done with an Air Press at the top of the Calf Raise.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["lower","upper"],"equipment":["bench_wall","stairs"],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-air-squared","name":"Air Squared","text":"Air Squared Air chair (People''s Chair without the wall) combined with air claps in cadence.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["cardio"],"equipment":["bench_wall"],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-airport-security","name":"Airport Security","text":"Set the coupon upright to the side of one foot.\n1) Bend to the side to pick up\n2) Almost put it down\n3 ) Back to straight\n4 ) Put it back down\nDo a full IC count, then flapjack on the other side.\nAlternate: With one or two coupons, swaying back and forth like the piano timekeeper, the metronome.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["cardio","heavy"],"equipment":["coupon"],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-al-gore","name":"Al Gore","text":"Al Gore Pretend to hug a tree from the squat position. Hold until the Q says to stop. Sometimes used to wait for all PAX to complete another exercise instead of planking.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["core","lower"],"equipment":[],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-alabama-ass-kickers","name":"Alabama Ass-Kickers","text":"Alabama Ass-Kickers aka Ass-kickers. Down on all fours, kick each leg individually up and back. 4-count on each leg - 1 up, 2 extend, 3 back to up position, 4 down.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["lower"],"equipment":[],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-alarm","name":"ALARM","text":"ALARM A-L-A-R-M (Similar to B.O.M.B.S. except these stand for Arm, Leg, Abs, ''R'' Exercise, ''M'' Exercise): An exercise group of movements performed in successive fashion without rest; generally these are performed in multiples (e.g. ALARM 1 = Shoulder Press, Lunge, LBC, Run, Merkin; ALARM 2 = Shoulder Taps, Squat Jumps, Peter Parkers, Ranger Merkins, Makhtar N''Diayes, ALARM 3 = Burpees, Jump Squat, Mountain Climbers, Rockette Hillbillies, Pattycake Merkins)","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["cardio","core","lower","run","upper"],"equipment":[],"tags":["mary"]},{"id":"x-alarm-clock","name":"Alarm Clock","text":"This is like a reverse burpee and can be used for those who can't complete a normal burpee. Start from a standing position, then bend down in squat, lay back on your six, then crunch back up, and get to a standing position again with a jump","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["cardio","core","lower","upper"],"equipment":[],"tags":["mary"]},{"id":"x-albatross-wings","name":"ALBATROSS WINGS","text":"ALBATROSS WINGS Start with 20 x Forward Arm Circles, hold, 20 x Backwards Arm Circles, hold, 20 x seal claps, hold, 20 x overhead claps. Everything is on a 4-count. Bat Wings w/the following added: Moroccan Night Club, Cherry Pickers, Mike Tyson''s, Chinooks, Front Raises, Overhead Press, Albatross (flapping wings), and finish with 45 degree angle hold.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["cardio","upper"],"equipment":[],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-all-about-the-benjamins","name":"All About The Benjamins","text":"All About The Benjamins Similar to 11''s, however each part equals 100, that''s why \"the Benjamins\". This is OYO and the Q can use the exercises of choice, but the suggested exercises are with a coupon, 25 Curls for the Girls, 25 Walking Lunges, 25 Squats, 25 Walking Lunges back to your coupon, 25 Overhead Press, 25 Walking Lunges, 25 Mountain Climbers, 25 Walking Lunges back. Depending on the mood of the Q, he could make the PAX lunge walk with their coupon or not, but at the end that''s 100 reps on the exercises, and 100 lunges.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["core","heavy","lower","upper"],"equipment":["coupon"],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-alligator-merkin","name":"Alligator Merkin","text":"Alligator Merkin Walking Merkin. Alternate stepping hands forward on successive @Merkin reps. You know...like an alligator walks, but with merkins.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["upper"],"equipment":[],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-alphabet-or-abcs","name":"Alphabet (or ABCs)","text":"Alphabet (or ABCs) On your 6 - feet elevated like 6-inch hold - spell out the alphabet with your feet. All capital letters preferred.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":[],"equipment":[],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-alpine-mountain-climbers","name":"Alpine Mountain Climbers","text":"A slower variation of @Mountain Climbers where, from a high plank, the foot steps farther forward and wider than a standard climber, planting flat beside the same-side hand to open the hips before returning to plank and alternating sides under control.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["core"],"equipment":["stairs"],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-alternating-shoulder-taps","name":"Alternating Shoulder Taps","text":"From the Merkin position, alternate touching your left hand to right shoulder and right hand to left shoulder. IC or OYO.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["upper"],"equipment":[],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-alternating-side-squats","name":"Alternating Side Squats","text":"Alternating Side Squats Start with feet together. Step one leg out to the side and do a squat, returning legs together at the top. Repeat on other side. Usually done in slow cadence so 1 rep is a squat on each side.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["lower"],"equipment":[],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-american-hammer","name":"American Hammer","text":"A more appropriate name for the former Russian Twist. Rocky did beat the Russian in the movie. Sounds tougher too... While on six in partial sit up position with heals just off the ground, twist at the waist so that both hands held together almost touch the ground beside your waist, alternating in cadence from side to side. Often done with a coupon in hand. AKA Zelensky Twist or Russian Twist.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["core","heavy"],"equipment":["coupon"],"tags":["mary"]},{"id":"x-amish-wobble","name":"Amish Wobble","text":"A LT. Dan with a Cindy immediately followed by a blockee","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["lower"],"equipment":[],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-angle-grinder","name":"Angle Grinder","text":"Angle Grinder Starting in plank position angle your body up (pike position) while touching your hand to the opposite knee perform a merkin then touch the other knee and perform another merkin. This exercise is performed 8 count. 1. Touch knee 2. Return to plank 3. Down Merkin 4. Up Merkin 5. Touch opposite knee 6. Return To Plank 7. Down Merkin 8. Up Merkin","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["core","upper"],"equipment":[],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-animal-style-squats","name":"Animal Style Squats","text":"This exercise instructs pax to get in the \"throw-up position\" (hands on knees), do a squat in that position, perform a burpee from there, then get back to throw up position to count for one squat. Q makes the call on time or repetitions.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["cardio","lower","upper"],"equipment":[],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-another-level-legs","name":"Another Level Legs","text":"To the song \"Another Level\" by Oh The Larceny - perform Squat Jacks while the song plays (It's an air squat, but each time you come up you jump your feet out wider (like a jumping jack), then returning to your original narrow squat stance to squat again. Can be reversed so that you start in a wide stance, squat, jump to a narrow stance, jump out wide, squat, repeat) until you hear the word \"level\" and complete a Bonnie Blair. Increase number of Bonnie Blairs for jelly legs in 3 minutes. The guys of Aggieland love this, but hate Cobbler.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["cardio","lower","upper"],"equipment":["speaker"],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-apollo-creed-burpee","name":"Apollo Creed Burpee","text":"Remember the scene from Rocky 3 with Apollo and Rocky doing one-armed push-ups? That''s right, a one-armed Burpee!","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["cardio","upper"],"equipment":[],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-apolo-anton-oh-no","name":"Apolo Anton Oh No!","text":"Apolo Anton Oh No! A speed skater movement (full leg kick behind is encouraged), holding a rock and moving it side to side, done in cadence.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["lower"],"equipment":[],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-apolo-ohno","name":"Apolo Ohno","text":"Apolo OhNo Speed Skater-style side hops","kind":"exercise","emphasis":[],"equipment":[],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-apple-turnover","name":"Apple Turnover","text":"Apple Turnover Best done on a parking lot or a set of cones evenly placed in a row. PAX would do a bear crawl for a certain length, 3 Lines in a parking lot or to the first cone. PAX would then flip to the crab walk for a designated length, 3 more lines or to the 2nd cone, Back to the bear crawl for a distance, flip crab walk for a distance etc... Length is determined by the lines in the parking lot or how many cones the Q has. Great for slowing PAX down that likes to run. Q can make it a Hot Apple Turnover by adding Crawl Bear to the mix.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["cardio","run","upper"],"equipment":["cones"],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-around-the-world","name":"Around the World","text":"Grab the coupon by the middle cross-section, then rotate the block around your head.","kind":"thang","emphasis":["heavy"],"equipment":["coupon"],"tags":["routine"]},{"id":"x-ascending-curb-crawl","name":"Ascending Curb Crawl","text":"Ascending Curb Crawl Locate PAX on quite curbed street. Starting position Bear Crawl facing opposite curb. BC to other side, turn & place feet on curb to complete one Derkin, crawl back and complete two Derkins, continue to 13. Jack Webb''s promiscuous cousin.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":[],"equipment":["bench_wall"],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-ascending-testicles","name":"Ascending Testicles","text":"Ascending Testicles Cousin of Balls to the Wall. Start with feet on wall in 15 degree descending Merkin (Derkin) position. Do 10 Derkins then walk feet up wall to 45 degree Derkin position. 10 more Derkins then walk feet up wall to full Balls to the Wall pose. Can add 10 more Derkins here if you''re tough enough. Or hold in BTTW pose.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["upper"],"equipment":["bench_wall"],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-atms","name":"ATMs","text":"All done in order, with no rest, without leaving plank position. Can be scaled using higher reps. 15 Alternating Shoulder Touches In Cadence (4-count), 10 Tempo Merkins (down on the 1-2-3, up on 4), 10 fast Merkins. That's 1 complete round.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["core","upper"],"equipment":[],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-aura-farmer","name":"Aura Farmer","text":"Stand feet shoulder-width, firmly planted. Keep legs and hips stable. Rotate the torso left, raising both arms overhead into a defiant Y (“bring it on” pose). Rotate the torso right, lowering the arms and then sweeping them back into a right-facing Y. Alternate sides with controlled, deep breaths. Named after the kids who stand on the bow of canoes in Indonesia’s Pacu Jalur boat races, projecting energy and presence to motivate their paddlers — the original aura farmers.","kind":"thang","emphasis":["lower","upper"],"equipment":[],"tags":["competitive","game","routine"]},{"id":"x-aussie-burpees","name":"Aussie Burpees","text":"A groiner with a small hop. Popularized by the very-soon-to-be-eclipsed May 8, 2018 Guiness World Record holder for the most burpees done in 60 minutes by a female. \"According to the folks at Guinness World Records, the start position is with hands and feet on the ground in a plank; all Elizabeth Llorente, 37, had to do when she got to the jump position was remove her hands and feet from the ground. So the personal trainer gives a little froglike hop rather than standing up and doing a full jump with arms to the sky; she also skips the pushup element.\" Can be substituted for 10 counts or stargazers when PAX could use a breather","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["cardio","core","lower","upper"],"equipment":[],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-austin-ass-kickers","name":"Austin Ass-kickers","text":"Austin Ass-kickers Same as Alabama Ass Kicker with one exception: if your left leg is extended also extend your right arm (and if your right leg is extended also extend your left arm).","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["lower","upper"],"equipment":[],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-australian-mountain-climber","name":"Australian Mountain Climber","text":"Get into the Balls to the Wall position and do a mountain climber, typically in cadence. Aka Aussie Mountain Climber","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["core"],"equipment":["bench_wall"],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-australian-shoulder-taps","name":"Australian Shoulder Taps","text":"Get into the Balls to the Wall position and do Shoulder Taps, typically in cadence.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["upper"],"equipment":["bench_wall"],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-australian-snow-angels","name":"Australian Snow Angels","text":"Begin in the prone position like Superman. With arms and legs extended as far and as high as possible begin \"Snow Angel\" making motion in a 4 count cadence. A real crowd pleaser, especially in the rain.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["lower","upper"],"equipment":[],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-b-o-m-b-s","name":"B.O.M.B.S.","text":"Similar to Dora 1-2-3 but more exercises. Partner up. Pax 1 does exercise while Pax 2 runs to the other end of the (insert your destination). Swap out and continue the exercise until each amount of reps are complete. The exercises and reps are: 50- Burpees / 100- Overhead Claps / 150- Merkins / 200- Big Boy Sit-ups / 250- Squats.","kind":"thang","emphasis":["cardio","core","lower","upper"],"equipment":[],"tags":["mary","partner","routine"]},{"id":"x-baba-o-riley","name":"Baba O'Riley","text":"Baba O''Riley Five minutes of Imperial Walkers set to the perfect five minute song, Baba O''Reilly by The Who. Increasing tempo for the final 30 seconds.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":[],"equipment":["speaker"],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-back-plank-aka-knalp","name":"Back Plank (aka Knalp)","text":"Back Plank (aka Knalp) Same as plank except facing upwards with arms behind the body and on heels. (Knalp = plank spelled backwards)","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["core","upper"],"equipment":[],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-back-scratchers","name":"Back Scratchers","text":"Exercise done in traditional 4 count cadence as a warm-up stretch (COP). While standing, (1) start with your arms at your side, palms facing forward. Then, (2) simultaneously reach your right arm up to the sky and bend the elbow to drop the right hand down your center back in between your shoulder blades, while your left arm rotates, elbow bends and you sweep your left hand up the center of your spine towards the right hand. Finally, (3) return to the starting position. If you can touch fingertips, great, otherwise, focus on incremental gains with each rep. Exercise was conceived by Daisy of F3 The Frontier during a 2ndF Thirsty Thursday event, and is based on upper body portion of a yoga move (Cow Face Pose)","kind":"thang","emphasis":["mobility","upper"],"equipment":[],"tags":["routine","warmup"]},{"id":"x-back-stroke","name":"Back Stroke","text":"Wall sit, then alternate slapping/backhanding the wall behind you. When your left hand goes high, your right hand goes low, and vice versa. Keep your core engaged and control every rep.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["cardio","core","lower"],"equipment":["bench_wall"],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-back-widow","name":"Back Widow","text":"Back Widows strengthen the upper back. Lie flat on your back with knees bent and feet on the ground. Place elbows on the ground close to your sides. Drive your elbows and upper arms into the ground to lift your upper back and shoulders off the floor. Squeeze your shoulder blades together at the top, then lower slowly to the starting position.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["upper"],"equipment":[],"tags":["mary"]},{"id":"x-ballerinas-toe-squats","name":"Ballerinas - Toe Squats","text":"Ballerinas - Toe Squats In parallel, raise heels off the floor then slowly squat as low as you can (stop before any knee discomfort). With control, straighten the legs all the way back up to standing while balancing on the toes. Can be completed with arms straight out for balance or with hands clasped behind head. Best performed either in a slow cadence or OYO.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["lower","upper"],"equipment":[],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-balls-to-the-wall","name":"Balls to the Wall","text":"Balls to the Wall Aka BTTW. Standing upside down on your hands with your feet above your head facing any type of structure that will support your body. As close to the wall as you can as the name implies.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":[],"equipment":["bench_wall"],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-balls-to-the-wall-crawl","name":"Balls to the Wall Crawl","text":"Balls to the Wall Crawl Like Balls to the Wall, where you are standing upside down on your hands with your feet above your head, facing any type of structure that will support your body. But also walking on your hands around the building.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":[],"equipment":["bench_wall"],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-baryshnikov-squats","name":"Baryshnikov Squats","text":"Baryshnikov Squats Legs rotated out to the sides, hips opened, heels raised, then squat.","kind":"thang","emphasis":["lower"],"equipment":[],"tags":["routine"]},{"id":"x-bat-wings-aka-the-martina-special","name":"Bat Wings (aka the Martina Special)","text":"Bat Wings (aka the Martina Special) Progression of arm exercises that are deceivingly difficult and named after Austin's bats. Start with 20 x Forward Arm Circles, hold, 20 x Backwards Arm Circles, hold, 20 x seal claps, hold, 20 x overhead claps. Everything is on a 4-count. Remember to enjoy the pain on the faces of your fellow men.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["cardio","upper"],"equipment":[],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-bataan-death-crawl","name":"Bataan Death Crawl","text":"A combination of Catch Me If You Can and a traditional Bear Crawl. The last person drops and does 5 Burpees, while the rest of the Pax Bear Crawl in a line. After completing the Burpees, the last guy runs to catch the group, tapping the (new) last Pax on the shoulder, who then stops to begin his 5 Burpees, while the (former) last guy continues on to the front of the line. Continue until all Pax have performed a set of Burpees, until the Q calls it or a certain distance has been reached.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["cardio","upper"],"equipment":[],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-bataan-death-march","name":"Bataan Death March","text":"AKA: Burpee Catch Me If You Can Indian Run...A combination of Catch Me If You Can and a traditional Indian Run. The last person drops and does 5 Burpees, while the rest of the Pax mosey in a line. After completing the Burpees, the last guy runs to catch the group, tapping the (new) last Pax on the shoulder, who then stops to begin his 5 Burpees, while the (former) last guy continues on to the front of the line. Continue until all Pax have performed a set of Burpees or until the Q calls it.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["cardio","run","upper"],"equipment":[],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-bay-city-scissors","name":"Bay City Scissors","text":"Alternating scissor kicks done in an 8-count. On your back start with your legs at a 45-degree angle. Alternate legs for a vertical 4-count scissor; 1-right leg up/ left leg down, 2-left leg up/ right leg down, 3-right leg up/ left leg down, 4-left leg up/ right leg down. Counts 5-8 are parallel to the ground; 5- right leg over left leg, 6- left over right, 7-right over left, 8-left over right. That''s ONE. A real crowd pleaser at the end of your AB workout.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["lower","upper"],"equipment":[],"tags":["mary"]},{"id":"x-bcgs","name":"BCGs","text":"On the Q's call for warm-o-rama or before COT:\nB = Bend (downward dog)\nC = Cobra\nG = Pay homage to the Sky Q\nFor Harrisburg, PA's brother BCG","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["upper"],"equipment":[],"tags":["warmup"]},{"id":"x-beach-bunnies","name":"Beach Bunnies","text":"Murder Bunnies performed in the sand (ie - a volleyball court, playground area, beach, etc)","kind":"exercise","emphasis":[],"equipment":[],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-bear-brawl","name":"Bear Brawl","text":"Bear Brawl Like a Football sled during two-a-days, Pax 1 assumes the Bear Crawl position while Pax 2 provides resistance to Pax 1''s shoulders and resists their forward progress for a pre-determined distance. Then FlapJack. Another advantage of this exercise is that P2 can provide encouragement/motivation into P1's ear directly. MumbleChatter rises as resistance increases reciprocally. As developed in F3 Nolensville.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["cardio","upper"],"equipment":[],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-bear-crawl","name":"Bear Crawl","text":"A bear crawl is a full-body exercise where you move on all fours with your hands and feet on the ground, keeping your knees slightly off the floor and your back relatively flat. You crawl forward by moving opposite hand and foot together, maintaining a stable core throughout the movement. It's commonly used in fitness training to build strength, coordination, and endurance.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["core"],"equipment":[],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-bear-crawl-1-2-3","name":"Bear Crawl 1-2-3","text":"Bear Crawl 1-2-3 Dora''s obnoxious neighbor who throws wild parties all night long. Partner up, perform 100 Merkins, 200 LBCs, and 300 Squats as a team. While Partner 1 is doing the 1-2-3, Partner 2 Bear Crawls across a defined space (parking lot works great), and Crawl Bear back, then flip flop until all Merkins, LBCs, and Squats are complete.","kind":"thang","emphasis":["core","lower","upper"],"equipment":[],"tags":["mary","partner","routine","team"]},{"id":"x-bear-crawl-burpees","name":"Bear Crawl Burpees","text":"PAX start in upright position arms raised (Grizzly bear rarwr) drop in to burpee, at the top of the push up start bear crawling. Everytime you hear Grizzly, you hop back up, drop back down, push up and crawl again.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["cardio","upper"],"equipment":[],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-bear-crawl-inchworm","name":"Bear Crawl Inchworm","text":"Bear Crawl Inch Worm PAX lines up head to to feet in plank position. The man in the back of the line bear crawls to front of the line and yells front and next man does the same thing until whole PAX has done it.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["core"],"equipment":[],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-bear-crawl-merkin","name":"Bear Crawl Merkin","text":"Bear Crawl Merkin 4ct exercise. Start in bear crawl. 3 count crawl with the 4th being the merkin. Hands should be staggered during merkin and if done correctly will result in each hand being staggered forward on opposing reps.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["upper"],"equipment":[],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-bear-crawl-ring-of-fire","name":"Bear Crawl Ring of Fire","text":"Bear Crawl Ring of Fire Combines exercises we have all come to love/hate. Circle up around shovel flag. Begin by bear crawling around in circle until Q says stop. Upon stopping, first Pax completes 10 merkins while other Pax plank, then next pax in line completes 10 merkins while other pax plank. Keep going around until all pax have completed the 10 merkins. The suck factor greatly increases the more pax you have (longer planks). Do as many rounds as time permits, or really until Q is smoked. Best when combined with a mucho chesto variation. 5 rounds of bear crawls in circle formation, 10x each of merkins, diamond merkins, werkins, stagger left merkin, and stagger right merkins. (ie Round 1 bear crawl in circle, Q halt, first pax does 10 merkins, pax plank until all pax have completed 10 merkins....begin bear crawling again for Round 2, Q halt, first pax does 10 diamond merkins, pax plank until all pax have com pleted 10 diamond merkins....etc.)","kind":"thang","emphasis":["core","upper"],"equipment":[],"tags":["routine"]},{"id":"x-bear-crawl-snake","name":"Bear Crawl Snake","text":"Bear Crawl Snake Similar to Bear Crawl Inch Worm, but adds a weave. PAX line up head to feet in plank position. The man at the back of the line, bear crawls to front of the line, weaving in and out of planking PAX and yells when at front. Next man does the same thing until all PAX have completed. Repeato as necessary.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["core"],"equipment":[],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-bear-hold","name":"Bear Hold","text":"Bear Hold What happens when you combine a plank and bear crawl.... you get the Bear Hold. Its is the bear crawl position, but don''t move. 4 points of contact, hands and toes. Knees should be slightly off the ground.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["core"],"equipment":[],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-bear-with-me","name":"Bear With Me","text":"Starting in a bear plank or tabletop position, lift one arm and twist to kick your opposite leg out and through to the side.\nThis can be done for reps or time","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["core","lower","upper"],"equipment":[],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-bearmuda-triangle","name":"Bearmuda Triangle","text":"3 markers ~30yds apart in shape of a triangle. Pax performs one burpee at first marker and bear crawls to 2nd marker, 2 burpees and bear crawl to 3rd marker, 3 burpees and bear crawl back to 1st marker. Rinse and Repeat x 3. Named Bearmuda Triangle as it has been known to mysteriously lose some pax along the way.","kind":"thang","emphasis":["cardio","upper"],"equipment":[],"tags":["routine"]},{"id":"x-bearpees","name":"Bearpees","text":"The Bearpees are long lost cousins to the Burpeedans and suck equally. Line up across a field or parking lot. OYO 1 Burpee followed up by 4 count bearcrawl forward. Once PAX get to other side, rinse and repeat adding another Burpee, keeping the 1:4 ratio but only increasing the number of Burpees. This is best achieved when going past 4!","kind":"thang","emphasis":["cardio"],"equipment":["field"],"tags":["routine"]},{"id":"x-bears-blocks","name":"Bears & Blocks","text":"Bears & Blocks Get on all fours (like you are doing a bear crawl) with your Cinder Block on the grass between your knees or feet. Reach between your legs and pull the Block across the grass past your head. Now, bear crawl forward until the Block is between your feet again, and keep repeating across the length of the field.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["heavy","lower"],"equipment":["coupon","field"],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-bearway-to-heaven","name":"Bearway to Heaven","text":"A Bear Crawl suicide of seven increasing lengths with decreasing burpees at the end of each length. Ideally the lengths and number of burpees should be such that the entire exercise takes the full 8:01 time of \"Stairway to Heaven\".","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["cardio"],"equipment":[],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-beat-the-clock","name":"Beat The Clock","text":"Beat The Clock is a Merkin (pushup) style exercise. You do regular merkins around the \"clock.\" There are 12 sets, but the amount of reps decrease after each set is completed for a total of 78 reps. You start at the top of the clock (12:00), and do 12 reps, then move to the left to 11:00, and do 11 reps, and so forth and so forth until you reach 1:00 and complete the circle of the clock. Your feet stay in the middle as your arms move to the left after each set is complete.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["upper"],"equipment":[],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-beep-test-highlander","name":"Beep Test/Highlander","text":"Beep Test/Highlander PAX run continuously between two points that are 20 meters apart from side to side. The runs are synchronized with a smart phone application that played beeps at set intervals. At the sound of a beep, the PAX run 20 meters before then next beep sounds As the test proceeds, the interval between each successive beep decreases, forcing the PAX to increase their speed over the course of the test, until it is impossible to keep in sync with the recording. Should the Pax fail to make the 20 meter distance prior to the sounding of the Beep, then the PAX are eliminated from the test. Any eliminated PAX do exercises previously designated by the ''Q'' until only 1 PAX remains doing the Bleep Test.","kind":"thang","emphasis":["cardio","run"],"equipment":["timer"],"tags":["routine"]},{"id":"x-belching","name":"Belching","text":"Pax lays flat on then ground in a line, Q says go. Everyone hops up similar to recovering from a burpee, and sprints 5 - 10 steps, then dives down flat on the ground remaining in line. Essentially, you're advancing the field without the enemy fire being able to smoke you. Go hard, go quick. After getting to your resting place, complete upper, and core routines, then do a different upper, core routine, then belch back to the starting point, mission accomplished. Best on grassy fields in the gloom with some morning dew, some dives have slides, one must reverse low crawl to get back to the line or forward low crawl to advance to the line.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["cardio","core","run"],"equipment":["field","stairs"],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-bent-jacob","name":"Bent Jacob","text":"Bent Jacob Any deviation from a straight #JacobsLadder.","kind":"thang","emphasis":[],"equipment":[],"tags":["routine"]},{"id":"x-berkins","name":"Berkins","text":"Berkins Doing merkins using bricks, best when including squats and jumpups.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["lower","upper"],"equipment":[],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-bernie-sanders","name":"Bernie Sanders","text":"Bernie Sanders Find the tallest hill you can and traverse it from bottom to top while running backwards. You''ll find the quads you never had and all the while feeling the BERN. Repeat as necessary.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["cardio","lower","run"],"equipment":[],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-bg-lizard","name":"BG Lizard","text":"Start with two coupons. Starting position is in a plank with one hand grabbing each coupon.\nKeeping your core engaged and your butt down, slide one coupon forward with one arm. Second, slide the other coupon forward with the other arm such that you are walking like a lizard.\nThe backwards version (dragging the cindies toward you as you lizard walk backwards) is a BG Drazil\nBest done as part of a Dora.","kind":"thang","emphasis":["core","heavy","upper"],"equipment":["coupon"],"tags":["routine"]},{"id":"x-big-bang","name":"Big Bang","text":"PAX form small circle, everyone in a plank, shoulder-to-shoulder. Place headlamp in the center. Q calls out a number and exercise. For example, \"10 burpees,\" means PAX stand up in an explosion of energy, run directly away from center of circle 10 yards/paces and do 10 burpees, then run back to the center and plank for the 6. Each PAX must find their own route away from the center of circle. Obstacles--ditches, trees, pits--are encouraged, but next round can''t start until all PAX accounted for. Generally performed in increasing counts (10 paces/reps, 20 paces/reps, 30 paces/reps, 40 paces/reps, 50 paces/reps) representing the ever-expanding universe.","kind":"thang","emphasis":["cardio","core","run","upper"],"equipment":[],"tags":["routine"]},{"id":"x-big-boy-knock-out","name":"Big Boy Knock Out","text":"Big Boy Sit Ups with 2 punches.\nOn your six. Get up then 2 punches before going back down to original position.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["core"],"equipment":[],"tags":["mary"]},{"id":"x-big-boy-sit-up-ups-aka-bissyous","name":"Big Boy Sit-up-Ups (aka, Bissyous)","text":"Big Boy Sit-up-Ups (aka, Bissyous) Big Boy Sit-up-Ups = standard Big Boy Sit-ups + stand all the way up when you get to the top of each sit-up position... helps to have a Partner holding your feet. Recommended Partner holding feet keep head down chin to chest - avoid strange encounters to the face during exercise!","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["core","upper"],"equipment":[],"tags":["mary","partner"]},{"id":"x-big-o","name":"Big O","text":"Big O Sit on the very edge of a skate bowl or any ledge with your legs hanging over the abyss, feet together. Make big O''s with your feet, bringing them down into the bowl on the downswing. Hands out to the side or gripping ledge.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["lower"],"equipment":[],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-bill-murray","name":"Bill Murray","text":"Same as Sheldon Cooper, but instead of decreasing reps after each run, you do 10 merkins, 10 squats, 10 BBSU, and 10 burpees each time. After the 3rd or 4th round, one of the PAX said he felt like he was in ''Groundhog Day.'' That is what led us to Bill Murray for the name.\nBest when done to Sonny & Cher's 'I Got You, Babe' on repeat....","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["cardio","lower","run","upper"],"equipment":[],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-billy-madison","name":"Billy Madison","text":"Billy Madison Inspired by Billy Madison''s journey through back through school, this routine involves a running loop and exercise per grade. For best effects, perform routine on school grounds. Begin with a loop (ideally single-file line leader style) to simulate the grade, followed by an exercise with 12 reps as the exam. This concludes 1st grade. Run the loop again, followed by the 1st grade exercise x 12 reps plus a new exercise x 12 reps. This concludes 2nd grade. Continue with the loop and adding an exercise each time until you''ve completed one loop and exercise combo for each of the 12 grades. Great for mumble chatter and telling of high school victories. Celebrate graduation with snack packs for all!","kind":"thang","emphasis":["cardio","run"],"equipment":[],"tags":["routine"]},{"id":"x-billy-run","name":"Billy Run","text":"Billy Run An AYG run performed during the last few hundred yards of what ought to be fellowship pace back to the parking lot at the end of a workout, initiated by one of the PAX when the spirit leads.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["cardio","run"],"equipment":[],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-bizarro","name":"Bizarro","text":"Bizarro Bizzaro is Superman''s Doppelganger (aka the \"negative Superman\"), from DC comics. The exercise involves pulsing in and out of the Superman position over the lip of a skate bowl/pool (picnic table, ledge, whatever) so that the legs actually go negative.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["lower"],"equipment":["bench_wall"],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-black-jack","name":"Black Jack","text":"Black Jack Start on the sideline of a football field. Perform 1 Merkin - run to other sideline - perform 20 LBCs. Run back and do 2 Merkins. Run back for 19 LBCs. Repeat until you do 20 Merkins and 1 LBC, running between the sidelines. Always adds up to 21 - BLACK JACK!","kind":"thang","emphasis":["cardio","core","run","upper"],"equipment":["field"],"tags":["mary","routine"]},{"id":"x-black-snake","name":"Black Snake","text":"Black Snake Take an Indian Run, but the last guy has to weave his way through the Pax to the front of the line.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["cardio","run"],"equipment":[],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-blades-of-steel","name":"Blades of Steel","text":"Start in plank position with hands directly under shoulders, keeping arms as straight as possible. Slowly perform merkin with only your shoulders doing the movement, no bend in your elbows. At your lowest position your shoulder blades are close together, with elbows and back still straight. Slowly raise your body with only your shoulder blades pushing away from your spine. Your shoulder blades will be slightly rounded at top once complete. Suggested to move slow.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["core","upper"],"equipment":[],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-blart","name":"Blart","text":"Blart Similar to an Al Gore, Pax are in Air Chair position and grab the handlebars of their Segway. Pax bend at the knees - left, forward, right, back is 1 count (Kodiak style)","kind":"exercise","emphasis":[],"equipment":[],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-blimps","name":"Blimps","text":"5 burpees, 10 lunge each leg, 15 imperial walker, 20 merkins, 25 plank jacks, 30 squats. Rinse and repeat as needed. Can be done to cross a field or lot.","kind":"thang","emphasis":["cardio","core","lower","upper"],"equipment":["field"],"tags":["routine"]},{"id":"x-blitzkrieg-boppin","name":"Blitzkrieg Boppin’","text":"To The Ramones “Blitzkreig Bop.”\nCurb touches (Cindy, curb or step) throughout song. Jump squat at “Let’s Go”. 2 jump squats at “Bop.”","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["lower"],"equipment":["bench_wall","speaker"],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-block-a-dock","name":"Block a Dock","text":"Block a Dock Where applicable with a loading dock. Place Cinder block at your feet close to the dock. Pickup the block set it on the dock and put it back down.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["heavy"],"equipment":["coupon"],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-block-burners","name":"Block Burners","text":"Best done with 12x12 Deck Blocks. Push deck block across a parking lot for about 40 yards. Do 11 Big boys with block. Push block back to start and do 1 Incline Merkin on the block. Repeat but drop 1 big boy each trip and add 1 merkin until you hit 13.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["cardio","core","heavy","upper"],"equipment":["coupon"],"tags":["mary"]},{"id":"x-block-webbs","name":"Block Webbs","text":"Block Webbs A Jack Webb using a concrete block incline merkin & a block press instead of an air press.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["heavy","upper"],"equipment":["coupon"],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-block-over-burpees","name":"Block-Over Burpees","text":"The block-over Burpee is a simple up-mod of the standard burpee where you must jump over a coupon on the up. It’s surprising how much extra effort these take when doing large quantities of them","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["cardio","heavy","lower"],"equipment":["coupon"],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-blockee","name":"Blockee","text":"Burpees with cinder blocks (or sandbags). With your cinder block drop down and do a Merkin on the cinder block. Return to the standing position and press the cinder block above your head to complete one rep.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["cardio","heavy","upper"],"equipment":["coupon","sandbag"],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-blocko-motor-city-shuffle-bmcs","name":"Blocko Motor City Shuffle (BMCS)","text":"Variation the on the @Motor City Shuffle\nWith a Cinder Block In hand, Lunge with OH Press x2, First Part of Blockee, Merkins on block x5, Plank Jacks on block x5, second Part of Blockee (thruster), squat, block thruster throw, Frog Hop to Block, = 1 Rep!\nShould be done in a grassy field.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["core","heavy","lower","upper"],"equipment":["coupon","field"],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-blocktanamo","name":"Blocktanamo","text":"Blocktanamo PAX circle up with their backs towards the center, holding a coupon straight out in front of them. One PAX sets down his block and runs outside the circle, pressing down on the others'' blocks as he passes. The next PAX sets his block down and begins his run as soon as the guy next to him returns to his spot. The exercise ends when the final PAX completes his lap. This can be done both clockwise and counterclockwise. A modified version of a PAX favorite, Guantanamo.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["cardio","heavy","run","upper"],"equipment":["coupon"],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-bloxanne","name":"Bloxanne","text":"The Q plays the song \"Roxanne\" by The Police. Remain on your six with your coupon and perform chest presses in tempo with the song. Every time Roxanne is heard, perform a @World War III Sit-up (Total 26 times).","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["core","heavy","upper"],"equipment":["coupon","speaker"],"tags":["mary"]},{"id":"x-blue-falcon","name":"Blue Falcon","text":"Pax is divided into two teams teams have 30 sec to come up with a plan then each team has 3 min (however long Q decides) to do their own workout at the end of the workout you trade workouts and the other team has 3 min to complete the other teams workout. This can be done single or multiple rounds at the end of each round loser has a punishment (20 burpees) or something like that if both teams complete the exercises it can be a tie. Or since this is America first one to complete others workout plan wins.","kind":"thang","emphasis":["cardio"],"equipment":[],"tags":["competitive","game","routine","team"]},{"id":"x-boat-canoe","name":"Boat Canoe","text":"Boat Canoe The Boat position would be while on six with legs pulled up to chest and arms beside body. Canoe is when legs and back are straightened while keeping both off the ground. Q calls out Boat or Canoe.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["lower","upper"],"equipment":[],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-bobby-hurley","name":"Bobby Hurley","text":"Bobby Hurley When one does a squat and slaps the ground with both hands like a Duke basketball player, then jumps up and raising arms as if taking a jump shot.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["cardio","lower","upper"],"equipment":[],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-bobby-shmurda","name":"Bobby Shmurda","text":"Similar to an elephant walk, this leg stretch starts upright, hinging at the hips to engage the calf muscles. Then alternate which heel is lifted up, to stretch each calf.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["lower","mobility"],"equipment":[],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-bodies-hit-the-floor","name":"Bodies Hit the Floor","text":"Bodies Hit the Floor This is done to the song Bodies by Drowning Pool (3:21). Start in plank position. When the song says \"Let The Bodies Hit The Floor\" do a Donkey Kick (26 Total). When the song counts (1, 2, 3, 4) do a Merkin (21 Total). Always plank when not doing Donkey Kicks or Merkins and never let your Bodies Hit The Floor.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["core","upper"],"equipment":["speaker"],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-body-bag-builders","name":"Body Bag Builders","text":"Body Bag Builders This is a 10-count exercise. Perform 8-ct Body Builder but *insert 2-ct (right knee/left knee) Mountain Climber* after 2-ct Plank Jack but before 2-ct Merkin portion...''voila''...\"8-ct Body Builder\" but worse; hence, the body bag reference.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["core","upper"],"equipment":[],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-body-builders","name":"Body Builders","text":"Essentially this is an 8 count Burpee, with a plank-jack added. (1) Squat down, (2) legs out, (3) down part of Merkin, (4) up part of Merkin, (5) out part of plank-jack, (6) in part of plank-jack, (7) feet to hands, and (8) stand up. Extra credit (and why wouldn't we?) is to jump and clap overhead.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["cardio","core","lower","upper"],"equipment":[],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-bohemian-rhapsody","name":"Bohemian Rhapsody","text":"Bohemian Rhapsody performed in cadence. Start with a slow Freddy Mercury, holding each side for 5 seconds on a single count. Finish with regular Freddy Mercurys.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":[],"equipment":["timer"],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-bohemian-whap-sody","name":"Bohemian Whap-sody","text":"Play Queen's \"Bohemian Rhapsody.\"\nPerform the following exercises in the noted parts:\n• Ballad: Slow Air Squats\n• Guitar Solo: Fast Merkins\n• Opera Section: Freddie Mercuries (Bicycles)\n• Hard Rock Section: Burpees (Empty the tank!)\n• Outro: Al Gore Hold (Static Squat)","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["cardio","lower","upper"],"equipment":[],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-bojangles-biscuit","name":"Bojangles Biscuit","text":"On a typical 400 meter track, sprint straights and mosey corners, each lap can add 10 blueberries (burpees) if want a blueberry biscuit","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["cardio","run"],"equipment":["field"],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-bolt-45s","name":"Bolt 45s","text":"Bolt 45s As in Usain Bolt Olympic runner. The Colt 45s of legs. Begin with 15 squats full standing position down to halfway position and return. Then go from halfway down position to full squat position and return up to halfway position 15x. Finish off with 15 full squats or jump squats.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["cardio","lower"],"equipment":[],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-bone-the-fish","name":"Bone The Fish","text":"Bone The Fish Find a parking lot with spaces \"facing\" each other and without concrete \"stops\". Start on the first set of lines by shuffle right, sprint up to the next line, shuffle left. Rinse and repeat for 4 lines then switch to karaoke for 4 lines, then back pedal/sprint for 4 lines. Repeat a few times to get the blood flowing","kind":"thang","emphasis":["cardio","run"],"equipment":[],"tags":["routine"]},{"id":"x-bonnie-blairs","name":"Bonnie Blairs","text":"Bonnie Blairs, Jumping Lunges. Yes, it's really that simple.\nA 4-count exercise: ONE- left leg lunge, TWO- jump up from lunge position, reversing legs in the air, THREE- right leg lunge, FOUR- jump up from lunge position, reversing legs in the air... repeat as necessary to end Mumble Chatter.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["lower"],"equipment":[],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-boo-boo-bear-crawl","name":"Boo Boo Bear Crawl","text":"Boo Boo Bear Crawl Similar to Bear Crawl but with either leg held off the ground all the time so the back leg has to basically hop forward.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["lower"],"equipment":[],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-booyah-merkin","name":"Booyah! Merkin","text":"Booyah! Merkin In honor of the late great Stuart Scott, who no doubt would have been an F3 Dash pax, had F3 been in Chapel HIll decades ago. 2 pax plank facing each other perform merkin in unison and on up move reach out and tap right hand to partner''s left shoulder, repeat merkin in unison with left hand tap to partner''s shoulder to complete one rep. Each up move accompanied by a spirited BOOYAH!","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["core","upper"],"equipment":[],"tags":["partner"]},{"id":"x-bopo","name":"BOPO","text":"Burpee, One-Legged Burpee, Plank Jack, One-Legged Burpee (other leg) - call this OYO for 10 reps.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["cardio","core","lower"],"equipment":[],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-born-to-lunge","name":"Born to Lunge","text":"Play Bruce Springsteen's \"Born to Run\" and do lunges around the speaker. If the PAX gases out, switch to reverse lunges.\nAlternate: Do @Bonnie Blairs","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["cardio","lower"],"equipment":["speaker"],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-bottom-feeders","name":"Bottom Feeders","text":"Bottom Feeders Any set of exercises where the pax travel back and forth and the traveling portion is limited to bear crawls, crab walks or other height-restricted method. (The exercises on either end do not need to be ground-based) - Examples: 7s 11s, 21s, suicides, pyramids, etc...","kind":"thang","emphasis":["cardio"],"equipment":[],"tags":["routine"]},{"id":"x-boxcutter","name":"Boxcutter","text":"This ab exercise starts on your 6 with legs together 6 inches, out like a Dolly for 1, up for 2, back together for 3, and down without touching the ground for count. Can also be reversed from 6 inches, feet up together, feet out, down, back together at 6 inches for count. Feet are moving in a square motion.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["core","lower"],"equipment":[],"tags":["mary"]},{"id":"x-breakdancer-merkin","name":"Breakdancer Merkin","text":"Breakdancer Merkin Begin in plank and perform the down part of a merkin. On the up, raise the right arm and come into a side plank, kicking your left leg in front of your body. Rotate back to plank and repeat on the other side. Can be done in (slow) cadence: 1) down; 2) right arm up, left leg through; 3) down; 4) left arm up, right leg through.","kind":"thang","emphasis":["core","lower","upper"],"equipment":[],"tags":["routine"]},{"id":"x-brick-by-brick-shuttlerun-bbbs","name":"Brick by Brick Shuttlerun (BBBS)","text":"PAX number off 1s&2s and form two lines 10 yards apart (3 parking spaces at today''s AO). First PAX from Group 1 does the shuttle run by picking up a brick at the other groups line, returns brick to his line, then retrieves the second brick, then returns brick to his starting spot. Remaining PAX are meanwhile in plank position or crab hold awaiting their turn and rotate between the two positions. After PAX completes the shuttle run, he proceeds to perform: R1: 15 Burpees, then falls in line in either plank or crab hold R2: 15 BBs, falls in line R3: 10 Burpees, fall in line R4: 10 BBs, fall in line R5: 5 Burpees, fall in line R6: 5 BBs, fall in line","kind":"thang","emphasis":["cardio","core","run"],"equipment":[],"tags":["routine"]},{"id":"x-brickbarrow","name":"Brickbarrow","text":"Brickbarrow It''s a wheelbarrow with 2 pax except the pax crawling on his hands also has to \"walk\" with a brick in each hand.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["upper"],"equipment":[],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-bricklayers","name":"Bricklayers","text":"BrickLayers is a side jump over the coupon, then lift the block from one side to the other. Always keep the flat side up. Rinse and repeat. Reposition the block to your other side when you are facing perpendicular to the direction of movement.\nFrom IPC 2024 - Week 2","kind":"thang","emphasis":["heavy","lower"],"equipment":["coupon"],"tags":["routine"]},{"id":"x-bridge-of-hate","name":"Bridge of Hate","text":"Bridge of Hate The bridge of hate is the exact opposite of the tunnel of love. The pax form a line by laying on their backs, shoulder to shoulder. One pax will then be lifted and passed down the line of the pax that are laying on the ground. When the pax that was being passed down the line gets to the front he lays next to the last man and the man at the rear of the line then gets passed down, so forth and so on. Just like an inverted tunnel of love. Exercise can be done for distance or turns. Q''s choice.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["upper"],"equipment":[],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-bridge-over-the-nest","name":"Bridge Over The Nest","text":"Bridge Over The Nest Both partners start at the base of a bridge or hill. Partner 1 starts bear crawling over the bridge while Partner 2 completes 10 squats, 10 merkins, and 10 LBCs. Partner 2 then runs to the opposite side of the bridge and then runs back to the bear crawling Partner 1. Partner 2 picks up with the bear crawl while Partner 1 runs to the start to complete the exercises, runs across to the other side, and runs back to Partner 2. Repeato back and forth across the bridge until time runs out or the PAX start a mutiny against the Q for excessive cardio. Swap bear crawls for lunges, crab walks, inch worms, etc. after each round as desired.","kind":"thang","emphasis":["cardio","core","lower","upper"],"equipment":[],"tags":["mary","partner","routine"]},{"id":"x-broad-jump-burpee","name":"Broad Jump Burpee","text":"Combination of burpee with a broad jump forward at end of burpee.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["cardio","lower"],"equipment":[],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-broken-bicycle","name":"Broken Bicycle","text":"The Broken Bicycle is a variation of Freddie Mercurys. Lay on six with leg straight out and hands behind head. Lift torso like doing a crunch while bringing one knee to meet elbows with the other leg remaining straight. Return to original position and repeat with opposite leg. It is a four count exercise with you alternating legs on each sit up. When done correctly it looks like you are riding a \"broken bicycle\".","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["cardio","core","lower"],"equipment":[],"tags":["mary"]},{"id":"x-broken-wheelbarrow","name":"Broken Wheelbarrow","text":"Broken Wheelbarrow Similar to a wheelbarrow. Partner one walking on ground with hands while partner two is holding only one leg, with the other leg free of held leg. This demands dramatically more core stability. This has been referred to as the Broken Spirit.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["core","lower","upper"],"equipment":[],"tags":["partner"]},{"id":"x-bropee","name":"Bropee","text":"Performing a burpee with a partner simultaneously so that on your squat jump up you execute a most excellent high ten.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["cardio","lower"],"equipment":[],"tags":["partner"]},{"id":"x-bruce-lee","name":"Bruce Lee","text":"An super set consisting of 6 ab exercises: 1. Hammer, 2. Leg raises, 3. LBC's, 4. Heel Touches, 5. Crunchy Frog, 6. 100's. 20 reps, 3 sets. 30 seconds rest between each set. work up to 90 reps, 7 sets: Bruce Lee's work out.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["cardio","core","lower"],"equipment":[],"tags":["mary"]},{"id":"x-bubbles-the-union-wod","name":"Bubbles (The Union) WOD","text":"F3 Bubbles Memorial BD — \"The Thang\"\nBUY-IN: 20 Merkins with a clap if you're Bad\nExercises:\nExercise\nReps / Action / Significance\nLunges\n25 Reps (birth day)\nMan Makers\n8 Reps (# of times he Q’s)\nCross-Squat\n26 Reps (1 each side; death year)\nRifle Carry\n3 Parking Spaces & Back ( Dirt bike track size)\nBent Over Row\n12 Reps (Combined age of his 2 kids)\nBear Crawl\n3 Parking Spaces & Back (Dirt bike track size)\nWWI\n23 Reps (year he started F3)\nCurls\n70 Reps (# of F3 workout posts)\nTricep Extensions\n16 Reps (day he was an FNG)\nPress\n23 Reps (year he completed his VQ)\nPlank\n91 Seconds (birth year)\nDuck Walk\n1 Parking Space & Back (his #1, his M)\nFinish: Yell out \"Bubbles is here!\" then AMRAP until time.\nWOD_BUBBLES.png (572×1024)","kind":"thang","emphasis":["cardio","core","lower","run","upper"],"equipment":["field"],"tags":["routine"]},{"id":"x-bucket-brigade","name":"Bucket Brigade","text":"Works best with 4 - 8 men. Line up at top of stairs (or large hill). One man on each stair shoulder-to-shoulder. Man on highest stair passes heavy object (i.e. 60lb sandbag, cinderblock, etc) down to next man, who passes it along the line. Once you hand off object, run down stairs to end of the line to receive object again. Once at bottom of stairs, repeat going back up.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["cardio","heavy","run","upper"],"equipment":["coupon","sandbag","stairs"],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-bucket-brigade-lunge","name":"Bucket Brigade Lunge","text":"Bucket Brigade Lunge With Rock or other coupon in hand, backwards lunge and twist towards front leg. Alternate legs and direction...like in a bucket brigade.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["heavy","lower"],"equipment":["coupon"],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-bulgarian-split-squat","name":"Bulgarian Split Squat","text":"Use a bench or a partner's back while they hold a plank position. Extend one leg out roughly 24 inches, with the other leg placed on the bench or your partner''s back. Squat down until your knee is nearly touching the ground, then return to the starting position. Perform the movement on the ''down'' command, typically in sets of 15-20 reps per leg. To modify, add weight using a coupon, ruck, or sandbag.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["core","heavy","lower","ruck"],"equipment":["bench_wall","coupon","ruck","sandbag","weights"],"tags":["partner"]},{"id":"x-burnouts","name":"Burnouts","text":"Place down a cone or other marker.\nGet into a low plank position and then attempt to rotate your body 360 degrees around the marker, with your head staying as close to the marker as possible and your feet as far away from the marker as possible.\n1 count equals one full rotation of the marker.","kind":"thang","emphasis":["core"],"equipment":["cones"],"tags":["routine"]},{"id":"x-burp-groin","name":"Burp & Groin","text":"Like the Burp & Merk, but do ascending Groiners 1-10 after the merkin part of the burpee.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["cardio","upper"],"equipment":[],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-burp-merk","name":"Burp & Merk","text":"Begin a traditional burpee with a single push up at the bottom, then complete. Drop back down for a second burpee with two push ups, then complete. Pyramid up to 5 if you're a girl or 10 if you're a man, pyramid all the way back down to one if you're an F3 Man!! Hooah!","kind":"thang","emphasis":["cardio","upper"],"equipment":[],"tags":["routine"]},{"id":"x-burp-back-mountain","name":"Burp Back Mountain","text":"A punishing full body exercise begins by locating a nice-sized hill. The exercise is then performed by pairing up with one person proceeding to run backward up the hill/forward down the hill 5X while the other person is performing burpees. The individuals continue to alternate running with burpees until 100 total burpees are completed. When finished, pax continue to run hills until entire pax completes.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["cardio","run"],"equipment":[],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-burp-ups","name":"Burp-Ups","text":"Standard Burpee done (typically under monkey bars) where you do the Burpee, then when you jump you grab the monkey bar and go straight into a pull up. Rinse repeat.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["cardio","lower","upper"],"equipment":["pull_up_bar"],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-burpee","name":"Burpee","text":"A multi-step, full-body exercise in which you move from standing to push-up to squat to jump. Best seen in F3 TV example.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["cardio","lower","upper"],"equipment":[],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-burpee-dans","name":"Burpee Dans","text":"This exercise is OYO. Line up across field/parking lot. Perform 1 Burpee : 4 lunges forward until you reach other side of parking lot. Turn around, perform 2 burpees : 4 lunges back to starting position. Rinse and repeat as necessary increasing burpees by 1. Pick up the six or plank until all PAX finish.","kind":"thang","emphasis":["cardio","core","lower"],"equipment":["field"],"tags":["routine"]},{"id":"x-burpee-mile","name":"Burpee Mile","text":"48 burpees, 1 mile run. Done as 12 burpees, run 1/4 mile x 4.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["cardio","run"],"equipment":[],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-burpee-sandwich","name":"Burpee Sandwich","text":"Place your block on the ground in front of you with space on either side. Start standing to the left of the block. Perform one Burpee. Step to the block and perform one Blocky (Manmaker). Step to the right of the block and perform one Burpee. That’s one rep.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["cardio","heavy"],"equipment":["coupon"],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-burpeevators","name":"Burpeevators","text":"A ladder of exercises in the form of deconstructed Burpees:\n@Burpee\n@Flying Squirrel\n@Merkin\n@Jump Squat\nExample:\nMosey to location 1: Do 10 of each.\nMosey to location 2: Do 9 of each.\nRinse and repeat down to 1 of each.","kind":"thang","emphasis":["cardio","lower","upper"],"equipment":[],"tags":["routine"]},{"id":"x-burpo","name":"Burpo","text":"A low burpee. Starting position is bottom of a squat. Then reach hands out to ground, legs fire back into a plank, chest to the ground, pushup, draw legs back into a squat, final position is the bottom of a squat. No standing up for the duration of the reps.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["cardio","core","lower","upper"],"equipment":[],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-bus-driver","name":"Bus Driver","text":"Hold a coupon with both hands in front of your body at chest-to-face height, as if gripping a steering wheel. Keeping your arms extended, rotate the block left and right in a controlled side-to-side motion, like turning a steering wheel while driving.\nCan be performed while walking or while stationary and as a pure rotation at a fixed height or combined with a front raise (lift the coupon from waist to face level, then rotate left and right at the top).","kind":"thang","emphasis":["heavy","upper"],"equipment":["coupon"],"tags":["routine"]},{"id":"x-butkus","name":"Butkus","text":"Butkus Consists of rapid step ups on a curb for at least a minute, then 30 second rest, then another minute, etc. (like rounds of boxing...how many rounds the Q wants to bring it). At least 3, with a \"Ding, ding\"","kind":"thang","emphasis":["lower"],"equipment":["bench_wall"],"tags":["routine"]},{"id":"x-butterfly-sit-up","name":"Butterfly Sit-up","text":"Butterfly sit-ups are a sit-up variation where the bottom of the feet are pressed against each other so the legs are in a diamond shape for a greater range of motion and reduced involvement from the hip flexors compared to classic sit-ups.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["core","lower","mobility","upper"],"equipment":[],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-buzz-saw","name":"Buzz Saw","text":"Starting in a chillcut plank, rock your entire body forward and backward in cadence engaging your core as you move.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["core"],"equipment":[],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-c-h-i-p-s-and-dips","name":"C.H.I.P.S. and Dips","text":"Complete 20 reps each of exercises, in cadence, followed by 20 dips off a park bench or ledge. Then run a lap. Rinse and repeat as needed. Swap out the exercises and in a coupon as desired.\nC - Calf Raises, Dips\nH - Hello Dollies, Dips\nI - Imperial Walkers, Dips\nP - Pickle Pointers, Dips\nS - Squats, Dips\nCrafted by Roleplay out of F3 Twin Cities","kind":"thang","emphasis":["cardio","heavy","lower","run","upper"],"equipment":["bench_wall","coupon"],"tags":["routine"]},{"id":"x-c2c","name":"C2C","text":"C2C Short for Corner to Corner, running short, fast distances to a corner or designated spot, where the #SugarRays pick up a plank to wait for the #Six.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["cardio","core","run"],"equipment":[],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-cactus-jump-squat","name":"Cactus Jump Squat","text":"With a block standing vertically, squat down till you're siting on the block, then raise you're feet off the ground, put them back down and explode up into a jump squat. Could be done IC, but done best OYO.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["heavy","lower"],"equipment":["coupon"],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-cactus-jumps","name":"Cactus Jumps","text":"Think Cactus Jack with a jump.\nHands over head, starting position is seated on coupon. Feet come off the ground, then stand up like a normal Cactus Jack, but instead of a small jump at the top, jump onto an elevated surface like a curb or bleacher. Step back down, repeat.\nWorks best if elevated surfaces are knee level or above, but a curb works too.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["heavy","lower"],"equipment":["bench_wall","coupon"],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-capri-lap","name":"Capri Lap","text":"Capri Lap Usually a warmup lap around the parking lot or AO staying close enough to be seen by any that arrive late, but can include and or all of the the warmup. Named this in honor of Mint Hill''s Capri who seems to always be a minute or two late.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["cardio","upper"],"equipment":[],"tags":["warmup"]},{"id":"x-captain-morgan","name":"Captain Morgan","text":"Captain Morgan In plank position raise on one side and bring the high side knee up. Like Captain Morgan.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["core"],"equipment":[],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-captain-therkin","name":"Captain Therkin","text":"Captain Therkin Captain Thor modified with 5 merkins between each set. 1:4, 5x merkin, 2:8, 5x merkin, 3:12, 5x merkin, etc.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["upper"],"equipment":[],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-captain-thor","name":"Captain Thor","text":"Captain Thor An ab exercise done in a 1:4 ratio. 1 big boy sit up to 4 American Hammers (Russian Twist). Try to get 10:40 before Merlot comes.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["core"],"equipment":[],"tags":["mary"]},{"id":"x-carioca","name":"Carioca","text":"Carioca Running while crossing left foot over right and twisting at the hips, reverse - like the DBs do in the NFL. Often mistaken for Karaoke.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["cardio","run"],"equipment":[],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-carolina-dry-docks","name":"Carolina Dry Docks","text":"Modified push-up. Bend only your elbows, allowing body to drop head toward hands without lowering your six.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["upper"],"equipment":[],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-carolina-knee-dips","name":"Carolina Knee Dips","text":"Start in a Declined Downward Dog position, with your feet on a bench… Touch your knees to the ground, then move back into a Declined Downward Dog position. Keep your core engaged and control every rep.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["core","upper"],"equipment":["bench_wall"],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-catalina-wine-mixer","name":"Catalina Wine Mixer","text":"Catalina Wine Mixer Starting in plank position, go down onto each arm into a chilcutt. Last arm down becomes the first one to go back up into a plank. Then do a merkin. That''s 1.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["core","upper"],"equipment":[],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-catapillar-walk","name":"Catapillar Walk","text":"Standing with arms straight forward, palms down as close to toes as possible while keeping knees straight.\nArm walk away from toes to full body extension, then walk back to toes. Return to starting position, and that's 1 rep.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["upper"],"equipment":[],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-catch-me-if-you-can","name":"Catch Me If You Can","text":"Partner up. Partner 1 performs 5 Burpees (or 10 Diamond Merkins or X Number of Whatever the Q says), and then sprints to catch the Partner 2, who has been running backwards. Repeato until Q says stop or track lap is complete.","kind":"thang","emphasis":["cardio","run","upper"],"equipment":["field"],"tags":["partner","routine"]},{"id":"x-catch-us-if-you-can","name":"Catch Us If You Can","text":"Three partners. Partner A partner carries Partner B. Partner C performs 5 Burpees (or 10 Diamond Merkins or X Number of Whatever the Q says), and then sprints to catch the pair. Partner C then partner carries Partner A. Partner B performs the called number of the called exercise and then sprints to catch the pair. Partner B then partner carries Partner C. Partner A performs the called number of the called exercise and then sprints to catch the pair. Repeato.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["cardio","run","upper"],"equipment":[],"tags":["partner"]},{"id":"x-caterpillar","name":"Caterpillar","text":"Caterpillar PAX forms 2 lines face-to-face, down in plank position. Allow 2-3 feet between PAX. Last man box-jumps over the planking PAX to the head of the line, Indian Run style. Continue cycling through over a Q-prescribed distance or until toasted.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["cardio","core","lower","run"],"equipment":[],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-charles-bronson","name":"Charles Bronson","text":"Start with 3 shovel flags, cones or other distance markers with first two 100 yards apart in a line, the last another 10-30 yards past. At starting point, perform 50 SSH's, sprint to 2nd point, then army crawl or bear crawl to 3rd point. Mosey back to start, 50 Merkins then rinse/repeat. 50 burpees, rinse/repeat. 50 LBC's, rinse/repeat. Finish with 50 Jump Squats rinse/repeat. Coupons optional. NOTE: a white board at start with exercises listed is invaluable.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["cardio","core","heavy","lower","run","upper"],"equipment":["cones","coupon"],"tags":["mary"]},{"id":"x-cheerleader","name":"Cheerleader","text":"Cheerleader Start in SSH position, go to the up SSH position, on the down go into a squat and bring hands to a point below the knees and repeat. Can be called IC or OYO.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["lower"],"equipment":[],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-cheerleader-merkin","name":"Cheerleader Merkin","text":"Cheerleader Merkin Needed: odd count of pax (example below is with 5 pax) and a raised surface (bench, bleacher, etc) 3 pax in plank side by side 2 pax on top (with feet on bench and hands on back of 2 pax below) to form pyramid 10 abyss merkins for pax on top and everyone rotates clockwise until rotation is complete","kind":"thang","emphasis":["core","upper"],"equipment":["bench_wall"],"tags":["routine"]},{"id":"x-cherkin","name":"CHerkin","text":"CHerkin Like a merkin or carolina dry dock but you lower your body slowly to touch your forehead to the ground. \"CH\" refers to \"Cheesehead\". (Thanks Carrier in CLT Metro.)","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["upper"],"equipment":[],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-chicken-peckers","name":"Chicken Peckers","text":"Chicken Peckers Feet up on the Wall, Hands on the ground. In Cadence lift your hand and touch your opposite shoulder.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["upper"],"equipment":["bench_wall"],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-chilcutt-peter-parkers","name":"Chilcutt Peter Parkers","text":"While holding Chilcutt position (see above), alternate bringing each leg up towards your arms (see Peter Parkers).","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["lower","upper"],"equipment":[],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-chilcutts","name":"Chilcutts","text":"Chilcutts An elbow plank. All elbows and no discernible movement is the way Big Pete rolled.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["core"],"equipment":[],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-chilly-broad-jumps","name":"Chilly Broad Jumps","text":"Chilly Broad Jumps Each Pax member will be in the Chillcut position about 4-5 feet apart.Â The person on the end will Broad Jump over each person until he gets to the end.Â Then he will Chilcut and the next guy broad jumps etc. etc.Â This will continue for 25-50 yards depending on the Q.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["cardio","lower"],"equipment":[],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-chilly-jacks","name":"Chilly Jacks","text":"Chilly Jacks A kissing cousin to the Plank Jack. This is a jumping jack while in the Chilcutt plank position.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["cardio","core","lower"],"equipment":[],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-chinook-squats","name":"Chinook Squats","text":"Three Chinook arm circles, followed by a squat, count in cadence. Repeato until you feel you've had enough.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["lower","upper"],"equipment":[],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-chuck-norris-merkins","name":"Chuck Norris Merkins","text":"AKA the \"Knerkin\". A traditional Merkin but performed using the knuckles instead of the open hand.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["upper"],"equipment":[],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-chumbaburpee","name":"Chumbaburpee","text":"The Q plays \"Tubthumping\" by Chumbawamba. Start with SSH at the beginning of the song, and every time they say, \"I get knocked down, but I get up again,\" do a burpee. While not doing burpees, continue performing SSH. By the end of the song, you will have done approximately 27 burpees. This exercise is great for the Warmorama and can help shut down any mumblechatter early in the workout or at any point during it.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["cardio","upper"],"equipment":["speaker"],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-ciabatta","name":"Ciabatta","text":"Ciabatta Properly known as''Tabata.'' A four-minute #Routine that involves 20 seconds of work followed by 10 seconds of of rest repeated 8 times.'' Properly done, all but guaranteed to induce #TBQ. Good for introverted Qs.","kind":"thang","emphasis":[],"equipment":["timer"],"tags":["routine"]},{"id":"x-cindy","name":"Cindy","text":"Cindy AMRAP in 20 minutes: 5 pullups, 10 merkins, & 15 squats.\"Borrowed\" from a popular fitness craze, Cindy is a great total body beatdown and a great benchmark to gauge your progress over time. Plus, if you complete 20 rounds during the 20 minutes, add a mile run to the front and back end of the workout, and you''ve just completed The Murph.","kind":"thang","emphasis":["cardio","lower","run","upper"],"equipment":["pull_up_bar"],"tags":["benchmark","routine"]},{"id":"x-cindy-crawford","name":"Cindy Crawford","text":"Cindy Crawford Like Cindy (AMRAP 5 pull-ups, 10 merkins, and 15 squats) Plus 20 LBCs and 25 toe raises to get the full body bikini ready. Complete 20 rounds in 30 minutes and you''re ready for the two piece!","kind":"thang","emphasis":["core","lower","upper"],"equipment":["pull_up_bar"],"tags":["mary","routine"]},{"id":"x-circle-burp","name":"Circle Burp","text":"PAX Circle up and start chopping feet or doing high knees. Starting with the Q and going around the circle each PAX, one by one, calls out \"down\" and everyone drops and does a burpee. The circle burp is complete after each PAX in the circle has called \"down\". This is similar to doing Up Downs.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["cardio"],"equipment":[],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-classic-sit-up","name":"Classic Sit-Up","text":"Start on your back with knees bent and touching eachother, and your hands touching your head. Activate your core by bringing your chest to your knees. Your feet should remain flat on the ground, knees together, and your hands should never stop touching your head.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["core","upper"],"equipment":[],"tags":["mary"]},{"id":"x-clerkin","name":"Clerkin","text":"Clerkin A merkin with a clap, either OYO or with a partner.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["cardio","upper"],"equipment":[],"tags":["partner"]},{"id":"x-cliff-hanger-arm-ups","name":"Cliff Hanger Arm-ups","text":"Cliff Hanger Arm-ups Think of it as a cliff hanger merkin and step ups getting together and having a baby. Get with a partner and get in cliff hanger position (see cliff hanger merkin) but you want to do it on a bench or picnic table something that has a upper and lower level. Start on lower part of bench or whatever you are using. When Q says go right arm up left arm up right arm down left arm down. You get the picture. Best to do OYO and keep a good grip or this will become a face smasher.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["lower","upper"],"equipment":["bench_wall"],"tags":["partner"]},{"id":"x-cliff-hanger-merkins","name":"Cliff Hanger Merkins","text":"Cliff Hanger Merkins Cliff Hanger Merkins are performed in parking decks all across F3Nation. In order to complete the exercise you will need a partner. P1 will grab ahold of a rail or top of a wall on the perimeter of the parking garage at any level. P2 will hold P1''s legs in the air while P1 completes the required number of Merkins. Nothing more, nothing less. #Disclaimer is always necessary for this exercise.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["lower","upper"],"equipment":["bench_wall"],"tags":["partner"]},{"id":"x-climate-change","name":"Climate Change","text":"While in a circle the Pax holds the ''Al Gore'' pose. The Pax then proceeds to do a time bomb (just like the Merkin Time Bomb). A five burpee time bomb is a great way to end the mumble chatter. Continue the countdown until the Q is smoked or everyone quits. The burpee can be switched to jump lunges or burpees depending on the mood of the Q.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["cardio","lower","upper"],"equipment":[],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-clock-merkins","name":"Clock Merkins","text":"Clock Merkins Find a hill and line up in plank position at 12 o''clock. 5 Merkins. Move to 3 o''clock, 5 Merkins. Move to 6, 9, or whatever Q calls out and do 5 Merkins in each position.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["core","upper"],"equipment":[],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-clock-pendulum","name":"Clock Pendulum","text":"Bending at waist, back straight parallel to ground. Use sandbag/ weight / CMU raise weight 90 deg to left, back to center, 90 deg to right, back to center....repeat Keep back straight.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["heavy"],"equipment":["coupon","sandbag","weights"],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-clowney","name":"Clowney","text":"Clowney Named after the Univ. of South Carolina football DE standout, this exercise involves 7 sets (per Clowneys''s college jersey number 7). The exercises are 4 jumping lunges in cadence (IC) followed by 4 merkins IC. Rinse and repeat this set of exercises 7 times.","kind":"thang","emphasis":["lower","upper"],"equipment":[],"tags":["routine"]},{"id":"x-clurpee","name":"Clurpee","text":"A burpee, with a clap merkin instead of a regular merkin.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["cardio","upper"],"equipment":[],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-coach","name":"Coach","text":"Partner up into groups of 3. Partner 1 performs a pull up and holds in the up position while partner 2 takes on the role of the Coach. It''s the Coach''s responsibility to encourage P1 to give his best effort, to push through the pain, to do whatever it takes to stay in the up position while P3 sprints around the pickle (parking lot) one time. Upon P3's arrival P1 comes down from the pull up and gives P2 a high five for being a great coach. P1 will now sprint the pickle while P2 goes up on the bar. P3 is now the coach. This cycle continues until everyone has had a turn at all three positions. Repeat until all pax have lost their voices, arms have fallen off, or the Q is ready to move on.","kind":"thang","emphasis":["cardio","run","upper"],"equipment":[],"tags":["partner","routine"]},{"id":"x-cocaine-bear-crawl","name":"Cocaine Bear Crawl","text":"A bear crawl across a parking lot, stopping at each white line to perform a merkin, bringing your nose to the white line.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["upper"],"equipment":[],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-cockroach-resurrection","name":"Cockroach Resurrection","text":"Cockroach Resurrection 4-count ab exercise done lying down on your six and pulling your knees and arms to your chest, then rapidly extending arms and legs back out, then back in. Preferably done directly after the Dying Cockroach and with at least one extra rep.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["lower","upper"],"equipment":[],"tags":["mary"]},{"id":"x-code-red","name":"Code Red","text":"The Call of Code Red is a call for all PAX to immediately stop in place and perform 5 burpees OYO. Any PAX can call the code red at any time during the BD, but it is usually done when the Q is indecisive or pauses too long before calling the next exercise. The term comes from the Movie A Few Good Men. \"Did you order the code red? Your GD right I did!\"","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["cardio"],"equipment":[],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-colonel-trautman","name":"Colonel Trautman","text":"Pair up and one partner runs 20 yards to the pull up bar and do 3 pull ups while the other partner does either 5 fingertip Merkins or 10 regular Merkins then hold Chillcutt for their partner to tell them to go and do their pull ups. And you do as many sets as you can with in the time frame the Q gives you.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["cardio","upper"],"equipment":["pull_up_bar"],"tags":["partner"]},{"id":"x-colt-45","name":"Colt 45","text":"45 Cinder Block Curls (Similar to 21's). 15 reps go from the bottom of the movement up to the halfway point (with your arms at a 90 degree angle and hands at elbow level). 15 reps Go from the halfway point up to the top of the bicep curl (hands up near shoulder level). 15 reps Start at the bottom of the movement and complete a full range of movement all the way up.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["heavy","upper"],"equipment":["coupon"],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-commando-jacks","name":"Commando Jacks","text":"Start in the High Plank (push-up position), drop one elbow, then the other to achieve the Chilcutt Plank and then back to the high plank. Then both arms and legs fly out to the sides like a horizontal jumping jack - akin to a plank jack, but adding in the arms - and then back to the starting position. Repeat for reps.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["cardio","core","lower","upper"],"equipment":[],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-concrete-canoe","name":"Concrete Canoe","text":"Each pair of PAX begins on their Sixes, facing each other. May brace each other's legs for support. PAX 1 holds a coupon (cinder block) to the chest, PAX 2 is empty-handed.\nOn Cue, simultaneously perform Big Boy Sit Ups. At the top of each positive motion, pass the coupon to each other, then perform the negative motion. Repeat.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["core","heavy","lower","upper"],"equipment":["coupon"],"tags":["competitive","game","mary"]},{"id":"x-contra-burpees","name":"Contra Burpees","text":"Burpees with increasing number of merkins. Especially effective when combined with Broad Jumps.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["cardio","lower","upper"],"equipment":[],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-control-freak-merkins","name":"Control Freak Merkins","text":"Control Freak Merkins The Q has complete control of the merkin. His down and up. This can be as brutal as the Q wants it.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["upper"],"equipment":[],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-conveyor-belt","name":"Conveyor Belt","text":"Conveyor Belt Columns of 5-6 PAX deep, standing at \"stations\" positioned 2 parking spaces apart, perform appointed exercise (5 monkey humpers or 3 merkins, for example), BearCrawl forward to next station, guy at front runs to back of column. Reverse Conveyor Belt is the same idea but going in the reverse direction by CrawlBearing between stations. This works really nicely with kettlebells: leave your kettlebell at the station where you start.","kind":"thang","emphasis":["cardio","heavy","lower","upper"],"equipment":["weights"],"tags":["routine"]},{"id":"x-cooler-super-duper-cooler","name":"Cooler / Super Duper Cooler","text":"For the Cooler... start with a side plank, resting on your forearm at 90 degrees. Legs are resting together. The exercise is done in four-count cadence. On 1, the top leg extends upward parallel to the body (as in \"right arm high, but it's your leg\"). On 2, you're back to original position with legs back together. On 3, tuck the top leg toward your chest. There, the knee should meet the top hand around shoulder level. On 4, you're back to original position again. Typically, Q calls out 10 on the right side, then flapjack, and perform 10 on the left. The Super Duper Cooler is the same, except you're not resting on your forearm... you're in full extension and supported only by your hand.","kind":"thang","emphasis":["cardio","core","lower","upper"],"equipment":[],"tags":["routine"]},{"id":"x-copperhead-lunge","name":"Copperhead Lunge","text":"In the same family as the Copperhead Squat, it is a stepped lunge with one leg at a time, go down further each count in a 4 count cadence.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["lower"],"equipment":[],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-copperhead-merkins","name":"Copperhead Merkins","text":"Regular Merkin, each rep done in 3 stages, much like the copperhead squat. Excellent in high reps to feel the burn on the deltoids and rhomboids. Can be modified ad infinitum (eg copperhead derkin, copperhead drydock, etc.)","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["lower","upper"],"equipment":[],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-copperhead-squat","name":"Copperhead Squat","text":"Regular squat but lowering body slowly on first 3 counts, then lifting up on 4 count. Good form is keeping hands on back of heads with elbows held back, weight on heels, and back kept straight.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["heavy","lower"],"equipment":["weights"],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-cosey","name":"Cosey","text":"Mosey with a coupon.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["cardio","heavy"],"equipment":["coupon"],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-cotton-eyed-joe","name":"Cotton-eyed Joe","text":"Cotton-eyed Joe The Q plays \"Cotton Eye Joe\" by Rednex. Start with Side Straddle Hops (SSH) to the music when the singing begins. When the banjo solo starts, squat low, then raise and kick your leg to the left, squat low again, and kick your leg to the right. Alternate legs. When the music changes and the woman sings, switch to merkins. Switch back to Side Straddle Hops when the man sings again. Rinse and repeat: Man singing: SSH / Banjo solo: CEJ / Woman singing: Merkins","kind":"thang","emphasis":["lower","upper"],"equipment":["speaker"],"tags":["routine"]},{"id":"x-coupon-crucible","name":"Coupon Crucible","text":"This is a block curl straight into a overhead press and then slowly (3-5) count to lower the block into starting position. That's one rep","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["heavy","upper"],"equipment":["coupon"],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-coupon-curl","name":"Coupon Curl","text":"A curl with cinderblock","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["heavy","upper"],"equipment":["coupon"],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-coupon-kettle-bell-swing","name":"Coupon Kettle Bell Swing","text":"A dynamic, full-body exercise where you swing a kettlebell (or coupon/found object) between your legs and up to chest or shoulder height using a powerful hip hinge movement. Start with feet shoulder-width apart, hinge at the hips to swing the weight back between your legs, then explosively drive your hips forward to propel the weight upward. Keep your arms relatively straight and let the hip thrust generate the power. This movement builds explosive strength, cardiovascular endurance, and works the posterior chain, core, and shoulders","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["core","heavy","lower","upper"],"equipment":["coupon","swing","weights"],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-coupon-military-press","name":"Coupon Military Press","text":"A shoulder-focused strength exercise where you press a cinderblock (cindy) from shoulder height straight overhead to full arm extension. Start with the cindy held at shoulder level, core engaged and feet shoulder-width apart. Press the block straight up until your arms are fully extended overhead, then lower it back to the starting position with control. The awkward shape and weight distribution of the cinderblock challenges grip strength, shoulder stability, and core engagement more than traditional weights.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["core","heavy","upper"],"equipment":["coupon","weights"],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-coupon-salt-shaker","name":"Coupon Salt Shaker","text":"The Slat Shaker and its up-mod the Squat Shaker are classic variations on the coupon curl where the coupon is curled up once over each shoulder.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["heavy","lower","upper"],"equipment":["coupon"],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-coyote-uglys","name":"Coyote Uglys","text":"Coyote Uglys Find a picnic table and partner up. Starting in a wheel barrow position with partner, PAX will start on the ground and step up to picnic table ''seat'' with their hands , complete 1 Merkin, step up to top of the ''table'' , 1 Merkin, step down to the ''seat'', 1 Merkin, step down to the ground, 1 Merkin. That completes 1 rep. Goal is 5 reps, then switch with Partner.","kind":"thang","emphasis":["lower","upper"],"equipment":["bench_wall"],"tags":["partner","routine"]},{"id":"x-cprs","name":"CPRs","text":"A combination of 3 Arm exercises with Cinderblocks. Starting position, like doing curls, and done all together in 6-count cadence. Watch the video, for example.\n1=\"C\"url. 2= Overhead \"P\"ress. 3 = Tricep \"R\"aise. 4= Tricep Extension (returning back towards the starting position). 5= Return to OHP starting position. 6=Reverse Curl returning to waist (starting position). PAX counts the rep on step 6.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["heavy","upper"],"equipment":["coupon"],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-crab-cakes","name":"Crab Cakes","text":"Start from crab walk position, raise right hand and left leg, touch hand to knee. Return to starting position and repeat with opposite hand/leg. In cadence.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["lower"],"equipment":[],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-crab-humper","name":"Crab Humper","text":"Like air humpers but in the crab walk position (hands and feet on ground, keeping 6 off ground, thrust hips up and down).","kind":"exercise","emphasis":[],"equipment":[],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-crab-jacks","name":"Crab Jacks","text":"Just like plank jacks, but facing the sky. Get into crab walk position, knees bent at 90 degrees and hips towards the sky. Move thighs apart and back together. Decline CJ are when feet are uphill.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["core"],"equipment":[],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-crab-vs-bear-soccer","name":"Crab vs. Bear Soccer","text":"Crab vs. Bear Soccer Preferably played on a soccer field with goals, divide into teams, one team has to crab walk while the other has to bear crawl. Once someone scores a goal, then the teams swap roles (bear to crab and crab to bear). Goalies have to plank, and goalies must be swapped out after every goal scored. Play for as long as you want, real men play for at least 20 minutes.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["core"],"equipment":["field"],"tags":["team"]},{"id":"x-crab-walk","name":"Crab Walk","text":"Crab Walk (Aka Jameis Winston in some parts.) Balancing on your hands and feet with your front facing the ceiling and your hips thrust upwards. Walk like a crab.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":[],"equipment":[],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-cracker-jacks","name":"Cracker Jacks","text":"Cracker Jacks Starting in ATG-Frog Squat position, w/ both arms extended straight down b/w legs + hands planted on ground. Perform a Star Jump & return to 1st position.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["lower","upper"],"equipment":[],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-crawl-bear","name":"Crawl Bear","text":"Crawl Bear Same as Bear Crawl, except backwards. Totally different exercise. Often combined with Bear Crawl, as in, \"Bear Crawl up and Crawl Bear back.\"","kind":"exercise","emphasis":[],"equipment":[],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-crawl-bear-360","name":"Crawl Bear 360","text":"Perform Crawl Bear while rotating 360 degrees the entire time. Can be performed clockwise or counter-clockwise.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":[],"equipment":[],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-creapees","name":"Creapees","text":"This is a normal burpee with a creature merkin variant at the bottom. This version of the creature merkin is where the creature is climbing out of the black lagoon, so it is performed in front of a bench and transitions from a regular merkin to an inclined merkin (F3Orlando Flowerchild favorite).","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["cardio","upper"],"equipment":["bench_wall"],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-creature-merkins","name":"Creature Merkins","text":"Creature Merkins Start in an incline merkin position with feet together on the ground hand up on seat/bench. Using feet as a pivot and keeping your body straight, move your body with your hands to the right then down to the ground to perform a merkin. Then, using hands, bring yourself back up on the seat/bench and over to the left side to perform a merkin. Q''s call on how many merkins to perform on each side.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["upper"],"equipment":["bench_wall"],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-cross-climbers","name":"Cross Climbers","text":"Similar to @Mountain Climbers , but instead of bringing your right knee up to your right elbow and your left knee up to your left elbow, you cross your knees to the opposite elbow. Right knee to the left elbow, and left knee to the right elbow.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["core"],"equipment":[],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-crowd-pleaser","name":"Crowd Pleaser","text":"Essentially a Merkin followed by a Groiner, but done as a pyramid. For regular men, going from 1:1 (1 Merkin and 1 Groiner) to 4:4 (4 Merkins followed by 4 Groiners) and back down to 1:1 may be a challenge, but average F3 men should go from 1:1 up to 5:5 and back down to 1:1 to truly enjoy the moment (at total of 25 reps of each). Working up to a 6:6 pyramid is an admirable goal for the Sugar Rays in the PAX... going any higher is not advised unless you have good disability insurance.","kind":"thang","emphasis":["upper"],"equipment":[],"tags":["routine"]},{"id":"x-crucible-merkin","name":"Crucible Merkin","text":"Crucible Merkin Start in a wide merkin stance with hands much further out than shoulder-width. Rotate hands 90 degrees outward until they are facing away from the body. Perform a merkin.","kind":"thang","emphasis":["upper"],"equipment":[],"tags":["routine"]},{"id":"x-crunchy-frog","name":"Crunchy Frog","text":"Done in cadence, in a V-like sitting position, first wrap your legs with your arms. Quickly open yourself up by moving your arms out to your sides and extending your legs out in front of you. Bring them back in. Repeato. Video here.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["cardio","core","lower","upper"],"equipment":[],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-cumberland-county-viaduct-ccv","name":"Cumberland County Viaduct (CCV)","text":"Basically - these are side raises. Lay on side with weight on elbow. In cadence - 1) raise hip up as high as you can. 2) back down but don''t let other hip touch ground 3) raise up again 4) back down.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["heavy"],"equipment":["weights"],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-cupid-shuffle","name":"Cupid Shuffle","text":"Cupid Shuffle The Q plays \"Cupid Shuffle.\" Follow the commands from the plank position: Right = right, Left = left, Kick = kick, Walk = Mt. Climber, Down = merkin. EXTRA: Do mountain climbers when not performing the specified movements.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["core","upper"],"equipment":[],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-curb-alpert","name":"Curb Alpert","text":"In push up position alongside curb, and walk hands up and down the the curb as if they are drumming like the legendary Herb Alpert.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["lower","upper"],"equipment":["bench_wall"],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-cut-a-flip","name":"Cut A Flip","text":"Alternating between 5 Merkins and 5 Big Boy Sit-ups, flipping between the 2 exercises over and over, no rest. Can be performed until a specific number is reached, ex. 100 Merkins and 100 Big Boys; or can be used in an AMRAP scenario that is timed such as 1 Minute or waiting for partner to complete a movement.","kind":"thang","emphasis":["core","upper"],"equipment":[],"tags":["mary","partner","routine"]},{"id":"x-daft-punk","name":"Daft Punk","text":"Lunge exercise performed in cadence with a cadence count that you cycle through three times (12 count move). Also sometimes know as the \"around the world lunge\" hence the F3 Moniker after Daft Punk''s classic \"Around the World.\" Right leg lunge forward (step back to center after each) / Right leg lunge sideways / Right leg lunge back / Left leg lunge back / Left leg lunge sideways / Left leg lunge forward. This completes one full Daft Punk.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["lower"],"equipment":[],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-dan-taylor","name":"Dan Taylor","text":"Dan Taylor Punishing leg exercise that is a cousin (of sorts) to Jack Webb. Named after Lt. Dan in Forrest Gump, it combines 1 squat followed by 4 lunges (alternating legs) in ascending order (maintaining the 1:4 ratio). It will leave the PAX feeling like \"they ain''t got no legs\".","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["lower"],"equipment":[],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-dancing-bear-pyramid","name":"Dancing Bear Pyramid","text":"PAX perform 1 Merkin and then recover to perform 1 Dancing Bear (Andean Bear from Nashville Zoo on news...basically a jump squat and OHP). R&R going up until 10 & 10. Then back down the other side of the pyramid back to 1 each. Great way to get in 101 Merkins and OHP Jump Squats in ~6 minutes as invented at F3Nolensville","kind":"thang","emphasis":["lower","upper"],"equipment":[],"tags":["routine"]},{"id":"x-dancing-bears","name":"Dancing Bears","text":"Hands and feet on the ground, lift left leg and right arm to an uncomfortable height, then back on ground. Lift right leg and left arm to an uncomfortable height, return to the ground. Works great with a 4 count.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["lower","upper"],"equipment":[],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-dancing-chilcutt","name":"Dancing Chilcutt","text":"Elbow Plank w/alternating leg lifts in cadence. Great for the back, not so much for the elbows.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["core","lower"],"equipment":[],"tags":["mary"]},{"id":"x-danger-zone","name":"Danger Zone","text":"The Q plays \"Danger Zone\" by Kenny Loggins. The PAX continually performs side straddle hops (SSH). Every time the words \"danger zone\" are heard, the PAX does a single squat before resuming SSH. Alternatively, you can do burpees for each \"danger zone\" phrase. The end result is approximately 3.5 minutes of SSH with intermittent squats.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["cardio","lower"],"equipment":[],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-daniel-son","name":"Daniel-Son","text":"Karate Kid crane kick position. Alternate legs in quick succession. \"If do right, none can defend.\"","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["lower"],"equipment":[],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-darekong-merkins","name":"DareKong Merkins","text":"Crawl out, merkin, shoulder tap, merkin, shoulder tap; merkin, knee touch, merkin, knee knee touch; merkin, touch the foot, merkin, touch the foot; merkin, swing toe touch, merkin, swing toe touch; merkin, Mike Tyson, merkin; crawl back, then squat and up = 1 rep.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["lower","upper"],"equipment":["swing"],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-dark-webbs","name":"Dark Webbs","text":"A series of Webb routines. A Jack Webb starts with 1 Merkin and 2 Raise the Roofs, then the Merkins increase one at a time while the Raise the Roofs increase in that 1 to 2 ratio, so that you end with 10 Merkins and 20 Raise the Roofs. The Dark Webb consists of all the following, done without rest: Jack Webb - 1 Merkin to 2 Raise the Roofs House of Paine - 1 Jump Squat with 2 Iron Mikes / Bonnie Blairs / Jump Lunges (one per leg) Captain Thor - 1 Big Boy with 2 American Hammers (4 count, if you want the PAX to stop complaining) Happy Jack Webb - A bad marriage between a Happy Jack and a Jack Webb - 1 Burpee with 2 Side Straddle Hops (at this point 4 count is unnecessary) This one is fairly brutal, so don''t plan on getting much out of the PAX after it. Invented by Preach from Birmingham.","kind":"thang","emphasis":["cardio","core","lower","upper"],"equipment":[],"tags":["mary","routine"]},{"id":"x-davinci-cartwheel","name":"DaVinci Cartwheel","text":"Begin in a low squat. Reach across with both hands, placing your left hand next to your right foot and your right hand a bit further off. Push off with your feet, lift your hips over your shoulders into a mini tucked handstand, then (as gracefully as possible) put your feet back down past your right hand (left foot next to right hand), facing the same direction as you started. Rinse and repeat. Sometimes called a \"monkey crawl\" or \"monkey scoot.\" Can be done in both directions.","kind":"thang","emphasis":["lower","upper"],"equipment":[],"tags":["competitive","game","routine"]},{"id":"x-dayton-flyers","name":"Dayton Flyers","text":"Take flight like the original Dayton Flyer. PAX runs 25 yards, stops does a burpee with a jump squat, then runs 25 yards to end. Turn around and repeat process back to start. The more you do the better. Orville and Wilbur Wright would be proud.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["cardio","lower"],"equipment":[],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-de-motivators","name":"De-motivators","text":"Deconstruct an exercise and execute/count it like @Motivators\nExamples: @CPRs @Burpee @World War III Sit-up\nCan be done with multiple exercises in the count.\nFor example, a Burpee might be deconstructed into the following:\nFlying Squirrel\nMerkin\nMonkey Humper\nJump Squat","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["cardio","core","lower","upper"],"equipment":[],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-death-rabbit","name":"Death Rabbit","text":"Variation of the Murder Bunny.\nStart as you would with a Murder Bunny by bending and moving the coupon forward as far our as possible. At this point PAX does a diamond merkin with hands on the coupon. \"Hop\" your feet to either side of the coupon. At this point PAX will perform a thruster with their coupon.\nReset for the next rep.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["heavy","upper"],"equipment":["coupon"],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-death-star","name":"Death Star","text":"Set 10 cones out in shape of star. Bear crawl to each cone and perform 30 merkins at each. Adds up to total of 300. Good times.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["upper"],"equipment":["cones"],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-deck-of-death","name":"Deck of Death","text":"A routine done with a deck of playing cards where each suit is an exercise and each card dictates the number of reps you do of that exercise all the way up to an Ace being 14 reps. Exercise complete when all 52 cards have been flipped.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":[],"equipment":[],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-deconstructed-burpees","name":"Deconstructed Burpees","text":"The perfect exercise, broken down into pieces. Squats, then leg thrusts, then Merkins, then leg thrusts, then up. For example, do 10 squats, 10 leg thrusts, 10 Merkins, 10 leg thrusts, then up. Decrease reps by 1 each time until you get to 1 each.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["cardio","lower","upper"],"equipment":[],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-deep-sea-diver","name":"Deep Sea Diver","text":"Hip Slapper variation. Best used on steps. 1. Start with feet on 1st step. Perform x amount of Hip Slappers. 2. Move feet up 1 step. Perform x amount of Hip Slappers. Continue with this pattern, reaching desired pinnacle. (5 or more steps = F3). 3. Then move feet down 1 step. Perform x amount of Hip Slappers. Repeat pattern until reaching 1st step. Looks like a deep sea diver swimming down down down.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["cardio"],"equipment":["stairs"],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-del-brown","name":"Del Brown","text":"Named after saltwater fly fisherman who developed spectacular Merkin Crab fly. 10 Merkins then 25 yard Crab Walk then 10 Diamond Merkins then 25 yard Crab Walk then 10 Merkins. Repeato.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["upper"],"equipment":[],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-derkin","name":"Derkin","text":"Decline merkin. Legs raised or elevated so that the push-up accents the arms.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["lower","upper"],"equipment":[],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-derkin-n-diayes","name":"Derkin N'Diayes","text":"The other end of the rainbow of the Makhtar N'Diayes movements: From Derkin position (feet up), a 5-count exercise in which you put each foot to the ground and back into regular Derkin position, and then complete a Derkin. Increase the incline to really burn your core.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["core"],"equipment":[],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-derricks","name":"Derricks","text":"Derricks Single leg dead lift, slow 4-ct in cadence. Good warm up/balance move. Movement resembles oil derricks.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["lower","upper"],"equipment":[],"tags":["warmup"]},{"id":"x-devin-hester","name":"Devin Hester","text":"Two PAX of similar speed, one with a rock or other coupon and a small headstart, race 100 yds. 2nd Pax attempts to run down the 1st. Created by Glass Joe in Union County.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["cardio","heavy","run"],"equipment":["coupon"],"tags":["competitive","game"]},{"id":"x-diamond-david-lee-roth-burpee","name":"Diamond David Lee Roth Burpee","text":"Burpee with a Diamond Merkin. Instead of just \"Jumping\", do a David Lee Roth scissor kick at the end.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["cardio","lower","upper"],"equipment":[],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-diamond-merkin","name":"Diamond Merkin","text":"A challenging push-up variation where you form a diamond shape with your hands by touching your thumbs and index fingers together directly under your chest. Lower your body until your chest nearly touches your hands, keeping your elbows close to your sides, then press back up to the starting position. This hand placement shifts emphasis to the triceps and inner chest while still engaging the core and shoulders. The narrow hand position makes this significantly more difficult than a standard merkin.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["core","upper"],"equipment":[],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-diego","name":"Diego","text":"(Dora the explorer''s cousin) - Similar to Dora 1, 2, 3 but just tougher... Same partner situation but the exercises are as follows: 100 - Merkins, 150 - Overhead press w/ block, 200 - LBC, 250 - Block Curls, 300 - Squats w/ Block","kind":"thang","emphasis":["core","heavy","lower","upper"],"equipment":["coupon"],"tags":["mary","partner","routine"]},{"id":"x-dips","name":"Dips","text":"Done on elevated surface such as benches, low walls, or even curbs. While in facing upward with hands on surface and legs laying on heels, lower body to work back of arms, shoulders and core.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["core","lower","upper"],"equipment":["bench_wall"],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-dirty-diaper-carry","name":"Dirty Diaper Carry","text":"Hold the coupon in front of you as you would a dirty diaper. Arms straight out in front, grip the coupon with thumb and fingers.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["heavy","upper"],"equipment":["coupon"],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-dirty-harry","name":"Dirty Harry","text":"Crab walk forwards or backwards. Every time a step is taken, stepping leg is extended parallel to ground before being placed back on ground. Best if done over a long distance.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["lower"],"equipment":[],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-dirty-hookup","name":"Dirty Hookup","text":"Performed as 4 count exercise. Pax plank up, facing a wall with eyes on wall. \"1\" Right hand raised to press against the wall, \"2\" Left hand raised to the wall (now in horizontal plank), \"3\" Right hand down to ground, \"4\" Left hand down (back to plank position)","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["core","upper"],"equipment":["bench_wall"],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-dirty-mac-deuce","name":"Dirty Mac Deuce","text":"4 sets of 3 exercises done to 12 4-count reps. Each set has one chest exercise, one leg exercise and one core exercise. After each set of three exercises, you run a lap of a track or whatever else is handy (parking lot, etc.)","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["cardio","core","lower","run","upper"],"equipment":["field"],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-dirty-man-maker","name":"Dirty Man Maker","text":"With a ruck or coupon, perform a man maker. Burpee with squat thruster. Except at bottom, 3 hand release merkins, at the top, 3 squat thrusters. Do not warn PAX you plan to do these, as they may incite a mutiny.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["cardio","heavy","lower","ruck","upper"],"equipment":["coupon","ruck"],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-dive-bombers","name":"Dive Bombers","text":"Dive Bombers Dive Bomber is a Merkin with your hands ahead of your shoulders after you move to down position pull with your arms to move your hands behind your shoulders then push up.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["upper"],"equipment":[],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-dizzy-bear","name":"Dizzy Bear","text":"Dizzy Bear - Perform Bear Crawl while rotating 360 degrees the entire time around a coupon. Q may call out “switch” to have PAX go from clockwise to counter clockwise, or vice versa.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["heavy"],"equipment":["coupon"],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-dmc","name":"DMC","text":"Best on a football field, but can be done with any designated points or posts. From the goal line, Duck Walk to the 10-yard line, 5 Merkins, Reverse Bear Crawl back to the goal line. Repeat to the 20, 30, 40, and 50 yardlines, increasing # of merkins by 5. Duckwalk-Merkin-Reverse Bear Crawl.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["upper"],"equipment":["field"],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-dmx","name":"DMX","text":"Inspired by DMX's \"Ruff Riders' Anthem\" song and the \"stop, drop, ...\" lyrics.\nBest as OYO on grass or turf. No coupon needed. Like a football training camp drill. 1 = 1\nFrom a standing position; drop to the ground laying flat like a burpee on your chest and hands; roll over, get up, chop your feet. Drop to the ground again; roll over the other way, get up, chop your feet. Repeat until desired rep count or time limit.","kind":"thang","emphasis":["cardio","heavy","upper"],"equipment":["coupon","speaker"],"tags":["routine"]},{"id":"x-do-ah-diddy","name":"Do-ah-diddy","text":"Forming a single file formation in Indian run fashion, the PAX begins in a forward mosey pace. The Front Man Peels off performing a set amount of pre-determined movement (Squat, Merkin, Burpee, ect.) and Holds Plank until entirety of PAX has passed him, At which point he falls in rank taking the 6 position and announces LOUD & PROUD \"6\". Front man on hearing the \"6\" call then continues the cycle until the Q is satisfied with the distance covered. Q can increase the \"6\" call from the beginning to shorten the periods between front men dropping. Be sure to not leave anyone behind and always pick up your 6!","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["cardio","core","lower","run","upper"],"equipment":[],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-doc-ock-s-octogon-of-pain","name":"Doc Ock's Octogon of Pain","text":"The PAX partner up & start at different stations. Area is setup with cones in an Octagon - 8 Stations - one for each of the Doc Ock''s 2.0s - Each stations exercise begins with the respective 2.0's first letter of their name. PAX will perform 8 of each exercise, bear crawling from cone to cone after each exercise, after each completion around the Octagon the PAX jog to the middle, to pay respect to my better half and perform Motivator from 4. Station 1 - 2.0 - Decline Merkins; Station 2 - 2.1 - Jump Squats; Station 3 - 2.2 - Burpee; Station 4 - 2.3 - American Hammers; Station 5 - 2.4 - Outlaws; Station 6 - 2.5 - Lt. Dans; Station 7 - 2.6 - The Lion King; Station 8 - 2.7 - Jumping Spiders. Rinse and repeat adding 8 to each exercise each trip around the Octagon of Pain 8, 16, 24, 32... (Motivators continue from 4 each trip to the middle).","kind":"thang","emphasis":["cardio","core","lower","run","upper"],"equipment":["cones"],"tags":["mary","partner","routine"]},{"id":"x-doc-wings","name":"Doc Wings","text":"A killer shoulder \"warm-up\" from Doc out of F3 Twin Cities. All exercises are performed in cadence, without break. PAX should be reminded to keep their arms up after each exercises as rest is not permitted.\n• Moroccan Nightclubs X30 Double Count\n• Arm circles forward X30 DC\n• Air Presses X30 DC\n• Arm circles back X30 DC\n• Grady Corn X30 DC\n• Jack Reachers X30 DC\n• Overhead Claps X30 DC\n• Chinooks X30 DC\n• Pretzels X30 DC\n• Seal Claps X30 DC\n• Raise the Roofs X30 DC","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["cardio","upper"],"equipment":[],"tags":["warmup"]},{"id":"x-dodo-bird","name":"Dodo bird","text":"With two bricks assume the People's Chair, brick in each hand and at rest down your sides is the default position. In cadence or OYO, (1) side shoulder raise [arms straight and lifted to the sides to shoulder height], (2) back to default, (3) front shoulder raise [arms straight and lifted in front of you to shoulder height], (4) back to default. After doing these you''ll find out why the Dodo is extinct. First, never flap your wings in front of you. Second, never try to fly while holding bricks. This can be combined with the Wonder Bra to perform the Wonder Dodo. Follow 1, 2, 3 above, then (4) bring arms in to the chest, (5) shoulder press above your head, (6) bring arms back to the chest, (7) front shoulder raise, (8) back to default described above.","kind":"thang","emphasis":["cardio","upper"],"equipment":[],"tags":["routine"]},{"id":"x-dog","name":"Dog","text":"Hands and knees, as in \"pick up the #Dog\". Yeah, it probably comes from Yoga.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["mobility"],"equipment":[],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-doggie-paddle","name":"Doggie Paddle","text":"Starting position - In Dog (hands and knees). Extend opposite arm and leg at same time. In cadence, 1 - left arm and right leg extend, 2 - return to Dog, 3 - extend right arm left leg, 4 - return to Dog = 1 complete exercise. Good exercise for strengthening lower back and even the buttocks. For those who need more challenging and need to work on balance, extend arm and leg on same side (quickly reminded of your weak side).","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["lower","upper"],"equipment":[],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-dolly","name":"Dolly","text":"Dolly Ab exercise done laying on back, legs raised about six inches from ground. Keeping legs parallel to ground, separate legs outward then return to start.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["core","lower"],"equipment":[],"tags":["mary"]},{"id":"x-dolly-parton","name":"Dolly Parton","text":"Motivators from 9 down to 5! (What did you think it was?)","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["core"],"equipment":[],"tags":["mary"]},{"id":"x-dominos","name":"Dominos","text":"Preferably performed in a parking lot with a row of curbs (can also be done on ground). Line up 1 or 2 PAX per curb down the parking lot, entire PAX side planks on curb with left hand high, starting at one end, first PAX rotates to regular plank position for set number of Merkins, first PAX then holds regular plank and next PAX rotates down for Merkins, and so on down the line. Once the entire PAX is in regular plank position, the entire PAX reverses and starts again with right hand high. Repeato as desired. When done properly the PAX should resemble dominoes slowly toppling over. Best for a larger PAX.","kind":"thang","emphasis":["core","upper"],"equipment":["bench_wall"],"tags":["routine"]},{"id":"x-donkey-kick-offs","name":"Donkey Kick-offs","text":"Before the initial circle of pain, find the nearest wall and do 5 donkey kicks. On the 5th donkey kick hold feet to the wall for 5 seconds. Then up the number to 10 donkey kicks and 10 second hold. Continue adding by 5's until the PAX is dead donkey tired. Great way to start off a workout!","kind":"exercise","emphasis":[],"equipment":["bench_wall"],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-donkey-kicks","name":"Donkey Kicks","text":"While planking near a wall with your feet facing the wall, kick both feet up on wall above your body.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["core"],"equipment":["bench_wall"],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-dora-1-2-3","name":"Dora 1-2-3","text":"Teams of 2 pax working together to reach cumulative exercise goals of 100, 200, and 300 reps. Pax 1 executes as many reps as possible while Pax 2 sprints 100 yards down and back. Flapjack until team goal is reached. Exercises are a top-to-bottom of body progression, i,e, 100 merkins per team (chest), 200 LBCs per team (core), 300 squats per team (legs). Modified Dora 1-2-3 is 50, 100, and 150 reps.","kind":"thang","emphasis":["cardio","core","lower","run","upper"],"equipment":[],"tags":["mary","routine","team"]},{"id":"x-dora-2100","name":"DORA 2100","text":"The Dora 2100 is a routine with 3-4 PAX per team. One PAX at each of two stations, and the third/fourth PAX carries a coupon between stations, rotating through until all of the reps have been completed. The distance should be far enough to allow each PAX to complete around 10% of the reps each round. Should take 20-30 minutes. Station 1 Burpees x100 Merkins x300 LBCs x500 Station 2 Jump Squats x200 Lunges x400 Flutter Kicks (2x1) x600","kind":"thang","emphasis":["cardio","core","heavy","lower","upper"],"equipment":["coupon"],"tags":["mary","routine","team"]},{"id":"x-doracides","name":"Doracides","text":"Dora's twin sister and she is a lil' cray cray. Use the same concept as the regular Dora, 2 PAX work together to reach cumulative exercise goals of 100, 200, 300, and 400 reps. The difference comes in the sprint, instead of running 100 yards you will do suicides instead. 1 PAX member will execute as many reps as possible while PAX 2 sprints to cone 1 (or use a pole, tree, etc. for your point of turnaround), 1 burpee, sprint back to partner, touch, sprint to cone 2, 2 burpees, sprint back to partner, touch, sprint to cone 3, 3 burpees, sprint back, switch with partner. PAX member picks up where PAX member doing the exercises left off.","kind":"thang","emphasis":["cardio","run"],"equipment":["cones"],"tags":["partner","routine"]},{"id":"x-double-applesauce","name":"Double Applesauce","text":"A two-column Indian run.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["cardio","run"],"equipment":[],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-double-merkin-burpee","name":"Double Merkin Burpee","text":"A Burpee with 2 merkins.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["cardio","upper"],"equipment":[],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-double-shot-of-jackies","name":"Double Shot of Jackies","text":"Burpee Variation where after the Merkin, perform a plank Jack (first shot) and after recovery, instead of just jumping, perform a Jumping Jack or SSH (2nd shot)","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["cardio","core","lower","upper"],"equipment":[],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-dr-w","name":"Dr. W","text":"Dr. W is a sufferable 8-count ab exercise that combines Dolly, Rosalita, and the W; often within the 6MOM. Always a #CrowdPleaser. 1 is legs apart like a Low Dolly, 2 is legs together, 3 is raise the legs to Rosalita position (45-60 degrees-ish), 4 is spread ''em, 5 is The W (hands together and stretching forward between your legs), 6 is the return to your back (legs still up), 7 is legs together, 8 is legs down. 5-8 Dr. W's is a good start to get the pax coordinated with the counting. 10 is a magic # that most build up to 15 is just dumb and torture #FetalPositionMaker Qtip '' We always emphasize that the W is on the 5 count. Kinda breaks down the motions and gives a 2nd starting point.","kind":"thang","emphasis":["core","lower","mobility","upper"],"equipment":[],"tags":["mary","routine"]},{"id":"x-dragon-walk","name":"Dragon Walk","text":"Dragon Walk Like the @Peter Parker (and Parker Peter) except you are moving forward. Resembles a Komodo Dragon walking.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":[],"equipment":[],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-dragon-wing","name":"Dragon Wing","text":"A modified @Bat Wings (aka the Martina Special) , where cinder are used in each hand","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["heavy"],"equipment":["coupon"],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-dreadbow","name":"Dreadbow","text":"Rainbows with Coupon over your head, set your difficulty. In wide stance set difficulty, 1 Lean to one side, 2 back to center, 3 lean to other side, 4 back to upright. Beginner on head, Mid held half way up, Advanced full extension.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["heavy"],"equipment":["coupon"],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-drill-instructors","name":"Drill Instructors","text":"On the Q's command, rapidly transition through any combination of standing (\"On your feet!\"), holding 6\" (\"On your six!\"), high plank (\"On your face!\"), and Merkins (\"Down/Up\"). Speed, order, and duration are completely at the Q''s discretion, with the goal being to test the pax's reaction time and/or keep them in an uncomfortable position (esp. 6 inches or down part of Merkin). Inspired by a certain Marine at the Spring 2016 F3 Mud Run and best executed with a gruff, barking orders style. Example: \"On your face! On your six! On your face! On your six! On your feet! On your face! Down! Up! Down! Up! Down! [painful delay] Up!\"","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["cardio","core","run","upper"],"equipment":[],"tags":["mary"]},{"id":"x-dropzone","name":"Dropzone","text":"Similar to @Superman, lie prone on the ground with arms, legs, and head held up as high as possible. But instead of holding your arms out to the side, or forward, they are held up near your shoulders. Like a skydiver in freefall. Hold position to tolerance.\nNamed after the movie, Dropzone.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["lower","upper"],"equipment":[],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-dry-dock-crabs","name":"Dry Dock Crabs","text":"A wrestling drill aka hip heists that needed a cool F3 name. Start in Carolina Dry Dock position and move right foot to approx. location of left hand while moving left hand to former position of right foot then back to dry dock and then other side all while keeping 6 off the ground. Done in cadence.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["core"],"equipment":[],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-dubya","name":"Dubya","text":"Grab the bar for a pull up variation. The first ''up'' is toward your left hand, the second ''up'' is a regular pull up to the middle, the third ''up'' is toward your right hand. Your chin traces a Dubya (W), aye?","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["upper"],"equipment":[],"tags":["competitive","game"]},{"id":"x-duck-and-weave","name":"Duck and Weave","text":"Pax line up as if doing an Indian Run, except this offers more pain. The Pax start duck walking and the six runs to the front by weaving in between each Pax member. Then he joins the rest of the Pax duck walking until everyone has weaved to the front at least once or until the Q's legs burn out.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["cardio","lower","run"],"equipment":[],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-duck-jousting","name":"Duck Jousting","text":"Friendly combat between PAX in the duck walk position. Arms must remain crossing your chest. Bumping, nudging, rubbing and checking are highly encouraged. There is no biting, scratching, standing up or falling over or you are out. Kicking is actually allowed if you are possibly able to remain in the duck walk position on one leg. Last man to remain on his feet in the duck position is declared the winner. Best performed as the final exercise of 6MOM.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["lower","upper"],"equipment":[],"tags":["competitive","game"]},{"id":"x-duck-walk","name":"Duck Walk","text":"Duck Walk The duck walk is an exercise done by squatting and walking slowly, while relying on your hips, quadriceps, hamstrings and gluteal muscles for support.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["lower"],"equipment":[],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-dumbees","name":"Dumbees","text":"Evil distant cousin of the classic burpee. Hold a 15 pound dumbbell in each hand while performing the classic burpee. The dumbells serve as bars for deeper merkins at the bottom and the added weight is a shoulder burner at the top. Any more than 15lbs is cruel and unusual punishment. 10 OYO should cause all mumblechatter to cease immediately due to oxygen depravity. If no dumbbells are available, hand sized rocks work well & add a stability factor.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["cardio","heavy","upper"],"equipment":["weights"],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-dutch-skate","name":"Dutch Skate","text":"Push off explosively on one foot, jump forward ~45° in the opposite direction, and land on the lead foot in a half squat. Immediately pull the trailing foot behind so the shin contacts the landing leg’s calf; keep the trailing foot off the ground. Alternate sides while moving forward, resembling a forward-traveling speed skater. Best performed in single-file.\nCadence options: Q may call cadence on each push-off (“LEFT! RIGHT!”), or use a 4-count rhythm with push-offs on counts 1 and 3 and trailing-leg shin kisses on counts 2 and 4.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["lower"],"equipment":[],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-dwight-howard","name":"Dwight Howard","text":"Dwight Howard Standing facing a wall, jump from rest with both hands and touch as high up on the wall as possible (like Dwight Howard slapping a sticker on the backboard while dunking). AMRAP while your partner circles a building. Normally part of a larger set (people''s chair, rocky balboas, donkey kicks, etc.) of partner work.","kind":"thang","emphasis":["cardio","lower"],"equipment":["bench_wall"],"tags":["partner","routine"]},{"id":"x-dying-birds","name":"Dying Birds","text":"Starting position, Half Squat and hinge at the waist till chest is over knees, hands hanging down. In Cadence, 1 both arms raise straight up to 'I' and bring back down, 2 both arms raise to 'Y' and back down, 3 both arms open out to 'T' and back down, 4 both arms do backwards raise. IYTs in the PT world","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["lower","upper"],"equipment":[],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-dying-cockroach","name":"Dying Cockroach","text":"Dying Cockroach 4-count ab exercise done lying down that involves touching hand to opposite leg, back down, then other hand to opposite leg. Form can vary wildly.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["lower"],"equipment":[],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-e2k","name":"E2K","text":"E2K On your six. Right ankle over the left knee, bring your left elbow to your right knee. Switch. Aka the oblique crunch if you take the right foot and put that on the ground.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["cardio","core"],"equipment":[],"tags":["mary"]},{"id":"x-earl-fonda","name":"Earl Fonda","text":"A combination of the sleeping hillbilly and a jane fonda. You perform the exercise on a 4 count. First count is the upward motion of the jane fonda, second count is the downward motion, but you suspend your leg without touching the ground. The third count is bringing your leg up towards your chest and fourth count is extending the leg. Your leg will not touch the ground until the desired amount of reps are completed.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["lower","upper"],"equipment":[],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-earl-greys","name":"Earl Greys","text":"Another word for squat pump - similar to a move you perform after eliminating a fellow opponent on a first person shooter game. From a standing position, drop down into a deep squat, then move up to a 1/4 Squat, back down to a 3/4 Squat, then back to a standing position.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["lower"],"equipment":[],"tags":["game"]},{"id":"x-el-capitan","name":"El Capitan","text":"El Capitan is a deep walking lunge going up a small hill. The lunge has the back leg straight out behind you, your front leg at 90 degrees or less - both hands go fully on the ground in merkin position on the inside of your front leg. Return to a standing position and repeat the lunge until you reach the top of the hill. Named El Capitan because it looks like you are scaling a sheer rock face.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["lower","upper"],"equipment":[],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-elaine-benes","name":"Elaine Benes","text":"A warm-up exercise, similar to an Arm Circle or a @Moroccan Nightclub , but with Elaine from the sitcom Seinfeld's dance moves. Start with your arms held out on each side and your thumbs pointed upward. Next, move your arms in a figure-eight pattern with your thumbs pointing the way.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["upper"],"equipment":[],"tags":["warmup"]},{"id":"x-electric-chair","name":"Electric Chair","text":"Holding Al Gore, walk in place. Can be in cadence or OYO.\nCredit F3 St. Simons","kind":"exercise","emphasis":[],"equipment":[],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-elephant-walk","name":"Elephant Walk","text":"The walking version of the @Coupon Kettle Bell Swing . Start with performing a Coupon Kettle Bell Swing. Hold the Coupon at the top of the swing above the head and take 3-4 steps then perform another Coupon Kettle Bell Swing. Rinse and repeat for any distance but 200-400 yards of this will gas the PAX. Gloves highly recommended.","kind":"thang","emphasis":["cardio","heavy"],"equipment":["coupon","stairs","swing"],"tags":["routine"]},{"id":"x-elevens","name":"Elevens","text":"An exercise in which you start with 1 rep of one exercise and 10 reps of another exercise, then add one additional rep to the first exercise and subtract one rep from the second. The sum must always add up to 11. Example: Elevens along the oak trees at #45MinutesofMary with Burpees and Merkins starts you with 1 Burpee and 10 Merkins at the first tree, then 2 Burpees and 9 Merkins at the second tree, then 3 and 8 etc. until you do 10 Burpees and 1 Merkin at the last tree.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["cardio","upper"],"equipment":[],"tags":["mary"]},{"id":"x-elf-on-the-shelf","name":"Elf on the Shelf","text":"Elf on the Shelf This exercise is done with one concrete block. Start with the block on the ground beside you. Grab the block and lift it from the ground across your body reaching up as high as you can. Like putting it on a shelf. After a set from right to left then do left to right. Named after some Elf on the Shelf mumble chatter at a workout around Christmas time.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["heavy"],"equipment":["coupon"],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-elizabeth-warren","name":"Elizabeth Warren","text":"Elizabeth Warren Indian Run: while PAX are lunge-walking backwards in a line, the PAX in the front (back) will Bernie Sanders backwards to the back (front) of the line. Upon reaching the end of the line, they will resume lunge-walking backwards and yell 'go' so the next PAX can proceed with his Bernie.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["cardio","lower"],"equipment":[],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-elvis-meets-forrest","name":"Elvis Meets Forrest","text":"Referencing the meeting between \"Elvis\" and \"Forrest Gump\" - alternative to lunges over a distance. Do your best impression of Forrest walking with leg braces and teaching Elvis his patented moves.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["lower","upper"],"equipment":[],"tags":["competitive","game"]},{"id":"x-empty-wheelbarrow","name":"Empty Wheelbarrow","text":"A belly up plank walk with someone holding your feet. Essentially a crabwalk with partner holding feet.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["core","upper"],"equipment":[],"tags":["partner"]},{"id":"x-energizer-bunnies","name":"Energizer Bunnies","text":"Perform a murder bunny, then execute 3 Groiners (Starting from a pushup/merkin position, thrust your feet forward, landing outside of each hand. Thrust backwards to original position) after each \"Hop.\" Distance set by Q.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["upper"],"equipment":[],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-escalator","name":"Escalator","text":"10 jump-ups, 20 burpees, 30 merkins, 40 squats, 50 lunge-walks. Mix and match as long as reps go up by 10. Sometimes followed by a lap around a parking lot.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["cardio","lower","upper"],"equipment":[],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-everest","name":"Everest","text":"Find a set of stairs or a hill. Lunge up one step, perform 1 squat, lunge up with other leg, perform 1 squat, repeato to top. Works best with many steps or sizable hill.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["lower"],"equipment":["stairs"],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-everything-bagel","name":"Everything Bagel","text":"A \"traveling\" series of 4 exercises: a burpee, imperial walker (both legs), lunge walk (both legs), and a broad jump = 1 rep. Best to call out each \"topping\" as you progress down a parking lot. Feel free to add or substitute any of your favorite ingredients to spice things up. Why is this an everything bagel? Because there aren't that many exercises that start with E and everyone loves everything bagels!","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["cardio","lower"],"equipment":[],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-explosive-burpee","name":"Explosive Burpee","text":"Like your traditional burpee - Drop down to do an explosive Merkin, to do another Merkin, jump back up to do a knee tuck jump.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["cardio","lower","upper"],"equipment":[],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-f3-baseball","name":"F3 Baseball","text":"Performed on a baseball diamond or using cones as bases. Pax are divided into four teams. Each team starts at its own base. Teams must complete a cumulative number of reps of different exercise at each base, for example, 120 team merkins at first, 120 team squats at second, 120 team crab cakes at 3rd, 120 team burpees at home, and then move using different modes of transportation to the next base. Each time a team passes the base it started on, it gets a point. Team with the most points after 20 minutes or some other set time wins.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["cardio","lower","upper"],"equipment":["cones"],"tags":["team"]},{"id":"x-failure-to-launch","name":"Failure to Launch","text":"Hold Al Gore while Q counts down from 10. At Lift-Off, explode up into a tuck jump, immediately returning to Al Gore upon landing. Repeat until unable to leave the ground (usually around rep 8 or 9, depending on count speed)","kind":"thang","emphasis":["lower"],"equipment":[],"tags":["routine"]},{"id":"x-fairy-jack","name":"Fairy Jack","text":"Very quick Side Straddle Hop, where your feet only hit the ground in the middle. Usually done OYO.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":[],"equipment":[],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-febreze","name":"Febreze","text":"On your six, do 2 Big Boy Situps. Remain upright after last BB and lift feet up 6\". Do 10 Air Presses. Back down for 4 BB followed by 20 Air Presses with legs held 6\". Repeat using increments of 2:10 ratio. (2:10, 4:20, 6:30, 8:40, 10:50, etc...) (Called \"The Febreze\" because PAX named Febreze always increases the difficulty of a workout and he was the one who decided to hold his feet up 6\" during the Air Presses.)","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["core","lower","upper"],"equipment":[],"tags":["mary"]},{"id":"x-ferkin-aka-fia-merkin","name":"Ferkin (aka FiA Merkin)","text":"Ferkin (aka FiA Merkin) A deviation from the Standard American Push-Up (the Merkin) whereby a PAX, either by design or exhaustion, drops to his knees to perform a Merkin. No shame will be dealt to said PAX as he has at least chosen to keep moving in the face of extreme physical toil and certain mumblechattered mockery.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["upper"],"equipment":[],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-fiddler-crab","name":"Fiddler Crab","text":"Perform a crab walk movement except in a sideways direction.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":[],"equipment":[],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-field-of-dreams","name":"Field of Dreams","text":"Created on a baseball diamond, but can be done in a field with cones. Start out by counting off by fours. 1s start at First Base (1st cone) do AMRAP Squats until relieved. 2s at Second Base (2nd cone) do AMRAP Merkins until relieved. 3s at Third Base (3rd cone) do AMRAP LBC''s until relieved. 4s at Home Plate (4th cone) will perform 15 Burpees then run to First, relieving the Pax there. Continue until all Pax have done the Burpees.","kind":"thang","emphasis":["cardio","core","lower","run","upper"],"equipment":["cones","field"],"tags":["mary","routine"]},{"id":"x-finger-tip-merkin","name":"Finger-tip Merkin","text":"Just like a Merkin or a Knerkin, except you perform these on your finger-tips. Great for grip strength and preparing for obstacle races.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["upper"],"equipment":[],"tags":["competitive","game"]},{"id":"x-finkle-swings","name":"Finkle Swings","text":"Meet the Finkle Swing, named for the infamous kicker ''Ray Finkle'' it is said that this was the stretch that lost him the big game. Pax swings one leg at a time back and forth to warm up those hips.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["lower","mobility","upper"],"equipment":["swing"],"tags":["game","warmup"]},{"id":"x-fire-drill","name":"Fire Drill","text":"PAX in a circle, chopping feet or high knees. Each PAX calls out \"Fire\" all PAX hits the ground rolls right, merkin, roll back left, another merkin, then back up chopping. Go around the circle with the \"stop, drop and roll\" until all PAX have called \"Fire\".","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["cardio","upper"],"equipment":[],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-fireworks","name":"Fireworks","text":"Pax find suitable hill,\nSlosey down, sprint up, at top do one star jump burpee, repeat process adding another rep to the star jump burpee each time…1, 2,3,4 etc typically ending at 10","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["cardio","lower","run"],"equipment":[],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-flamingo-merkins","name":"Flamingo Merkins","text":"Bend at the waist, fingers touching your toes. Walk your hands out to a plank position while keeping one leg raised in the air. Perform a merkin, then walk your hands back, lowering your leg to the ground and touching your toes again. Stand upright and repeat the movement with the other leg for 1 rep. Rinse and repeat. Reps are determined by the Q.","kind":"thang","emphasis":["core","lower","upper"],"equipment":[],"tags":["routine"]},{"id":"x-flat-tire","name":"Flat Tire","text":"Partner 1 gets into wheelbarrow and takes 4 steps then does 1 derkin, takes 8 steps and does 2 derkins. Continue this 1:4 progression until each partner gets to 40:10, switching partners as needed. This gets it name because, you will look like a wheelbarrow with a flat tire.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["upper"],"equipment":["stairs"],"tags":["partner"]},{"id":"x-flip-flops","name":"Flip Flops","text":"In basic terms, the PAX will flip a large tire, then drop down for a burpee. If solo, he will rinse and repeat. In a team, the Flip Flop can be performed like a reverse Indian Run: Flip (flip tire), Flop (burpee), then move to the back of the line, with each man taking a turn.","kind":"thang","emphasis":["cardio"],"equipment":[],"tags":["routine","team"]},{"id":"x-flora-1-2-3","name":"Flora 1-2-3","text":"Flora 1-2-3 Dora''s lazy, mean stepsister. All pax partner up, and grab a coupon, preferably of the 35 lbs CMU size (concrete masonry unit). 100 Merkins - P1 does 10 with feet on coupon. P2 holds plank with feet on his coupon. Flapjack. 200 LBCs - P1 does 20 LBC holding coupon high on chest. P2 holds legs 6\" off ground, and extends arms w/ coupon over chest. Flapjack. 300 Goblet Squats - P1 does 25 goblet squats. P2 lowers to bottom of goblet squat w/ coupon, and holds. Flapjack.","kind":"thang","emphasis":["cardio","core","heavy","lower","upper"],"equipment":["coupon"],"tags":["mary","partner","routine"]},{"id":"x-floyd-mayweather-plank-punch","name":"Floyd Mayweather - Plank Punch","text":"From a basic plank position, raise one hand off the ground and punch across, behind and under the opposite arm, keeping the core stabilized. Complete in cadence and switch to other arm. Add a small dumbbell or brick for an extra challenge. Can also be completed from a Knerkin Plank position.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["core","heavy","upper"],"equipment":["weights"],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-floyd-plank","name":"Floyd Plank","text":"Floyd Plank When smoked, lie on back with both hands behind head and one ankle up on one knee. Loudly complain of exhaustion for optimal results. Named in honor of F3 Churham legend Floyd.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["core","lower"],"equipment":[],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-flutter-kicks","name":"Flutter kicks","text":"Ab exercise done laying on your back. Legs off the ground, alternate kicking legs as if you're swimming. Usually done in cadence.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["core","lower"],"equipment":[],"tags":["mary"]},{"id":"x-flying-nun","name":"Flying Nun","text":"Lunge walk with little baby arm circles","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["lower","upper"],"equipment":[],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-flying-squirrel","name":"Flying Squirrel","text":"Burpee done where the move from standing to pushup skips the raised push-up position. Usually done with arms and legs spread out like name of exercise.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["cardio","lower","upper"],"equipment":[],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-flying-sun-gods-sobriety-style-aka-nancy-kerrigans","name":"Flying sun gods sobriety style (AKA Nancy Kerrigans)","text":"Lean torso forward, raise one leg out to the back, reach arms out to side and do small arm circles. Count in cadence just like sun gods. Forward on one leg, then switch legs and reverse.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["lower","upper"],"equipment":[],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-forest-to-the-sea","name":"Forest to the Sea","text":"Conducted on any field, parking lot or basketball court that has a halfway point. You bear crawl to the middle and crab walk the rest. The bear represents your forest and the the crab is the sea. You can throw some burpees in at the half way point to help countdown (5,4,3,2,1) and to make the exercise harder. The length is up to the Q.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["cardio","upper"],"equipment":["field"],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-fornicola-s","name":"Fornicola’s","text":"Named after a college wrestling national champ and coach. Great for warm-up/COP in cadence. Arms straight out make a tight fist and the thumb placed across the space between 2nd & 3rd knuckles. Snap your fingers all the way out, rinse and repeat. Move to arms extended to side then above the head. Recommend 30 to 50 4-count reps in each position.","kind":"thang","emphasis":["lower","upper"],"equipment":[],"tags":["routine","warmup"]},{"id":"x-four-corners-escalator","name":"Four Corners Escalator","text":"ination of Four Corners and an Escalator. Four exercises. 10 reps, run to next corner, 10 reps+20 reps next exercise, run, 10, 20, 30 reps, run, 10, 20, 30, 40 reps, run to start. Can go back down escalator: 40, 30, 20, 10, run, 30, 20, 10, run, 20, 10, run, 10.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["cardio","run"],"equipment":[],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-foxhole","name":"Foxhole","text":"Foxhole 2 for 1 value exercise! Its a WWI, roll to the side into a Merken. Repeato.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":[],"equipment":[],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-frankenstein-squat","name":"Frankenstein Squat","text":"A @Frankensteins followed immediately by a squat","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["lower"],"equipment":[],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-frankensteins","name":"Frankensteins","text":"Stand with Arms straight out. As you walk forward, raise each leg as high as you can toward corresponding arm. Knees slightly bent. Looks like Frankenstein.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["lower","upper"],"equipment":[],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-freddie-mercury","name":"Freddie Mercury","text":"Aka the bicycle sit-up. Alternate extending legs and arms in a bicycling motion during the sit-up.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["core","lower","upper"],"equipment":[],"tags":["mary"]},{"id":"x-friday-night-lights","name":"Friday Night Lights","text":"5 stations rotating every 4 minutes RB Station At picnic tables 20 each: Dips Step-ups Irkins Mt. Climbers OL Station Using coupon 20 each: Squats Rows Curls Swings DL Station 15 yards moving together One PAX bear crawl One PAX rifle carry coupon Switch DB Station 15 yard run catch One PAX runs backwards One PAX throws the ball when teammate reaches endzone 5 burpee penalty for each dropped ball Switch WR Station 15 yard run catch One PAX runs One PAX throws the ball when teammate reaches endzone 5 burpee penalty for each dropped ball Switch","kind":"thang","emphasis":["cardio","heavy","lower","run","upper"],"equipment":["coupon","swing"],"tags":["routine"]},{"id":"x-frog-squats","name":"Frog Squats","text":"With your hands on a horizontally flat Cindy (coupon), position your body as if you were about to Bear Crawl or Murder Bunny, but stay in place and perform a squat. Higher rep count leads to a burner of a leg exercise!","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["heavy","lower"],"equipment":["coupon"],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-froggies","name":"Froggies","text":"Start in the high plank position with your hands shoulder-width apart. Bring your chest almost to the ground and hold, alternate your right knee to your right elbow and back, then your left knee to your left elbow and back. Push up into high plank, alternate your right knee to your right elbow and back, then your left knee to your left elbow and back. 6-count = 1 rep.\nRinse and repeat...","kind":"thang","emphasis":["core","upper"],"equipment":[],"tags":["routine"]},{"id":"x-gargoyle","name":"Gargoyle","text":"A variation of @Monkey Humpers , which is a half-squat performed while grabbing the inside of your ankles. In this variation, the exercise is performed on a coupon, bench, or any elevated surface.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["heavy","lower"],"equipment":["bench_wall","coupon"],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-gas-pump","name":"Gas Pump","text":"Start in the LBC position and straighten your legs to the Dolly position and then back to the LBC position. Sit next to @Mungo in the Lake Murray region when he does these and you'll know where the name comes from.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["core","lower"],"equipment":[],"tags":["mary"]},{"id":"x-get-low","name":"Get Low","text":"Performed to the song Get Low by DJ Snake, hold the people's chair while the song says Get Low over and over again. When the Beat Drops do squats up and down in Cadence with the beat. The song will repeat and you can either repeat this or you can drop to a low plank. Hold the low point of a merkin while the song says Get Low for what seems like a ridiculously Long Time. When the Beat Drops do merkins, if you can. Good warm up to a ridiculous song","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["core","lower","upper"],"equipment":["speaker"],"tags":["warmup"]},{"id":"x-get-low-or-buried-face","name":"Get Low or Buried Face","text":"Merkin/pushup position, feet are raised onto a bench (2.5ft or higher elevation is preferred). While in pushup position w/feet elevated together, each hand is placed on a cinder-block/brick, allowing push-ups to have a lower range to dip and push back up from. Since the head now parallels the hands, the pectorals get a better stretch, as well as the arms & shoulders, since the head & body now fall below the level of a typical face-to-ground push-up.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["heavy","mobility","upper"],"equipment":["bench_wall","coupon"],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-get-lucky-or-not-so-much","name":"Get Lucky or not so much","text":"Listen to \"Get Lucky\" by Daft Punk, and every time they say \"get lucky\" do a merkin. Every time the song says \"we're up all night\" hold an Al Gore until he says \"get lucky\" again.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["upper"],"equipment":["speaker"],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-glen-campbells","name":"Glen Campbells","text":"Another name for Partner Carries, but Partner Carry is too simplistic a name for a dignified, musically well rounded PAX. 70's Gold. The lyrics and angelic voice say it all.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":[],"equipment":["speaker"],"tags":["partner"]},{"id":"x-global-warming","name":"Global Warming","text":"PAX in circle of pain. Hold Al Gore while slowly shuffling in a circle. Q shouts out exercise and amount (10 merkins, 20 Bobby Hurleys, 10 burpees, etc.) PAX recover and continue Al Gore shuffle in opposite direction. Rinse, repeat, and continue until Q is smoked.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["cardio","upper"],"equipment":[],"tags":["warmup"]},{"id":"x-golden-arches","name":"Golden Arches","text":"Golden Arches is an Ab exercise done lying on your back. Starting with your legs spread apart and off the ground, raise your legs, drawing them toward the center, then down, like you are drawing an 'M'. Then reverse direction. Usually done to a four-count cadence.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["lower"],"equipment":[],"tags":["mary"]},{"id":"x-good-morning-abby","name":"Good Morning Abby","text":"Starting position laying on your back, sit upright at the same time bending your legs and planting your feet then stand upright not using hands for support. Lower back down to a sitting position and extend legs while laying back down to complete one round. Originally called prisoner get ups but we like good morning Abby better.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["core","lower"],"equipment":[],"tags":["mary"]},{"id":"x-good-morning-burpees","name":"Good Morning Burpees","text":"While moseying you must say \"good morning\" to everyone you pass. If they reply \"good morning\" then the pax stop and perform 5 burpees then continue on your way. Bonus points if the person who replies to the pax performs the burpees also.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["cardio"],"equipment":[],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-good-morning-squat","name":"Good Morning Squat","text":"Stand with a coupon in the front rack position, drop down into a low squat, then pivot to a Good Morning by straightening your legs, so your back is horizontal. Next, drop back down into a low squat before standing up again. Rinse and repeat.\nFor better form, stand on something with your heels raised about 2 inches.","kind":"thang","emphasis":["heavy","lower"],"equipment":["coupon"],"tags":["routine"]},{"id":"x-google-bun-shaper","name":"Google Bun Shaper","text":"Walking Lunge and extend back leg at a slight angle to align with the glute muscle fibers. Make sure to squeeze and focus on the glute you are raising.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["lower"],"equipment":[],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-gorilla-complex","name":"Gorilla Complex","text":"With a cinder block or other coupon of Q's choosing, PAX perform the following OYO without stop: 8 Curls For Girls, 8 High Pulls, 8 Overhead Presses, 8 Tricep Extensions, then drop coupon for 8 Merkins. Follow this up by a quick mosey for a brief upper body recovery, typically no more than 50 yards. Rinse and Repeat 8 Times.","kind":"thang","emphasis":["cardio","heavy","upper"],"equipment":["coupon"],"tags":["routine"]},{"id":"x-gorilla-humpers","name":"Gorilla Humpers","text":"Like Monkey Humpers, only bigger! Stand with feet much wider than shoulder width, half-squat performed while grabbing the inside of your ankles. Still gets all of the burn, but it's significantly different than your normal monkey hump.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["lower","upper"],"equipment":[],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-grady-corn","name":"Grady Corn","text":"In memory of Grady Pitstick, aka \"Quikrete\", who passed away a year ago. He was only 30 years old, and the son of another member of the Knoxville PAX, Brian Pitstick, aka \"Sparkler\". \"Grady Corn\" is a a combination of Grady's name and \"Candy Corn\", which was an exercise Grady brought to us that became his trademark. It is a shoulder warm up that can become a full-on exercise with enough reps. Here is its description: Four-count exercise that begins in a standing position with your arms together, straight out in front of you. Swing your arms back to a \"T\" formation, then over your head to form a triangle, then back down to a \"T\", and then back to the starting position. 25 reps makes for a good shoulder warm up. At 50 reps the mumblechatter starts to dwindle. Groans of pain begin at about rep 75, which should be taken by the Q as encouragement to keep going to 100.","kind":"thang","emphasis":["upper"],"equipment":["swing"],"tags":["routine","warmup"]},{"id":"x-grave-diggers","name":"Grave Diggers","text":"Grave Diggers Coupon exercise. Start standing with feet shoulder width apart and straddling a coupon. Bend over and grap coupon and lift it up and over the right shoulder until the coupon is by your right ear. Then return the coupon between your feet. Repeat on left side. This is easily completed as a 4-count exercise.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["heavy","upper"],"equipment":["coupon"],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-green-sally-up","name":"Green Sally Up","text":"Q plays the song \"Flower\" by Moby (Gone in 60 seconds soundtrack). Start with your chest on the ground, and enjoy it because your chest shouldn''t touch the ground again until the song is over. When the song says \"Green Sally Up\" the Pax will be in the ''Merican up position, and \"Green Sally Down\" the Pax will be in the ''Merican down position. Pax will hold the down position until the next rep. It''s only 31 little reps in 3:30. Scale this workout to your fitness level: If you are fatigued, modify the ''mericans by either doing chest to ground at the bottom, or take no shame and use your knees. Here''s a tip to complete it, position hands between shoulders and chest and close to the body, much less stress on the shoulders. This can be modified to about any move; squats, curls, planks or even pull-ups if you are absolutely insane. http://www.youtube.com/watch?v=6A2V9Bu80J4","kind":"thang","emphasis":["core","lower","run","upper"],"equipment":["field","pull_up_bar","speaker"],"tags":["routine"]},{"id":"x-greg-louganis-merkin","name":"Greg Louganis Merkin","text":"From plank position, do a merkin then shoot your legs up and through your arms while flipping over backwards arriving in plank position. Don't hit your head.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["core","lower","upper"],"equipment":[],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-greta-1-2-3","name":"Greta 1-2-3","text":"Dora's Icelandic Cousin...she's frigid. It's like Dora 1-2-3 but performed with each exercise using a 30lb cinderblock (YHC used Kettle bell swings, squat to overhead press, and block burpees) . Also, while one of the pair is running, the runner is carrying another cinderblock to leave at the top of the run for the other to carry back. All the while the runner has to hurdle over three obstacles (hay bales). It's terrible and horrible combined.","kind":"thang","emphasis":["cardio","heavy","lower","run","upper"],"equipment":["coupon","swing"],"tags":["routine"]},{"id":"x-gridiron-gambit","name":"Gridiron Gambit","text":"Groups of 3, random \"points\" (cards) pick up workout competition! Start at the 0 yard line of a football field, group of 3 jogs to the left of the 50 yd line and picks up a random (flipped over) card. They then jog across to the right side of the 50 yd line to the card assignment whiteboard to receive the workout. Next they jog back to the 0 yd and perform the exercise.\nAce Spade: 5 cindy curls altogether\n2 spade: 10 cindy curls altogether\n3 spade: 15 cindy curls altogether\n4 spade: 20 cindy curls altogether\n5 spade: 25 cindy curls altogether\n6 spade: 30 cindy curls altogether\n7 spade: 35 cindy curls altogether\n8 spade: 40 cindy curls altogether\n9 spade: 45 cindy curls altogether\n10 spade: 50 cindy curls altogether\nAce diamonds: 5 cindy swings altogether\n2 diamonds: 10 cindy swings altogether\n3 diamonds: 15 cindy swings altogether\n4 diamonds: 20 cindy swings altogether\n5 diamonds: 25 cindy swings altogether\n6 diamonds: 30 cindy swings altogether\n7 diamonds: 35 cindy swings altogether\n8 diamonds: 40 cindy swings altogether\n9 diamonds: 45 cindy swings altogether\n10 diamonds: 50 cindy swings altogether\nAce hearts: 3 oh press altogether\n2 hearts: 6 oh press altogether\n3 hearts: 9 oh press altogether\n4 hearts: 12 oh press altogether\n5 hearts: 15 oh press altogether\n6 hearts: 18 oh press altogether\n7 hearts: 21 oh press altogether\n8 hearts: 24 oh press altogether\n9 hearts: 27 oh press altogether\n10 hearts: 30 oh press altogether\nAce clubs: 5 yd and back farmers carry each\n2 clubs: 10 yd and back farmers carry each\n3 clubs: 15 yd and back farmers carry each\n4 clubs: 20 yd and back farmers carry each\n5 clubs: 25 yd and back farmers carry each\n6 clubs: 30 yd and back farmers carry each\n7 clubs: 35 yd and back farmers carry each\n8 clubs: 40 yd and back farmers carry each\n9 clubs: 45 yd and back farmers carry each\n10 clubs: 50 yd and back farmers carry each\nAll Jacks: 15 burpees each\nAll queens: 30 yd bear crawl and back each\nAll kings: reward card, no cindy on next exercise\nJokers: Steal a \"point\" (card) from a fast moving team","kind":"thang","emphasis":["cardio","run","upper"],"equipment":["field","swing"],"tags":["competitive","game","routine","team"]},{"id":"x-griff","name":"Griff","text":"Run 800m; Run 400m backwards; Run 800m; Run 400m backwards. Griff is a Crossfit Hero.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["cardio","run"],"equipment":[],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-grip-rip-and-roll-grrs","name":"Grip, Rip, and Roll (GRRs)","text":"Grip, Rip, and Roll (GRRs) Sitting up on your six, set a cinder block by your side. Grip the cinder block. Pick it up and place it on the other side of your body. Now place your hands on top of the cinder block, roll into a plank on top of the block, then roll to the ground. Repeato movements until the PAX start to complain.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["core","heavy"],"equipment":["coupon"],"tags":["mary"]},{"id":"x-grizzcalator","name":"Grizzcalator","text":"Merkins Crawls up the stairs: Ascend the stairs one at a time in plank position. Perform a merkin on each stair.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["core","upper"],"equipment":["stairs"],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-grocery-carry","name":"Grocery Carry","text":"As a mode of travel, use 2 coupons with your wrists through the holes like your arms are full of groceries.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["heavy","upper"],"equipment":["coupon"],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-groiners","name":"Groiners","text":"Starting from a pushup/merkin position, thrust your feet forward, landing outside of each hand. Thrust backwards to original position. Repeato.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["upper"],"equipment":[],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-ground-pounder","name":"Ground Pounder","text":"Starting position - holding large rock up near chest. On 1: Lift Rock over head, On 2: bring rock back to chest, On 3: bring rock down to pound the ground in a deep squat then return to starting position.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["lower","upper"],"equipment":[],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-growing-pains","name":"Growing Pains","text":"An abs routine that consists of three exercises done with iterations of 30 in cadence or on the Q's count, each getting more \"mature.\" Start off with 30 LBCs (preferably 4-count, in cadence), immediately move into 30 Big Boys, then immediately into the Superman position while the Q counts off 30 seconds (can be done in a 4 count with the PAX). Developed for Marvel's 30th Birthday Q.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["core","upper"],"equipment":[],"tags":["mary"]},{"id":"x-guantanamo","name":"Guantanamo","text":"Pax in a circle on their backs heels up. First pax jumps up and pushes the feet down around the circle fighting to keep legs off the ground. Followed by next pax in line then hit the ground legs up when back to your start position until last man finishes the circle.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["lower"],"equipment":[],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-gunji-squat","name":"Gunji Squat","text":"A squat variation where you cross your arms in front of your body and hold your earlobes with opposite hands (right hand to left earlobe, left hand to right earlobe). From this position, perform deep squats by descending as low as you can go while maintaining the earlobe grip, then stand back up. This arm position challenges balance and flexibility while eliminating the ability to use your arms for momentum or counterbalance, making the squat more difficult and emphasizing leg strength and core stability","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["core","lower","mobility","upper"],"equipment":[],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-gunners","name":"Gunners","text":"The PAX completes a set of exercises in succession of the process of the firing of a gun. Hammer, to explosion, to barrel path PAX lines up in a across an open field on their Six. Complete a number of American Hammers and explosive exercise (eg. Burpees, Jump Squats) as set by the Q AYG Sprint to a point set by the Q Repeat Exercise pattern again.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["cardio","core","lower","run"],"equipment":["field"],"tags":["mary"]},{"id":"x-gut-busters","name":"Gut Busters","text":"The Q plays \"Ghostbusters\" by Ray Parker Jr. Everyone starts in and holds a plank for the entire song. Every time \"Ghostbusters\" is said, complete a burpee (21 times total in the song). During the \"I ain't afraid of no ghosts\" sections, do plank jacks in rhythm. Bustin' makes everyone feel good!","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["cardio","core"],"equipment":["speaker"],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-gwerkin","name":"Gwerkin","text":"Modified \"Squerkin.\" Instead of holding partner's legs at side, hold partner's feet together in \"goblet squat\" position, or put partner's feet on your shoulders.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["lower","upper"],"equipment":[],"tags":["partner"]},{"id":"x-hail-mary","name":"Hail Mary","text":"Partner up, near picnic table or other such object. First man planking on ground, second man with his legs on first back doing dips with his hands on picnic table. flapjack after each set.","kind":"thang","emphasis":["cardio","core","lower","upper"],"equipment":["bench_wall"],"tags":["mary","partner","routine"]},{"id":"x-hair-burners","name":"Hair Burners","text":"To push weight plates (10s, 25s, 35s or 45s) across the ground in a parking lot or around a track for a given time or distance. An Area 51 Tiger Rag special.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["heavy","run"],"equipment":["field","weights"],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-hairband-mile","name":"Hairband Mile","text":"A Mental Marathon with an Actual Run or Jogging Distance equal to or less than 1/4 mile. Named in honor of Hairband who claims to hate running but is secretly a closet runner.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["cardio","run"],"equipment":[],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-hairy-rockettes","name":"Hairy Rockettes","text":"Often called the alternating toe touch, PAX will start by standing with feet at shoulder width with arms extended out to sides. With a four count cadence, exercise will start by bringing right foot up to left hand for count 1 with leg kept as straight as possible. Return right foot to ground for count 2, followed by left foot to right hand for count 3. Return left foot to ground to complete count.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["lower","upper"],"equipment":[],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-half-burpee","name":"Half Burpee","text":"From the standing position, drop down into a Merkin. Then, without moving your hands, hop your feet up to your hands and back for the next rep. Perform the next Merkin, then hop your feet up to your hands and back. Rinse and repeat.","kind":"thang","emphasis":["cardio","upper"],"equipment":[],"tags":["routine"]},{"id":"x-hand-release-prisoner-cell-merkin-burpees-aka-hrpcmbs","name":"Hand Release Prisoner Cell Merkin Burpees aka HRPCMBs","text":"Same as PCMBs except the Merkins are replaced with Hand Release Merkins. Drop to Plank, do 1 Hand Release Merkin then bring your right knee in and back, do 1 Hand Release Merkin then bring your left knee in and back, do 1 Hand Release Merkin then bring both feet in and jump up = 1 HRPCMB complete. You think PCMBs are bad? Wait until you try these.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["cardio","core","lower","upper"],"equipment":[],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-hand-release-mike-tysons","name":"Hand-release Mike Tysons","text":"Like a Mike Tyson, with the added pleasure of a hand release. Place your feet against a curb or wall while in a plank position. 1. Contract the legs for a horizontal squat; 2. Extend legs back to plank; 3. Lower upper body to ground; 4. lift hands completely off ground; 5. Push back up to plank position.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["core","lower"],"equipment":["bench_wall"],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-hands-of-time","name":"Hands of Time","text":"Close COP with PAX on their 6's, heads in the center with legs out. (as though forming a clock). Q starts the PAX, legs up at 90 degrees, hands under your rear. One PAX at a time in a wave like motion- Each PAX counts off aloud as they drop and hold 1,2,3, etc around the circle until finished (suggested 60,120,180,240). Drop straightened legs to 10 degrees and hold until a full revolution has been made (as the second hands would move around a clock) then return to 90 degrees and repeat until smoked! Alternate version... MICKEY'S Hands of Time, similar to above but with a partner standing over the PAX on the ground and \"Throwing down\" their legs to the left or right instead or straight forward. Do not let the legs touch the ground during the exercise!","kind":"thang","emphasis":["lower","upper"],"equipment":[],"tags":["partner","routine"]},{"id":"x-hang-clean","name":"Hang Clean","text":"Can be done with coupon or sandbag.\nBend at waist with straight back. Hold coupon so it \"Hangs\" at your knees or slightly below. Then do a full extension & shrug at same time and snap-up to your chest like a \"Clean\".","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["heavy","upper"],"equipment":["coupon","sandbag"],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-hanging-overhead-press-h-o-p","name":"Hanging Overhead Press (H.O.P.)","text":"Curl + Over Head Press (OHP). 4 Count In-Cadence exercise.\nHold coupon from the top handle (or sandbag) in the hanging position with the coupon hanging at your waist.\n1 = Curl\n2= Over Head Press\n3 = Lower Coupon back to chest (top of curl position)\n4 = Lower coupon back to the hanging position at your waist.\nRepeat to desired rep count.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["heavy","upper"],"equipment":["coupon","sandbag"],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-hanging-toe-touch","name":"Hanging Toe Touch","text":"Hanging from monkey bars facing crossways of bars. Normally hanging from a bar in each hand. Swing feet up to touch opposite side of monkey bars.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":[],"equipment":["pull_up_bar","swing"],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-happy-jacks","name":"Happy Jacks","text":"Do 5 side straddle hops in cadence then after the 5th one everyone does two jump squats. Like this... Side Straddle Hops IC: One, two, three, ONE! One, two, three, TWO! One, two, three, THREE! One, two, three, FOUR! One, two, three, FIVE! Quickly followed by two jump squats. Repeat 4x or until no one can breathe.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["lower"],"equipment":[],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-harley-quinn-s","name":"Harley Quinn's","text":"Harley Quinn's, Margot Robbie's character in Suicide Squad, are a spin-off of classic suicides and performed on a football field or any field with set distances or cones. Two exercises are needed each round, Exercise A is performed on yardage that starts with odd number and Exercise B on yardage that starts with even number). Rounds consist of PAX starting on the end line, PAX run to the 10yd line, perform 10 reps of Exercise A, run back to baseline, Run to 20yd line and perform 20 reps of Exercise B, run back to baseline, 30yd= 30reps Ex A and so forth. (Yardage marker equals number of reps performed. Can do this down whole field or to set distance and back. (ie. 10,20,30,40,30,20,10) *For full football field, the opposite goal line = 10reps to ensure even count between the two exercises. Exercises can change after complete set is done. (ie. only going 40yd out and back). Harley Quinn's are best performed with a group!","kind":"thang","emphasis":["cardio","lower","run"],"equipment":["cones","field"],"tags":["routine","team"]},{"id":"x-hash-pipe","name":"Hash Pipe","text":"Purchased 10 iron pipes, 3/4\" x 30\", at Home Depot. Duck taped caps on the end. PAX1 takes a balanced straddle stance over PAX2 who is laying on his back. PAX1 is holding a 36\" iron pipe horizontally at upper thigh height. Arms straight, back arched, similar to a water skiing posture. PAX 2 reaches up and grabs a shoulder-width grip on the pipe and executes a reverse push-up. (Pull-up) After 20 reps you flapjack. We have also used the pipes for resistant curls. PAX1 Curls for the Girls, PAX2 pushes down on pipe.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["cardio","core","upper"],"equipment":["pull_up_bar"],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-hatching-butterfly","name":"Hatching Butterfly","text":"From the seated position place the bottom of your feet together as you would do if performing the butterfly stretch. Raise hands directly over your head, lay back as if performing a WWII sit-up and return to the starting position with hands over your head.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["core","mobility"],"equipment":[],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-head-shoulders-knees-toes","name":"Head, Shoulders, Knees & Toes","text":"Start with coupon on ground in front of you, feet shoulder width apart. 1) Deadlift coupon to thighs 2) Front Lateral Raise coupon, straight arms 3) Pull coupon, laterally, to chest 4) Press coupon overhead 5) Lower coupon behind your head, elbows pointing up 6) Extend coupon back over your head, keep elbows up 7) Lower coupon to chest 8) Extend coupon out laterally from chest, until arms straight 9) Lower coupon to thighs, arms straight 10) Lower coupon to ground, via reverse deadlift. That''s 1 rep. 15'll hurt so make'em do 20! Can be done in a group with a 10-count cadence or OYO. The PAX will never listen to the kid's classic the same again.","kind":"thang","emphasis":["heavy","upper"],"equipment":["coupon"],"tags":["routine"]},{"id":"x-heartbreak-1-2-3s","name":"Heartbreak 1, 2, 3s","text":"Heartbreak 1, 2, 3's are modified Dora 1, 2, 3's with a heartbreaking hill in place of the 100 meter sprint...a la the final soul-crushing hill in the Boston Marathon. Hill should be just steep enough that standing at the bottom looking up is enough to induce heartbreak when making that final run to the top. If you live in the flatlands, a very steep bridge abutment works just as well.","kind":"thang","emphasis":["cardio","run"],"equipment":[],"tags":["routine"]},{"id":"x-heavy-freddies","name":"Heavy Freddies","text":"Freddy Mercuries while holding up a coupon, rock, or ram.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["heavy"],"equipment":["coupon"],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-heel-toe-rocks","name":"Heel Toe Rocks","text":"In the standing position, perform a calf raise followed by a toe raise, IC: 1-calf raise up 2-calf raise down 3-toe raise up 4-toe raise down. Great for a warm-up.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["lower","upper"],"equipment":[],"tags":["warmup"]},{"id":"x-heels-to-heaven","name":"Heels to Heaven","text":"A traditional Mary exercise performed on the back. Begin with heels up at 90 degrees. Count cadence lowering the heels down to 6 inches, then thrust them back up to 90 degrees bringing your 6 off the pavement, thus shooting your heels to heaven.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":[],"equipment":[],"tags":["mary"]},{"id":"x-hernia","name":"Hernia","text":"Hernia The Hernia is a V-Up using a Coupon. Lying flat on your back, stretching arms above your head flat on the ground with coupon. Do a standard V-Up and bring coupon to toes in one motion. Careful to not hit shins. This works the full lower Abs, Lats, and triceps. Named after a Pax mentioned that it was going to cause a hernia!","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["core","heavy","mobility","upper"],"equipment":["coupon"],"tags":["mary"]},{"id":"x-hillbillies","name":"Hillbillies","text":"Hillbillies, hands on head as if you're doing a sit-up. Lift your knee to the side, touching the elbow of the same side. Flapjack.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["cardio","core"],"equipment":[],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-hillbilly-climbers","name":"Hillbilly Climbers","text":"Similar to @Mountain Climbers , but instead of bringing your right knee up to your right elbow and your left knee up to your left elbow, you lower your body into a low push-up position, open your pelvis, and bring your knees around the outside of your elbows. Right knee to the right elbow, and left knee to the left elbow.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["core","upper"],"equipment":[],"tags":["warmup"]},{"id":"x-hillbilly-squats","name":"Hillbilly Squats","text":"Hillbilly Squats Both hands behind your head, elbows out. Legs/feet set as in a sumo-squat ready position (feet slightly wider apart and pointed more outward than a normal LSS ready position). Initiate movement with a deep sumo squat, then transition to a hillbilly walker - after you thrust up you lift one knee up and side crunch the same side elbow down to where they both almost or lightly touch. Then place foot back down and straighten up from the side crunch. That''s one rep. Repeat, alternating L-R sides as you go. Could be called Sumo Hillbilly as well.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["cardio","core","lower"],"equipment":[],"tags":["warmup"]},{"id":"x-hindenburg-blimps","name":"Hindenburg BLIMPS","text":"Modified version of BLIMPS. Done on a field. Perform exercise at corner #1, sprint to corner #2, perform exercise. Sprint to corner #3 perform exercise. Then to corner #4, exercise and then back to corner #1. Plank it up until all have finished. Thats one round. Round 1 - 10 Burpees; Round 2 - 20 Lunges; Round 3 - 30 Imperial Walkers; Round 4- 40 Merkins; Round 5 - 50 Plank Jacks; Round 6 - 60 Squats","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["cardio","core","lower","run","upper"],"equipment":["field"],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-hip-slapper","name":"Hip Slapper","text":"Hands on the ground, feet on the wall, head and justifier facing the wall. Raise one hand and slap same side hip while balancing on other hand. Flapjack.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["cardio"],"equipment":["bench_wall"],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-homer-to-marge-to-mr-burns","name":"Homer to Marge to Mr. Burns","text":"As with much nomenclature in the Lake Norman area just north of Charlotte, we have a nuclear theme for this exercise. The Simpsons also lived within a 10 mile radius of a nuclear power plant where the potassium iodide pills only prolong the inevitable in the case of a meltdown. Homer is laying on your back and holding your feet 6 inches off the ground with your hands under your posterior. We raise our straight legs to vertical, which we call Marge (picture her hairdo) and then lower them on a 4 count to Homer. For an added twist (pun intended), from Marge, with your hands out to the side, lower your legs to the left and turn your head to the right for Mr. Burns (why? because it burns and he worked at the Springfield nuclear plant). Repeat on the other side. This can be done in cadence, slowly, quickly...mix it up!","kind":"thang","emphasis":["lower","run"],"equipment":["field"],"tags":["mary","routine"]},{"id":"x-hot-potato","name":"Hot Potato","text":"Pair up. Face each other. On your bums and lock ankles. Starting man grabs a paver or sandbag, tosses it over the head of his partner, then stays at 45 degrees. Partner catches the weight, falling to his back, touches the ground over his head with the weight , then performs a sit-up motion, tossing the weight back. Starting man performs the sit-up. Hot potato - get rid of that weight! / Perform for 90 seconds or as long as the Q has gas.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["core","heavy"],"equipment":["sandbag","weights"],"tags":["partner"]},{"id":"x-howling-monkeys","name":"Howling Monkeys","text":"In a circle, everyone grabs their ankles in Monkey Humper fashion (or Gorilla Humper, for the fearless) . The first person does ten monkey humpers followed by the next person and so on as in other \"ring of fire\" exercises. Don't let go of the ankles! Depending on the number of PAX, two rounds seems to result in Howling Monkeys. This will definitely not be a crowd pleaser, and it might be better to not be seen by light of day in a public space.","kind":"thang","emphasis":["core","lower","upper"],"equipment":[],"tags":["routine"]},{"id":"x-hrbs","name":"HRBs","text":"Hand-release Burpees, aka Cross-fit Burpee.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["cardio"],"equipment":[],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-hundreds","name":"Hundreds","text":"Exercise position...on your 6. legs straight and at a 45 deg angle off the ground. head and shoulders off ground. arms straight and down by your side with palms facing ground. do quick 6 inch pulses with arms/hands until you reach 100.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["lower","upper"],"equipment":[],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-hurpees","name":"Hurpees","text":"Hand Releasing when going down to do a Burpee. Aka Hand-release burpees or HRRRPPes.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["cardio"],"equipment":[],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-hurricane-hoedown","name":"Hurricane Hoedown","text":"Flutter kick circuit performed in cadence: 7 IC Seated Flutter Kicks with hands raised in Hallelujahs. Move immediately to hands behind you. 7 IC slightly reclined flutterkicks. Move immediately to 7 IC normal flutter kicks. Move immediately to 7 IC LBC Flutter kicks. Rinse and repeat as needed. The real crowd pleaser is to work your way down the cadence ladder 7,6,5...","kind":"thang","emphasis":["core","upper"],"equipment":[],"tags":["mary","routine"]},{"id":"x-hustle-mosey","name":"Hustle Mosey","text":"Sprint @Mosey","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["cardio","run"],"equipment":[],"tags":["warmup"]},{"id":"x-hydraulic-humper","name":"Hydraulic Humper","text":"Added to a monkey humper or gorilla humper to increase the intensity of the burn in the legs. While at the nadir of the humper go down to the right knee, then the left knee, then back up in reverse, then complete the bumper.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["lower"],"equipment":[],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-hydraulic-squat","name":"Hydraulic Squat","text":"Begin by doing a squat, once in the squat position put your right knee on the ground followed by your left knee, next bring your right knee up followed by your left knee then stand up.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["lower"],"equipment":[],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-ihop","name":"IHOP","text":"A single-leg lateral hop where you jump sideways from one foot, land on the other foot, and then immediately jump back.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["lower"],"equipment":[],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-imperial-blockee","name":"Imperial Blockee","text":"Imperial Walker + Blockee. 6 Count exercise. Done with coupon (or sandbag).\nStart in standing position with coupon overhead.\n1 = Raise left knee to parallel while bringing coupon down to knee. Return knee and coupon to starting position.\n2 = Raise left knee to parallel while bringing coupon down to knee. Return knee and coupon to starting position completing Imperial Walker portion.\n3 = Overhead Press\n4 = Lower coupon to chest\n5 = Coupon to ground for start of blockee (\"merkin on coupon\")\n6 = Stand Up & lift coupon to Overhead Press position completing the Blockee.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["heavy","upper"],"equipment":["coupon","sandbag"],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-imperial-blocker","name":"Imperial Blocker","text":"Imperial Walker using a cindy/coupon. The pax starts with the cindy overhead. As the pax brings a knee up to their stomach, he lowers the cindy to the down position of an overhead press with a slight twist toward the knee brought to his stomach. Cindy is returned overhead as his leg returns to the ground. Alternate legs performed in four count cadence.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["heavy","lower","upper"],"equipment":["coupon"],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-imperial-squat-walker","name":"Imperial Squat Walker","text":"Cruel cousin of the Imperial Walker. This 4-count exercise starts with hands clasp on head. Count 1 = a squat. Count 2 = stand up and bring one knee up to the opposite elbow. Count 3 = a squat. Count 4 = stand up, other knee to other elbow. Q should be mindful to count at a pace that allows/encourages a nice, deep squat. Rushing the count produces girly squats.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["lower"],"equipment":[],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-imperial-stormkickers","name":"Imperial Stormkickers","text":"Imperial Stormkickers Starts the same with arms behind the head. Bring the knees up and then extend for a front kick and back down. Then the other leg for a predetermined rep count. Basic front kick to be instructed but nothing too technical.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["lower","upper"],"equipment":[],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-imperial-walker","name":"Imperial Walker","text":"Imperial Walker Standing, hands on head as if you're doing a sit-up. Lift your knee to the opposite arm's elbow. Flapjack.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["cardio","core","upper"],"equipment":[],"tags":["warmup"]},{"id":"x-imperial-walkerjack","name":"Imperial WalkerJack","text":"A cross between an Imperial Walker with a Jack and something you'd see in a Richard Simmons workout video... In a nutshell, it is an Imperial Walker, but when your knee is at the top of the drive toward the opposite elbow, you hop. Then, when both feet touch the ground at the bottom, you hop again. Rinse and repeat with the opposite arm and leg.\nIn cadence, ONE would be the hop at the top of the left-knee drive to the right elbow, TWO would be the hop at the bottom of the left-knee drive, THREE would be the hop at the top of the right-knee drive to the left elbow, and FOUR would be the hop at the bottom of the right-knee drive. Rinse and repeat.","kind":"thang","emphasis":["lower","upper"],"equipment":[],"tags":["routine","warmup"]},{"id":"x-in-the-plank-tonight","name":"In The Plank Tonight","text":"Hold the plank position for the entirety of \"in the air tonight\" by Phil Collins.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["core"],"equipment":[],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-inchworm-blockees","name":"Inchworm Blockees","text":"With a Cindy (coupon) or sandbag, bend at the waist and place the Cindy on the ground a foot or two in front of you. Perform a blockee (a burpee using the Cindy followed by a thruster with the Cindy). Rinse and repeat. The distance is determined by the Q.","kind":"thang","emphasis":["cardio","heavy"],"equipment":["coupon","sandbag"],"tags":["routine"]},{"id":"x-inchworm-merkins","name":"Inchworm Merkins","text":"Start with a standard inch-worm. From a standing position, bend at the hips and place your hands on the ground in front of you. Proceed to walk your hands out until completely stretched out into the plank position. Do a Merkin, then walk your hands back, until you can stand. Lastly, raise your hands into the air. That is one rep.\nThis can be done as a form of transportation by walking your legs forward after the Merkin instead of walking your hands back.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["core","lower","mobility","upper"],"equipment":[],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-inchworm-n-diayes","name":"Inchworm N'Diayes","text":"Proceed with a standard inch-worm but when you get completely stretched out in plank, perform a Makhtar N'Diayes before completing the remainder of the inch-worm. It adds a little extra burn to the core and few extra grunts from the pax!","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["cardio","core","mobility"],"equipment":[],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-indian-bear-crawl","name":"Indian Bear Crawl","text":"Indian Bear Crawl Line up head to toe in plank, guy at the end bear crawls to the front, then the next guy etc. While waiting PAX are doing Merkins.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["core","upper"],"equipment":[],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-indian-crab-walk","name":"Indian Crab Walk","text":"Indian Crab Walk While lined up on your six, the guy in the back crabwalks to the front, then next guy, etc. Guys on 6 are doing LBCs while waiting.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["core"],"equipment":[],"tags":["mary"]},{"id":"x-indian-giver","name":"Indian Giver","text":"PAX in front runs facing forward to ensure safety. Rear PAX, 1 by 1, runs in reverse to front of line. Once in front, lead PAX faces forward. 2nd from front all the way to the back faces rear and continues the run. Repeat until all have completed rotation or for funsies, rinse and repeat.","kind":"thang","emphasis":["cardio","run"],"equipment":[],"tags":["routine"]},{"id":"x-indian-run-11s","name":"Indian Run 11s","text":"Indian Run 11s Standard Elevens with PAX in Indian run formation. All PAX complete 1st exercise together and then run in formation to perform 2nd excercise at next location approximately 400-500 yards apart.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["cardio","run"],"equipment":[],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-individual-medley","name":"Individual Medley","text":"Swimming has the individual medley (IM), swim all 4 strokes in one event. The F3 IM is 4 favorite F3 exercises done for a specific number of reps on a time interval. Exercises are Burpees, Merkins, Flutterkick, SSH. Start with 5 reps of each exercise. 5 Burpees, 5 Merkins, 5 2 count flutter kicks, 5 SSH, start a new set every 1:30, add a rep until you get to 10 of each. If you're fast you get loads of rest. If it takes you 89 seconds to complete the set you have 1 second to recover. When you miss a set, sit that one out and jump in the next number. If the group has beast and beastest pax the beastest guys can start at 8 and go up while the regular beasts of F3 start at 5. Variations, reduce time or go for the highest number you can hold for 10 sets. Swimmers will get this right away...","kind":"thang","emphasis":["cardio","core","lower","mobility","upper"],"equipment":["timer"],"tags":["mary","routine"]},{"id":"x-intentional-thinker","name":"Intentional Thinker","text":"Great for a change from simple 10-count between exercises. Form is critical! Kneel on your right knee with left upper leg parallel to ground and knee joint making a 90 degree angle. Rest left elbow on left knee and rest chin on left fist. Remain stationary as the Q says either \"down\" or \"up\" and count until Q is satisfied. At the next \"rest\" period, rinse and repeat with other leg ... to maintain symmetric training of course.","kind":"thang","emphasis":["lower"],"equipment":[],"tags":["routine"]},{"id":"x-iron-hulk","name":"Iron Hulk","text":"Big brother of Jack Webbs and Jack Jack Webbs. Essentially performing Jack Webbs with a 1:4 ratio of merkin to air press. Your shoulders and chest feel pumped up like Hulk, but the air starts feeling as heavy as Iron Man''s suit.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["upper"],"equipment":[],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-iron-squat","name":"Iron Squat","text":"Squat thruster but with arm movement like iron cross lifting brick or paver from side up to straight across shoulders. In 4 count cadence or oyo. 1: down squat with arms down. 2: arms raised to parallel. 3: arms down. 4: stand from squat.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["lower","upper"],"equipment":[],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-island-hoppers","name":"Island Hoppers","text":"Utilize three concrete planters or similar. Starting from the ground in a plank position, bear crawl up onto the first planter/\"Island\" and continue to bear crawl across the wall to the mid-point of the first planter. Stop and do a predetermined number of Merkins. Continue to the next \"Island,\" and do another set of Merkins. Then proceed to the final \"Island,\" and do another set of Merkins. These planters are of varying heights and widths making your Merkins vary from diamond to regular while challenging you to stay on the walls. Two PAX can start at the same time, thus making the workout truly intense and challenging. Increase or decrease the level of WO by increasing/decreasing the distance on the initial bear crawl before getting on the \"Island\" or by increasing/decreasing the number of Merkins done at each \"Island.\"","kind":"thang","emphasis":["core","upper"],"equipment":["bench_wall"],"tags":["routine"]},{"id":"x-j-los","name":"J-Los","text":"There are two separate definitions. Definition 1: Preparatory position of all 4's (hands & knees), start position is to draw one knee into your chest. Exercise is done to slowish pace 4-count and then repeated for the other leg. First, extend leg straight out to the rear, parallel to spine; second, swing leg out as wide as possible; third, bring leg back to straight behind, parallel with spine; fourth, bring knee back to chest. Enough of these will have abs & glutes feeling the burn. Variation for the bold: do from side plank position. Definition two: From low-plank position, touch right hip to ground, then back to center. Touch left hip to ground, back to center. Down in four-count cadence.","kind":"thang","emphasis":["core","lower","upper"],"equipment":["swing"],"tags":["routine"]},{"id":"x-jabber-walker-squat","name":"Jabber-Walker-Squat","text":"• Standing up, legs shoulder width apart\n• Each arm punches out\n• Then do Imperial Walker\n• Then Squat\ncount 1-2 (punches)\ncount 3-4 (IW)\ncount 5 squat","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["lower","upper"],"equipment":[],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-jack-jack-webbs","name":"Jack Jack Webbs","text":"A Jack Webb with a Plank Jack following the Merkin. Example of a 2 count would be DOWN (Merkin), JACK (Plank Jack), \"ONE\" DOWN (Merkin), JACK (Plank Jack), \"TWO\", then onto your knees for the count of shoulder presses or over the head claps (2 COUNT). Ascending count to 10.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["cardio","core","upper"],"equipment":[],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-jack-knives","name":"Jack Knives","text":"Jack Webbs as usual. Only Difference is Dumbbells are used for the Hallelujah motion.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["heavy"],"equipment":["weights"],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-jack-moses","name":"Jack Moses","text":"The Jack Moses is a cousin to both the Jack Webb and Iron Hulk. Pax circle up for a plank jack and then stand to lock hands (please don't hold hands) for air presses in 1:4 ratio. (May be used to point to leadership lessons from account of Moses' arms becoming tired and those who came along side to hold them up). Or use at next 2nd F. Look smooth as you belly up and order a \"Jack Moses please. Shaken not stirred.\"","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["core","upper"],"equipment":[],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-jackass-burpee-webb","name":"Jackass Burpee Webb","text":"Find a wall. Perform exercise like a Jack Webb but do 1 Burpee to 2 Donkey kicks, if you make it to 10 rounds you are a beast.","kind":"thang","emphasis":["cardio"],"equipment":["bench_wall"],"tags":["routine"]},{"id":"x-jackass-merkin","name":"JackAss Merkin","text":"Perform a merkin straight into a double-leg donkey kick. Rinse. Repeat.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["lower","upper"],"equipment":[],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-jacked-up","name":"Jacked Up","text":"Jacked Up A series of different types of jumping jack exercises performed with a descending count in cadence. A typical Jacked Up routine might go as follows: SSH x 50, Seal Jacks x 40, Plank Jacks x 30, Crossover Squat Jacks (aka Deny Terio) x 20, and Smurf Jacks x 10. Alternatively, the Q can keep the count the same for all exercises.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["cardio","core","lower"],"equipment":[],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-jackees","name":"Jackees","text":"Burpee Variation with SSH at the top instead of just a jump","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["cardio","lower"],"equipment":[],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-jackhammer","name":"Jackhammer","text":"The starting position is the squat position just above 90 degrees (thighs parallel with ground) while keeping the body quiet, jump as quickly as possible with just using the lower body repeat this as many times in the set time (30 seconds suggested)","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["core","lower"],"equipment":[],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-jacob-s-ladder","name":"Jacob's Ladder","text":"Seven times up the hill, with an increasing number of burpees at the top each trip up. See F3 TV.","kind":"thang","emphasis":["cardio"],"equipment":[],"tags":["routine"]},{"id":"x-james-bonds","name":"James Bonds","text":"On your 6 in seated row position (leaning back with legs about 10 inches off the ground) hold your hands in front of you like your holding a gun. Hold for 10 count and then slowly point your finger gun to the right for 10 count. Swing finger gun all the way to the left for 10 count and then back to the middle for hold as long as you want.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["lower","mobility","upper"],"equipment":["swing"],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-jason-bourne-mile","name":"Jason Bourne Mile","text":"A sub-seven minute mile, preferably parkour style. Push yourself and outrun the rest.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["cardio","run"],"equipment":[],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-jim-braddock","name":"Jim Braddock","text":"Jim Braddock Ever see the movie Cinderella Man? This one is named after the heavy weight champion during the Great Depression in the 1930''s who eventually went on to fight in WWII. You start with a WWII sit up, and up top throw a RH hook and a RH uppercut then go back down. Come back up and do the same with the left side. Rinse & repeat to the Q''s desire. Much better flow if you do a RH Hook followed by a LH Uppercut, and then alternate to a LH Hook and RH Uppercut.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["core","heavy","upper"],"equipment":["coupon","weights"],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-jingle-balls","name":"Jingle Balls","text":"From the plank position, move right foot to right hand, back, right foot to left hand, back, left foot to left hand, back, left foot to right band, back.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["core"],"equipment":[],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-joe-derk","name":"Joe Derk","text":"While doing Joe Hendricks, complete a derkin for every step.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":[],"equipment":[],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-joe-hendricks","name":"Joe Hendricks","text":"Backward bear crawl up an incline--the steeper and longer the better. Named after guy who leads free workouts at Red Rocks Amphitheater in Denver.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":[],"equipment":[],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-joe-louis","name":"Joe Louis","text":"4 count exercise starting from a boxers stance (dominant hand side foot leading: right-handers lead with right foot) Count 1: Punch with the dominant hand Count 2: Punch with the non-dominant hand Count 3: Duck down to just above the waist level as if avoiding a punch Count 4: Recover to the boxer stance","kind":"exercise","emphasis":[],"equipment":[],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-johnny-cash","name":"Johnny Cash","text":"Any combination of Ring of Fire exercises. Circle up in plank position or on your 6 for ab exercises. PAX hold plank/six while one man does reps of exercise. When he finishes the next man does reps until all in circle have done it. \"It burns, burns, burns, that Ring of Fire\"","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["core"],"equipment":[],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-johnny-drama","name":"Johnny Drama","text":"Stand with your toes on a stair. One hand on the handrail to the side. Drop your heels below the stair, and then do a calf raise (Technically a Negative Calf Raise). Johnny Drama wanted Calf implants because his calves were not big enough - get them bigger using this. Will smoke the PAX when multiple sets of 25+ are done in workout and folks start running funny.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["cardio","lower","run"],"equipment":["stairs"],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-johnny-roscoes","name":"Johnny Roscoes","text":"Similar to UP and DOWNS but Chop your feet or high knees. On Q's signal you drop to the the dirt and roll over then bounce back up and resume chopping or high knees until Q signals again roll RIGHT or LEFT.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["cardio"],"equipment":[],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-juggernaut","name":"Juggernaut","text":"One PAX straps on a ruck (30 or 45 lb.) and carries two kettlebells (each in one hand; 30 or 45 lb.) while doing lunges to and from a certain point and back (typically 50 yards round trip). 30 lb. kettlebells and ruck weight for the regular Juggernaut; 45 lb. kettlebells for Super Juggernaut. Pax can carry kettlebells as farmer carries or lifted above the head for Ultra Juggernaut status.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["cardio","heavy","lower","ruck","upper"],"equipment":["ruck","weights"],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-juicer","name":"Juicer","text":"All pax come together in a hugging circle, drop to your 6 and lay back. Place right ankle over the left ankle of the person to your right. Lift left ankle while the other pax applies downward force with their right. Straight count as along as the Q calls it, then switch ankles and repeat.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":[],"equipment":[],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-jump-squat","name":"Jump Squat","text":"An explosive plyometric exercise that combines a squat with a vertical jump. Start in a standing position, lower into a squat with your thighs parallel to the ground or slightly below, then explosively drive through your heels and jump as high as possible. Land softly with bent knees, absorbing the impact, and immediately descend into the next squat. This high-intensity movement builds explosive leg power, cardiovascular endurance, and overall athleticism while working the quads, glutes, hamstrings, and calves.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["core","lower"],"equipment":[],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-jump-squat-holds","name":"Jump Squat Holds","text":"As a group, perform jump squats counting down from 10 to 1. Then hold an Al Gore counting down from 10 to 1. Repeat starting at 9 then 8, etc... Surprise the group by holding the last Al Gore for 10 seconds. Its sure to bring out the mumbles.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["lower"],"equipment":[],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-jump-ups","name":"Jump Ups","text":"On a low wall, jump with both feet from ground up on the wall and back to the ground. Usually done as a ladder along with another exercise.","kind":"thang","emphasis":["lower"],"equipment":["bench_wall"],"tags":["routine"]},{"id":"x-jumping-jack-burpee-flash","name":"Jumping Jack Burpee Flash","text":"Start with 10 jumpin jacks (Side Straddle Hops) then quickly follow with 10 burpees. AMRAP. If doing 4 or more sets can break it in half and do 20 LBCs.","kind":"thang","emphasis":["cardio","core","lower"],"equipment":[],"tags":["mary","routine"]},{"id":"x-jumping-jack-burpee-flash-pull-ups","name":"Jumping Jack Burpee Flash Pull-ups","text":"Not a very creative name, but basically, I took the Jumping Jack Burpee Flash, and modified it to: Start with 20 Side Straddle Hops, quickly follow with 10 burps, quickly follow with 10 pull-ups. Rinse and Repeat. 20 LBCs. Start over and rinse and repeat whole series as many times as wanted or AMRAP it on the clock.","kind":"thang","emphasis":["cardio","core","lower","upper"],"equipment":["pull_up_bar"],"tags":["mary","routine"]},{"id":"x-jumping-spider","name":"Jumping Spider","text":"Plyometric merkin. Merkin with a bounce on the up (getting feet & hands off the ground.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["lower","upper"],"equipment":[],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-jungle-boy-squat","name":"Jungle Boy Squat","text":"Jungle Boy Squat: Stand, touch knuckles to the ground on the down, jump and lift hands above shoulders on the up.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["lower","upper"],"equipment":[],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-killer-bees","name":"Killer Bees","text":"The Killer B's are Bear Crawl, Broad Jump, and Burpees. PAX Bear crawl roughly 100ft or distance specified by Q, then Broad jump back to start, every 5 broad jumps, PAX performs 3 Burpees. Specified # of Sets or timed AMRAP works well.","kind":"thang","emphasis":["cardio","lower"],"equipment":[],"tags":["routine"]},{"id":"x-killer-roos","name":"Killer Roos","text":"Perform broad jumps while holding a Cindy (coupon), also known as ''Joey in the Pouch.''","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["heavy","lower"],"equipment":["coupon"],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-king-arthur","name":"King Arthur","text":"A form of non-running mosey in which one pretends to ride one's horse in a Kingly fashion, while \"Patsy\" bags two halves of a coconut together, providing hoofbeats for cadence. Requires two halves of a coconut and a volunteer to be \"Patsy\". Proper form, and proper mount/dismount adds veracity. See Monty Python and the Holy Grail for example. Not sure if should be an exercise, or just added to Lexicon......does work the shins, however...","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["cardio","run"],"equipment":[],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-king-louie","name":"King Louie","text":"The King Louie is a 1:4 routine that consists of a Burpee followed by four Jungle Boy Squats. Ascending count to 10:40.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["cardio","lower"],"equipment":[],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-king-of-hearts","name":"King of Hearts","text":"Series of suicides of varying variety (e.g, regular, karaoke suicides. Backward run suicides.)","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["cardio","run"],"equipment":[],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-knockout-of-death","name":"Knockout of Death","text":"Performed on a basketball court with two basketballs. PAX line up behind two shooters from the free throw line or 3-point line (Q''s choice). P1 shoots and, if made, hustles to get the rebound to pass to P3. Once P1 shoots, P2 shoots his shot. If P1 misses, the objective is for P2 to make their shot before P1, resulting in a \"Knockout.\" If P1 makes, P2 misses, and P3 makes, then P1 is safe and goes to the end of the line, P2 is \"knocked out,\" and P3 is safe to get back in line. Anyone knocked out must draw a card from the Deck of Death and perform the exercises + indicated number of reps or distance before being allowed back in the game. The winning PAX is the last man standing, ready to shoot, and NOT performing an exercise.","kind":"thang","emphasis":["upper"],"equipment":[],"tags":["game","routine"]},{"id":"x-kobe","name":"Kobe","text":"A core-intensive 4-count exercise performed while sitting on your six (glutes) doing flutter kicks or scissor kicks. Hold a medicine ball (or coupon) and pass it from hand to hand between your legs in rhythm with your kicks. As one leg rises, pass the ball under that leg to the opposite hand, then switch as the other leg comes up. This coordination challenge works your abs, hip flexors, and obliques while elevating your heart rate. Named after basketball legend Kobe Bryant, this movement demands focus, core strength, and cardiovascular endurance","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["core","heavy","lower"],"equipment":["coupon"],"tags":["mary"]},{"id":"x-kraken-burpee","name":"Kraken Burpee","text":"A Burpee that is performed with 3 hand-release Merkins at the bottom... As in \"Release the Kraken\". Originated in Lake Wylie (hence the nautical theme), hated by all.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["cardio","upper"],"equipment":[],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-kristi-yamaguchi","name":"Kristi Yamaguchi","text":"In honor of America’s great figure skating Olympic Champion, this burpee has four parts to make one coup de grâce burpee to please all:\n• Burpee, instead of just a hop, spin 360\n• Burpee again, instead of hop do a skater hop to the right\n• Burpee again, repeat the 360 in reverse spin\n• Burpee a last time, and do a skater hop to the left, back to the start\nYou have completed one ultimate Kristi Yamaguchi burpee! Do more…","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["cardio"],"equipment":[],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-kurpee","name":"Kurpee","text":"It's like a burpee and a traditional kettle bell turkish getup had a love child. Starting with the bell in one hand by your side, drop down for a merkin (one hand raised up on the bell). When coming up instead of jumping and clapping push the kettle bell to an overhead lock out. Bring it back down to your waist and switch hands - that's 1.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["cardio","lower","upper"],"equipment":[],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-la-la-leggy","name":"La La Leggy","text":"This consists of doing squats, lunges (both legs), drop lunges (both legs), squat jumps, and calf raises repeated one after the other usually 20 reps each with no rest. A good finisher to a workout.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["lower"],"equipment":[],"tags":["finisher"]},{"id":"x-ladder-jacks","name":"Ladder Jacks","text":"Two jacks each of side straddle hop, seal jack, smurf jack, plank jack, and bow jack. Down and back up is one rep.","kind":"thang","emphasis":["core"],"equipment":[],"tags":["routine"]},{"id":"x-laney-lu-plank-and-merk","name":"Laney Lu Plank and Merk","text":"From your six, get in the V-up (Laney Lu) position....hold 10x IC, then roll right or left to low plank, hold 10x IC, then perform 1x merkin. Thats 1 Laney Lu Plank and Merk. After merkin, back to Laney Lu hold. Repeato 5x for a burn....10x for a man burn. (cred to RepoMan on the Laney Lu, his 2.0 showed him the V-up move).","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["core","upper"],"equipment":[],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-lazy-clogger","name":"Lazy Clogger","text":"Starting position: lay on your back, feet planted flat below your knees, elevate your hips.\nIn cadence, step out each foot to the back of the heel, fully extending the leg but keeping your butt and legs off the ground, then return each foot back to flat under the knees.\nShould be done slowly and for high rips to target the hamstrings","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["lower"],"equipment":[],"tags":["mary"]},{"id":"x-lazy-doras","name":"Lazy Doras","text":"An estranged and despised relative of Dora 1-2-3. Partner up. Partners perform 100 Merkins, 200 LBCs, & 300 Squats as a team. Here''s the catch, no running. P1 starts with 10 Merkins while P2 planks, then switch. Continue switching between Merkins and plank until 100 total Merkins are reached. Next, while P1 does 20 LBCs, P2 performs a 6\" leg hold until P1 is finished, then switches. Continue switching until all 200 LBCs are completed. Finally, P1 does 25 squats while P2 does squat hold, then switch. Continue switching until 300 total squats are completed.","kind":"thang","emphasis":["cardio","core","lower","run","upper"],"equipment":[],"tags":["mary","partner","routine","team"]},{"id":"x-lazy-susan","name":"Lazy Susan","text":"Declined merkin position with feet on coupon. Perform one merkin, hand-walk one span clockwise, repeat. One full rotation around the coupon = 1 Lazy Susan (~20 merkins)","kind":"thang","emphasis":["heavy","upper"],"equipment":["coupon"],"tags":["routine"]},{"id":"x-lbcc-s","name":"LBCC's","text":"Little Baby Coupon Crunches — Start on your six with coupon on chest. Crunch up, press coupon up/down, crunch down.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["cardio","core","heavy","upper"],"equipment":["coupon"],"tags":["mary"]},{"id":"x-lbcs","name":"LBCs","text":"The \"Lil Baby Crunch.\" Aka a crunch/sit-up.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["cardio","core"],"equipment":[],"tags":["mary"]},{"id":"x-lbfcs","name":"LBFCs","text":"Little Baby Flutter Crunch. On your 6, feet do flutter kick while upper body does crunch. Ignore number of times your legs move, only count crunches.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["cardio","core","lower"],"equipment":[],"tags":["mary"]},{"id":"x-leeroy-jenkins","name":"Leeroy Jenkins","text":"Leeroy Jenkins is gaming slang for a person or thing that causes everything to go wrong for everyone else, usually in some extraordinary fashion. Whatever the PAX are doing, no matter the routine, someone can call out \"LEEROY JENKINS\" and PAX must quickly line up for a sprint (around 80-100 yds marked by cones or on a football field) and finish with 5 burpees. ***For a group of more than 10 PAX - Once you call it, you cannot call it again lest you get the penalty of x2 Leeroy's.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["cardio","run"],"equipment":["cones","field"],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-leg-wrecker","name":"Leg Wrecker","text":"Split pax into 2 groups. Separate groups at a distance as determined by Q (20-25 yards is a start). Group 1 does Lt. Dan's until they reach Group 2. Group 2 holds Al Gore. Upon arrival, Group 1 holds Al Gore while Group 2 Lt. Dan's back. Rinse and Repeat with Sumo Squats (and/or other leg exercises) instead of Lt. Dan''s.","kind":"thang","emphasis":["cardio","lower"],"equipment":[],"tags":["routine"]},{"id":"x-lemur-jump","name":"Lemur Jump","text":"An explosive, full-body traveling exercise that combines a burpee-like movement with a broad jump. Start in a standing position, drop down into a high-plank position, then explosively perform a triple extension (ankles, knees, and hips) while throwing your hands overhead and broad-jumping forward as far as possible. Land in a controlled athletic stance and repeat. This high-intensity movement builds explosive power, cardiovascular endurance, and covers ground quickly, making it an effective and challenging mode of transportation during workouts","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["cardio","core","lower","upper"],"equipment":[],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-lfg-warmup","name":"LFG Warmup","text":"LFG - Warmup\n1 minute each exercise:\n• Hops\n• 2 arm waves\n• Single Arm Swings\n• Bent-Over Trunk Twists\n• Twist Dead Arms\n• Golf Swings\n• Marches with knee taps\n• Ballet Squats\n• Horse Stance with easy sway\n• Upper Body Taps\n• Lower Body Taps\n• Face Taps","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["cardio","lower","upper"],"equipment":["swing"],"tags":["warmup"]},{"id":"x-lieutenant-dan-s-magic-legs","name":"Lieutenant Dan's Magic Legs","text":"Similar to @Lt. Dans , but with a coupon. Lieutenant Dan's Magic Legs is a coupon lunge-walk, left leg, right leg, left leg, into a Thruster. Rinse and repeat. Each lunge should have the knee touch the grass and lock at the top. For the Thruster, the legs go down to 90° or lower with full extension, and the arms at the top.\nExclude the coupon to modify down.\nFrom IPC 2024 - Week 2","kind":"thang","emphasis":["heavy","lower","upper"],"equipment":["coupon"],"tags":["routine"]},{"id":"x-lindsays-aka-forties","name":"Lindsays aka Forties","text":"Lindsays are a high-rep variation of Elevens. You start with 30 reps of one exercise and 10 reps of another exercise OYO, then subtract 5 reps from the first exercise and add five reps from the second. Repeat OYO until you have 10 reps of the first exercise and 30 reps of the second. The sum must always add up to 40. Example: Lindsays with Dips and Merkins starts you with 30 Dips and 10 Merkins, then 25 Dips and 15 Merkins, then 20 Dips and 20 Merkins, then 15 Dips and 25 Merkins, then 10 Dips and 30 Merkins.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["upper"],"equipment":[],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-little-merkin-boy","name":"Little Merkin Boy","text":"Play the Christmas song Little Drummer Boy by Bing Crosby. Hold plank and complete one Merkin every time you here \"Pa rum pum pum pum\". That is 3 minutes of plank and 21 Merkins. This is a great way to finish a Beatdown during the Christmas season.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["core","upper"],"equipment":["speaker"],"tags":["finisher"]},{"id":"x-little-mermaid","name":"Little Mermaid","text":"Lay on one side, one arm goes on the back of your head and the other on the ground. Keep your legs together since we are mermaids and do a sideways sit-up where your elbow gets to your knees.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["core","lower","upper"],"equipment":[],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-ll-cool-j","name":"LL Cool J","text":"Pax performs Alternating Lunges (R-L), then a standard Burpee & finish with a Jump Squat = LL Cool J. The \"Cool\" part is the burpee.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["cardio","lower"],"equipment":[],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-lochness-latte-merkins","name":"Lochness \"Latte\" Merkins","text":"Best used with bleachers or stairs. Can use picnic table as well. 4 Count exercise. 1 rep = 4 total Irkins/Merkins.\nStart in Irkin position on 1st bleacher step. Do 1 Irkin, reach for 2nd bleacher step for 1 Irkin. Move back to 1st bleacher step for 1 Irkin and down to flat ground for 1 Merkin to complete 1 full rep. Move back to 1st bleacher step and repeat until desired rep count.","kind":"thang","emphasis":["upper"],"equipment":["bench_wall","stairs"],"tags":["routine"]},{"id":"x-london-bridge","name":"London Bridge","text":"Starting position is plank with your head at the base of a wall. In Cadence move one hand up to the wall, then the other hand to the wall (so your balanced against the wall with both hands) then move one hand to the ground and the other hand to the ground.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["core"],"equipment":["bench_wall"],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-long-elevens","name":"Long Elevens","text":"Elevens but with a very long travel distance.\nAt each end have two exercises or a combo exercise (have done coupon squat with curl, shoulder tap merkins, tappy gilmores, etc for combo exercises)","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["heavy","lower","upper"],"equipment":["coupon"],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-lounge-act","name":"Lounge Act","text":"Lounge Act: Lie on your side, with your top leg bent, knee-high and facing up, and your foot on the ground; lift your lower leg off the ground. Switch sides to lift the other leg, too. Recommended Reps: 20 each side (XX, of course)\nWhile propped up on one arm, casually posing, like Derek Zoolander’s dramatic male-model pose is a natural fit. Lean into it: “Hit that Blue Steel while you’re lifting the bottom leg”, and “Channel your inner male model… and raise that leg”","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["lower","upper"],"equipment":[],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-low-country-crab","name":"Low Country Crab","text":"From the crab position (hands and feet, face up, back and bum off the ground), in cadence right hand up to touch left foot up, left hand up to touch right foot up. Repeat. Credit to Homeboy (I think).","kind":"exercise","emphasis":[],"equipment":[],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-low-country-crap-boil","name":"Low Country Crap Boil","text":"Similar to Low Country Crab but with one arm dips (again with fingers pointing forward). Starting in crab position, grab left foot with right hand and hold (1), while holding foot dip using left arm (2), press back up (3), release back to crab (4). Repeat, alternating left hand grabbing/holding right foot.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["upper"],"equipment":[],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-lt-danger","name":"Lt. Danger","text":"Lt. Dans plus a merkin. The sequence goes lunge-lunge-squat-merkin.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["lower","upper"],"equipment":[],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-lt-dans","name":"Lt. Dans","text":"A Squat and 2 Single-leg Lunge combination in ascending rep counts of each, usually up to 10. From Forrest Gump, Lt. Dan \"ain't got no legs.\"","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["lower"],"equipment":[],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-lt-get-ups","name":"Lt. Get-ups","text":"Perform two leg lunges forward followed by a prisoner get up. Perfect for crossing a field with a Pax. Sort of a mashup of Lt. Dans and Prisoner Get ups. Often greeted with, ''what the heck''?","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["lower"],"equipment":["field"],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-luge","name":"Luge","text":"From flat on your back, raise both your head and upper back and feet off the ground. From here, bring your knees and chest together, then return to the starting position.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["upper"],"equipment":[],"tags":["mary"]},{"id":"x-lunge-worm","name":"Lunge Worm","text":"Lunge Walk with each leg, then do an inch worm with two Merkins at the bottom before inching back up. When returning to standing position from the inch worm, repeat the full movement until the destination is reached.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["lower","upper"],"equipment":[],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-m-e-r-c-y-high-fives","name":"M.E.R.C.Y. High Fives","text":"Done with FIVE stations at the bottom of a hill. The hill climb and distance is your challenge. PAX must complete each station's circuit at the top of the hill before moving to the next. All stations (except the C-Crawl Station) have a WO at the top of the hill which start with 1 Rep and ascend up to 5 Reps before that station's circuit is complete. Station 1 - M - Manmakers (w coupon such as a Dead Seal or Cinderblock) - (Alternate for this is Merkins w/out coupon and must complete the 1-5 Reps at the Top AND Bottom of the hill) Station 2 - E - Elf on the Shelf (w coupon such as a rolled-up section of fire hose or Cenderblock) Station 3 - R - Rock-a-Bye Babies (w coupon such as sledge hammer or Ruck Sack) Station 4 - C - Crawl (aka Bear Crawl) (w coupon such as a high-rise section of fire hose or a Ruck Sack) Station 5 - Y - Yoke Walk (w coupon such as a section of flat-lay fire-hose or a Deal Seal) At the top of the hill, complete the required number of ascending Squats Lord Have MERCY on your muscles after you climb HIGH up the hill FIVE times for FIVE sets.","kind":"thang","emphasis":["core","heavy","lower","ruck","upper"],"equipment":["coupon","ruck"],"tags":["routine"]},{"id":"x-mabata","name":"MABAta","text":"The MABAta is a simple EMOM routine for those times when you need to get your MABA Burpees in for the day... Whether you've got 60 minutes or just 5. Set your timer and go.\nDo 5 Burpees, then do an alternate exercise for the remainder of the minute.\n20 minutes = 100 Burpees\nWe generally like to cycle through warm-up exercises that allow you to catch your breath, like Imperial Walkers, Squats or Lunges, and BBSU.","kind":"thang","emphasis":["cardio","lower","upper"],"equipment":["timer"],"tags":["routine","warmup"]},{"id":"x-makhtar-n-diayes","name":"Makhtar N'Diayes","text":"Makhtar N''Diayes From plank position, a 4-count exercise in which you put each elbow to the ground and then back into regular plank. Named for late ''90s Sengalese basketball player at UNC notorious for his elbows. Pronunciation: MAC-tar JIE - rhymes with \"sky\".","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["core"],"equipment":[],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-manatee","name":"Manatee","text":"While in the default Superman position, with left hand twist left and back to grab right foot, return to default, then take right hand and twist right and back to grab left foot. Bend at the knee as needed. A nice stretch on that lower back while working your core. If you were in the water you'd probably look as pretty as a Manatee, sometimes referred to as The Sea Cow.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["core","mobility"],"equipment":[],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-manmaker","name":"Manmaker","text":"Dumbell Merkin followed by right arm and left arm rows. Jump feet in then bring the weights up to shoulders while squatting. Similar to a dead lift. When coming out the squat shoulder press at the top.)","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["heavy","lower","upper"],"equipment":["weights"],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-manmaker-burpee","name":"Manmaker Burpee","text":"Burpee with a coupon","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["cardio","heavy"],"equipment":["coupon"],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-manmaker-merkin","name":"Manmaker Merkin","text":"High plank with coupon (cinders are great) laying to your right side. Perform a Merkin. Reach under your body with your left hand and drag the coupon to the opposite side of your body. Flap Jack. Repeato.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["cardio","core","heavy","upper"],"equipment":["coupon"],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-mario","name":"Mario","text":"Double Box jumps on picnic tables (or stairs)... Jump to seat, jump to tabletop, stand up, walk down. Named Marios for what we think are obvious reasons.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["lower"],"equipment":["stairs"],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-marionettes","name":"Marionettes","text":"Starting on your six laying flat. Big Boy Sit Up and touch the ground to the left of your legs then return to starting position laying flat. Big Boy Sit Up and touch the ground between your legs then return to starting position laying flat. Big Boy Sit Up and touch the ground to the right of your legs then return to starting position laying flat. This is a 3 count exercise best done OYO so you can embrace the mumble chatter.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["core","lower"],"equipment":[],"tags":["competitive","game","mary"]},{"id":"x-mary-in-the-middle","name":"Mary In The Middle","text":"A workout routine, loosely based on an ELEVEN, where you perform 1 rep of one exercise at one location, and 10 reps of another exercise at another location. But with this routine, you add a 'Mary' exercise in the middle.\nExample:\nPoint A:\n10 Thrusters\nPoint B:\n1 Burpee\nPerform 5 Big Boy SitUps every time you cross the middle between point A and point B.\nRinse and Repeat... Adding one Burpee, removing one Thruster.\nAlso works well with Twenty-One or a typical ladder.","kind":"thang","emphasis":["cardio","core"],"equipment":[],"tags":["mary","routine"]},{"id":"x-matt-biondi","name":"Matt Biondi","text":"Standing, legs shoulder width apart, arms down. Rotate arms in opposite directions (arms straight) so that they are synced to be by your side and above your head in rotation. Popular shoulder warm up for swimmers, thus Matt Biondi ( famous US Olympic swimmer).","kind":"thang","emphasis":["lower","upper"],"equipment":[],"tags":["routine","warmup"]},{"id":"x-mayhem-merkin","name":"Mayhem Merkin","text":"This is a 10-count exercise. Start in the plank position. Hip slap, shoulder tap, merkin. 1-2 right hip, 3-4 left hip, 5-6 left shoulder, 7-8 right shoulder, 9-10 merkin. Normally do 10-15 in cadence. Can also perform as part of 11s, route 66 or other.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["cardio","core","upper"],"equipment":[],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-mcduck","name":"McDuck","text":"Named after the one and only Scrooge McDuck F3 Denver and his love for the calf raises we give you the McDuck. 1 McDuck is 100 calf raises. Sprinkle in McDucks throughout your workout.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["lower"],"equipment":[],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-mcfly-run","name":"McFly Run","text":"Partners run around a loop ( track, parking lot etc…) one runs forward in one direction, the other runs backwards in the opposite direction. Where they meet the forward runner tags the backward runner and then runs backwards, back in the direction he came from. The partner who was running backward initially now runs forward, back in the direction he came from.\nRinse and repeat as desired","kind":"thang","emphasis":["cardio","run"],"equipment":["field"],"tags":["partner","routine"]},{"id":"x-mega-man","name":"Mega Man","text":"Done to the Mega Man video game theme song, approximately 4 minutes. Routine starts with 4 full squats... on last squat, stay in low squat position drop to hand and then push your self back into squat position (Squat Merkin) x 4. Once squat merkins are completed, from low squat jump up and complete high knee tuck touch jumps x 4 reps. Repeato until song is complete. Everyone knows Mega Man has mad hops!","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["lower","upper"],"equipment":["speaker"],"tags":["game"]},{"id":"x-men-makers","name":"Men Makers","text":"Have 2 - 15 pound weights. Do a Merkin. Up into a Burpee. Down into a Merkin. Bear Crawl 5 steps with weights. Rinse and Repeat UNTIL YOU have completed 5 Burpees. Other PAX may Bear Crawl or Lunge, but not to pass the Man who is with the weights","kind":"thang","emphasis":["cardio","heavy","lower","upper"],"equipment":["stairs","weights"],"tags":["routine"]},{"id":"x-merkin","name":"Merkin","text":"a pushup","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["upper"],"equipment":[],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-merkin-jack","name":"Merkin Jack","text":"Just as the name suggests. This is a merkin with a plank Jack at the bottom of the merkin. It is done on a 4 count. Down on 1 / Legs out on 2 (while in the bottom of the merkin) / Legs in on 3 / Up on 4","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["core","lower","upper"],"equipment":[],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-merkin-jax","name":"Merkin Jax","text":"Merkin Jax Much like Captain Thor, this routine follows a 1:4 ratio. Exercises are Merkins and plank Jacks. Routine: 1 Merkin. 4 plank Jacks. 2 Merkins. 8 plank jacks. Up to 5/20 and back down the mountain.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["core","upper"],"equipment":[],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-merkin-ladder","name":"Merkin Ladder","text":"Find a launch point and target point to sprint to. 50 yards or more. Start with 20 merkin. Sprint to target point. 19 merkin. Sprint back to launch point. 18 merkin. Continue decreasing merkin count down to 1 merkin. Total of 210 merkin.","kind":"thang","emphasis":["cardio","run","upper"],"equipment":[],"tags":["routine"]},{"id":"x-merkin-mania","name":"Merkin Mania","text":"Do all exercises without rest OYO: 5 Diamond Merkins, 5 Merkins, 5 Wide Arm Merkins, 5 Crucible Merkins, 5 Staggered Merkins 1 way, 5 Staggered Merkins the other way, 5 Tempo Merkins, 5 Hand Release Merkins.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["upper"],"equipment":[],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-merkin-mile","name":"Merkin Mile","text":"25 merkins are completed after each 1/4 mile (Total: 100 merkins, 1 mile). This is an especially great exercise to jump-start your reps for the day during a push-up challenge!","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["lower","run","upper"],"equipment":[],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-merkin-mountain","name":"Merkin Mountain","text":"Coined by F3 Gator of #jugtown; start in an incline Merkin at the base of any stadium bleacher. Perform one merkin and climb (preferably bear crawl) until your feet are where your hands started. Perform 2 Merkins and repeat adding one Merkin for every level you go up until you reach the pinnacle.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["upper"],"equipment":[],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-merkin-pyramid","name":"Merkin Pyramid","text":"The Merkin Pyramid is an \"On Q\" continuous set of pushups that total 50 reps.\n10 Full Range Merkins (Regular Pushup)\n10 Mid Range Merkins (Come Down Halfway on the Pushup)\n10 Hi Range Merkins (Come Down Slightly on the Pushup)\n10 Mid Range Merkins (Come Down Halfway on the Pushup)\n10 Full Range Merkins (Regular Pushup)","kind":"thang","emphasis":["upper"],"equipment":[],"tags":["routine"]},{"id":"x-merkin-roll","name":"Merkin Roll","text":"Regular merkin position go down roll to your right push up go down as you get close to the grown roll left as soon as you are facing the ground push up","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["upper"],"equipment":[],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-merkin-wipes","name":"Merkin Wipes","text":"Like a merkin but with a wipe affect while in the down position (not touching ground). Can be done IC. Go down like a normal merkin. While in down position but not touching the ground, touch nose to left hand then touch nose to right hand, return to center position, then back up...that is one. NOTE: hands do not move, take your nose to your hands, thus \"wiping\" your nose across the ground. Enjoy!","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["upper"],"equipment":[],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-mexican-jumping-bean-pull-ups","name":"Mexican Jumping Bean Pull-ups","text":"Perform squat, jump to the pull up, complete pull up.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["lower","upper"],"equipment":["pull_up_bar"],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-mexican-jumping-bean-squats","name":"Mexican Jumping Bean Squats","text":"Perform a full squat, then a hop or jump.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["lower"],"equipment":[],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-michelin-man-bolt","name":"Michelin Man Bolt","text":"Similar to the Usain Bolt but with a tractor trailer tire in tow. Two pax are harnessed to a tractor trailer tire - that trails them by 8-10 feet. The pax team drag the tire 40 yards out and back while remaining pax perform the prescribed exercise. Perform through all pax. Rinse and repeat for duration for a solid all over beat down.","kind":"thang","emphasis":["cardio"],"equipment":[],"tags":["routine","team"]},{"id":"x-mickey-mouse-merkin","name":"Mickey Mouse Merkin","text":"In plank position, perform Wide Arm Merkin, Diamond Merkin, Wide Arm Merkin, then return to your feet. That's one. Wide, Diamond, Wide (WDW - like Walt Disney World). That's the Mickey Mouse connection. Do enough of them and it won't be the happiest place on Earth...","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["core","upper"],"equipment":[],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-mighty-jungle","name":"Mighty Jungle","text":"Done while playing \"The Lion Sleeps Tonight\" by The Tokens. Hold a high plank during the verses, and then do Doggie Paddles timed to each \"Wimoweh\" like you're in the Lion King.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["core"],"equipment":[],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-mike-tyson-burpee","name":"Mike Tyson Burpee","text":"In a plank position, (1) contract the legs for a horizontal squat. (2) Extend legs and leap forward like a frog (3) Perform a Merkin (4) Return to the starting position in a horizontal squat. That is one rep.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["cardio","core","lower","upper"],"equipment":[],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-mike-tyson-merkin","name":"Mike Tyson Merkin","text":"Place your feet against a curb or wall while in a plank position. (1) Contract the legs for a horizontal squat. (2) Extend legs (3) Perform a Merkin (4) Return to starting position in a horizontal squat. That is one rep. 10 reps is a nice starter. Also good with 7's or 11's on a narrow street. Mike Tyson's in combination with Bear Crawl's is a killer.\nTake it to the next level with your feet 6-12 inches up on a wall or up on a bench.\nThe Mike Tyson Internet Challenge: 20 Mike Tyson Merkins per minute for 10 minutes. That's 200 Mike Tyson Merkins total.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["core","lower","upper"],"equipment":["bench_wall"],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-mike-tyson-shoulder-taps","name":"Mike Tyson Shoulder Taps","text":"Mike Tyson Shoulder Taps is a 1:4 routine that consists of a @Mike Tyson followed by four @Alternating Shoulder Taps (2x1). Ascending count to 10:40.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["upper"],"equipment":[],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-mile-of-50s","name":"Mile of 50s","text":"At a standard 400-m track, the PAX jog 50 meters then Sprint 50 meters for 4 laps. This was a favorite training exercise of a former US Olympic 400-meter runner. If a PAX can do it under 6 minutes, they have Olympic potential!","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["cardio","run"],"equipment":["field"],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-millenial","name":"Millenial","text":"Goal is a total count of 2000 as a team. The full pax does 100 reps each of a called exercise, then runs a 100m lap back to a point where they gather again for the next called exercise. There will be 10 cycles, which get you to your number. Teamwork matters. The first nine cycles end when the FIRST person gets to 100, which keeps the pax together. The last cycle, which is always burpees, is done together and usually with someone Q-ing or rotating the Q through the 100 burpees. A sample set of cycles: 1) SSH; 2) Lunges; 3) Merkins; 4) LBCs; 5) Mtn. Climbers; 6) Flutters; 7) Arm Raises; 8) Squats; 9) Oblique Crunches - 50 per side; 10) Burpees Named as year 2000 is within the time period around which the Millenial generation was born.","kind":"thang","emphasis":["cardio","core","lower","upper"],"equipment":[],"tags":["mary","routine","team"]},{"id":"x-mini-chesto","name":"Mini Chesto","text":"Half the reps of a Mucho Chesto","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["upper"],"equipment":[],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-mini-hair-burners","name":"Mini-Hair Burners","text":"In regular plank position with weights or coupons close at hand, push weight or coupon forward with one hand across concrete and pull it back in cadence times x reps. Rinse and repeat with the other arm.","kind":"thang","emphasis":["core","heavy","upper"],"equipment":["coupon","weights"],"tags":["routine"]},{"id":"x-minnesota-burpee","name":"Minnesota Burpee","text":"A staple of the Twin Cities Winter Wolves during MABA, the Minnesota Burpee is a @exicon-1753308746961-burpee performed in the snow, shirtless. PAX must touch bare chest to snow at the bottom and jump at the top, no clap necessary. A true MN Burpee requires temperature at or below 15 degrees F, but the Q is welcome to call this exercise any time there is snow on the ground.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["cardio","lower","upper"],"equipment":[],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-miracle-mile","name":"Miracle Mile","text":"Yet another way to make running a mile miserable. The Miracle Mile is a ladder routine. A mile is run in 16x 100m segments with exercises at the beginning, end, and between each segment. The exercises reps increase with each segment. Start with one rep of each exercise, then run 100m. Then two reps of each exercise and a 100m run. Next three reps of each exercise and a 100m run. Continue the pattern increasing the rep count to 16. Finish with 17 reps of each exercise. 1 . . 16 Jump Squat 1 . . 16 Merkins 1 . . 16 Spartan hammers or Sit-Ups 1 . . 16 Burpees 100m run (Rinse & repeat) (Finisher) 17x Jump Squat 17x Merkins 17x Spartan hammers or Sit-ups 17x Burpees","kind":"thang","emphasis":["cardio","core","lower","run","upper"],"equipment":[],"tags":["finisher","routine"]},{"id":"x-mjolnir","name":"Mjolnir","text":"An advanced rotational core exercise named after Thor's hammer. Sit on your six with legs extended or elevated, hold a coupon (cinderblock, sandbag, kettlebell, etc.) with both hands, and rotate your torso from side to side, touching the coupon all the way to the ground on each side. This up-mod of the American Hammer or Russian Twist requires greater range of motion and core engagement by demanding ground contact on every rep. The movement builds explosive rotational strength, oblique endurance, and grip strength while challenging core stability. Modify coupon weight as needed to maintain proper form and full range of motion","kind":"thang","emphasis":["core","heavy","lower","mobility"],"equipment":["coupon","sandbag","weights"],"tags":["mary","routine"]},{"id":"x-monkey-crunches","name":"Monkey Crunches","text":"Get in sit up position, as you start to come up you touch your ankles and then go back down. Similar to a crunch but you come up farther. The farther you put your heels from your butt the harder it becomes.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["cardio","core"],"equipment":[],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-monkey-drill","name":"Monkey Drill","text":"Sideways lunge (defensive basketball slide) palms to ground as you extend. Done in two sets, once each direction as part of parking lot fun. Thanks Coach McCoy.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["lower"],"equipment":[],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-monkey-humpers","name":"Monkey Humpers","text":"A half-squat performed while grabbing the inside of one's ankles. This restricts movement to a half-squat type exercise but increasing the burn.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["lower"],"equipment":[],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-monkey-humping-goblet-squat","name":"Monkey Humping Goblet Squat","text":"When you need to go ape...with a kettle bell, no better way than with the MHGS. Grab your KB ready for a goblet squat, begin going down to the squat position bending knees / pivoting at hips / keeping back straight and hold, keeping KB in hand transition using only knees and hips to pivot your rear out in a monkey humper then return to squat, rise up to finish the squat and count it as 1. Great as a ladder 10 to 1 or 1 to 10 combined with an upper body exercise (like a bicep curl chest press combo).","kind":"thang","emphasis":["heavy","lower","upper"],"equipment":["weights"],"tags":["finisher","routine"]},{"id":"x-monkey-jumpers","name":"Monkey Jumpers","text":"Start with a half-squat while grabbing the inside of your ankles. Go down and up then let go of the ankles and jump.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["lower"],"equipment":[],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-monkey-rolls","name":"Monkey Rolls","text":"Break out into groups of 3 and start from the standing position in a line shoulder to shoulder with 4' spacing between PAX. The PAX in the center dives to the ground toward the right hands first and finishes with a complete roll. While the first PAX is rolling toward the PAX on the right, the PAX on the right dives hands first over the PAX rolling toward him, finishing by in a complete roll toward the PAX who started on the left. The PAX on the left dives over the PAX rolling toward him and does a complete roll. Once each PAX finishes their complete roll, stand back up and get ready to dive over the next PAX rolling toward you. Repeat to failure or time defined by Q","kind":"thang","emphasis":["upper"],"equipment":[],"tags":["routine"]},{"id":"x-monkey-squats","name":"Monkey Squats","text":"Step 1 Start in a plank position on your hands. Hands should be shoulder width apart. Step 2: Then, jump your feet forward and to the outside of your hands, ending in a low squat position, keeping your butt down as much as possible. Step 3: Push into your hands and jump your legs back into the starting plank position.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["core","lower","upper"],"equipment":[],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-moon-gods","name":"Moon Gods","text":"These are sun god's southern cousins! Start in side plank on elbow and edge of lower foot. Bring top foot into the air as high as comfortable and move in circular pattern. Switch sides and repeat! Best done on grass and IC.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["core"],"equipment":[],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-morning-call","name":"Morning Call","text":"All but one PAX get into push-up position and hold the up position while one guy counts off doing 5 pull-ups. Every time a pull-up is called out, the PAX does a merkin. After 5 pull-ups, he joins the PAX and the next guy gets up and calls out his 5 pull-ups. The cycle continues until all have performed 5 pull-ups. No one leaves the push-up position unless it's his turn to call out pull-ups or until all calls have been made.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["upper"],"equipment":["pull_up_bar"],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-morning-wood","name":"Morning Wood","text":"This is a Turkish Get-up without the Kettlebell. Laying flat on back with one arm raised sit up and then come up into a standing position. Added degree of difficulty = don't use other hand to push yourself up! (A Turkish Get-up without a Kettlebell is aka A Turkish Get-up.)","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["core","heavy","upper"],"equipment":["weights"],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-moroccan-night-club","name":"Moroccan Night Club","text":"The Moroccan Night Club is a classic F3 upper-body conditioning and warm-up exercise. To do it, stand with your feet shoulder-width apart and extend your arms straight out to the sides at shoulder height. Make fists with your hands and rapidly rotate your wrists in small, backward circles.\nThis movement is typically performed In Cadence (IC). When the workout leader counts \"one, two, three,\" you perform three backward rotations, followed by a slight pause. The goal is to keep your arms entirely stationary—allowing only the wrists and forearms to do the rotating—which isolates and burns out your shoulders, triceps, and forearms.","kind":"thang","emphasis":["upper"],"equipment":[],"tags":["routine","warmup"]},{"id":"x-moseyvators","name":"Moseyvators","text":"Q leads PAX in a single file run and completes ‘Motivators’ from 10 or a number chosen by the Q. First sequence starts when the Q raises his hand and stops the line. Q does an about face in front of the line of PAX and then begins first sequence of 10 Motivators. After completion, Q does an about face and continues the mosey. Second sequence starts when Q raises his hand again and stops the line. Q does an about face and then 9 Motivators. Return to mosey. Repeato until entire sequence of Motivators is complete. Mosey can be as long or as short as the Q decides.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["cardio","run"],"equipment":[],"tags":["warmup"]},{"id":"x-motivators","name":"Motivators","text":"The Q calls a starting number (e.g., “Motivators from 7”).\nPax perform that number of reps of each of the following movements in cadence, then repeat the full sequence at one less rep, descending until reaching 1 rep of each movement:\n• Full Side Straddle Hops: standard SSH (arms + legs)\n• Half-Arm SSH: arms only rise to shoulder height in a “T” position (no leg movement change)\n• Leg-Only Jacks: legs open and close only (arms stay on hips)\n• Hops: small hops in place with feet together (no leg opening)\nExample (Motivators from 3):\n• 3 Full SSH → 3 Half-Arm SSH → 3 Leg-Only Jacks → 3 Hops\n• 2 Full SSH → 2 Half-Arm SSH → 2 Leg-Only Jacks → 2 Hops\n• 1 Full SSH → 1 Half-Arm SSH → 1 Leg-Only Jacks → 1 Hops\nQ Tip: It is helpful for the Q to count down (e.g. “7…6…5…”) rather than up.","kind":"thang","emphasis":["lower","upper"],"equipment":[],"tags":["routine"]},{"id":"x-motor-city-shuffle","name":"Motor City Shuffle","text":"Complete in order:\nLunge x2, Burpee, Merkins x5, Plank Jacks x5, Fog Hop = 1 rep. Can be done in place of mosey.\nThis one should be done in a grassy field.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["cardio","core","lower","upper"],"equipment":["field"],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-mountain-climber-merkin","name":"Mountain Climber Merkin","text":"Three mountain climber leg movements then Merkin down for count. 1,2,3, down!","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["core","lower","upper"],"equipment":[],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-mountain-climbers","name":"Mountain Climbers","text":"Done from high plank position, run in place.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["cardio","core","run"],"equipment":[],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-mountain-goats","name":"Mountain Goats","text":"Like Mountain Climbers but with an added goat kick (where both legs leave the ground simultaneously) - exercise is done on a four count ... three mountain climbers (1 - 2 - 3) and the 4 is the goat kick. Get those legs up high to 45 degrees! Repeato until you''ve had enough.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["core","lower"],"equipment":[],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-mountain-man-pooper","name":"Mountain Man Pooper","text":"A 4-count full-body exercise that flows through multiple positions in a rocking motion. Starting standing with arms extended forward, (1) bend at the waist and touch your toes with straight legs, (2) drop into a deep squat position with arms raised overhead, (3) press up out of the squat back to standing while bringing hands back down to touch toes, (4) rotate back up to the starting standing position with arms extended. The continuous flow between toe touches and deep squats creates a dynamic stretch while building leg strength, mobility, and cardiovascular endurance. The movement resembles a rocking chair motion, hence the alternate name","kind":"thang","emphasis":["lower","mobility","upper"],"equipment":[],"tags":["routine"]},{"id":"x-mountain-merkin","name":"Mountain Merkin","text":"From Merkin position, pax performs 4 mountain climbers and 1 merkin. That is one rep.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["core","upper"],"equipment":[],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-mountain-merkins","name":"Mountain Merkins","text":"While in plank position (preferably on an incline, hill, berm, etc.) PAX would do Mountain Climbers (right, left, right, left) in cadence. Perform 2 Merkins (down, up, down, up) in cadence. This equals 1 rep.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["core","upper"],"equipment":[],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-mucho-chesto","name":"Mucho Chesto","text":"Chest blaster exercise intended to build mucho chesto. 10 x Merkin / 10 x Wide Merkin / 10 x Diamonds / 10 Stagger Merkin Left / 10 Stagger Merkin Right. Rinse and repeat for a total 100 Merkins. Time yourself and try to improve for a bonus.","kind":"thang","emphasis":["upper"],"equipment":[],"tags":["routine"]},{"id":"x-mucho-leg-o","name":"Mucho Leg-o","text":"Mucho Leg-o 1) Narrow squat (feet together), 2) regular-stance squat, 3) wide squat, 4) bonnie blair (jumping lunge) with left foot forward, 5) bonnie blair with right foot forward (then back to narrow stance). Repeato until you look like a baby giraffe stumbling across the Savannah.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["lower","upper"],"equipment":[],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-muffin-man","name":"Muffin Man","text":"A full-body, high-intensity movement combining a forward roll, burpee, and squat clean using a cinder block (“Cindy”), finished with a call-and-response cadence.\nExecution:\n• Start standing, holding the Cindy at chest level\n• Hinge at the hips and place the Cindy on the ground (“set the pan”)\n• Assume a push-up position with hands on the Cindy\n• Roll the Cindy forward approximately 1–2 feet (“roll the dough”)\n• Immediately perform a burpee\n• Upon standing, step forward to the Cindy\n• Squat clean the Cindy to chest level\n• Extend the Cindy slightly forward (“put the pan in the oven”)\n• Return to standing position\nCadence:\nLeader:\n“Do you know the Muffin Man?!”\nGroup:\n“THE MUFFIN MAN!!”\n(Cadence is performed after each completed repetition)\nModification:\n• Step back instead of full burpee\n• Remove squat clean and perform a simple lift to chest\n• Eliminate push-up portion for beginners\nAdvanced Variation:\nThe Muffin Man Deluxe\n• Add a controlled “pop” (slight toss) of the Cindy during the squat clean before catching it at the chest\n• Option to add overhead press after clean","kind":"thang","emphasis":["cardio","heavy","lower","upper"],"equipment":["coupon"],"tags":["routine"]},{"id":"x-multi-merkin-m-m","name":"Multi-Merkin (M&M)","text":"Start in high plank position, perform merkin, the tough left knee, merkin, right knee, merkin left foot, merkin, right foot, merkin, stretch left, merkin stretch right, merkin, inch worm back, stand up is one repetition.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["core","mobility","upper"],"equipment":[],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-murder-blockee","name":"Murder Blockee","text":"Perform a Murder Bunny as usual, but when you end the murder bunny hop movement, you immediately throw your legs back and go into the down position of a blockee and then continue the blockee movment up, raising the coupon or sandbag above your head to complete the rep. Performed as a moving exercise across a field, parking lot or other area for distance.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["heavy","lower","upper"],"equipment":["coupon","field","sandbag"],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-murder-bunny","name":"Murder Bunny","text":"Stand with feet slightly more than shoulder width apart with coupon longways between them. Bend over and grab the coupon, lift it a few inches off the ground and move it forward until you can't reach. Then, put the coupon down, transition your weight to the coupon (through your hands) and hop (think burpee) your feet back to where they are on either side of the coupon.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["cardio","heavy","upper"],"equipment":["coupon","weights"],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-murder-burpees","name":"Murder Burpees","text":"Play the song \"Here Comes the Hotstepper\" by Ini Kamoze. Every time he says the word \"murderer\" you have to do a burpee. The rest of the time you should be doing side straddle hops or high knees. Can be done as a warmup. Burpee total will be 24.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["cardio","upper"],"equipment":["speaker"],"tags":["warmup"]},{"id":"x-murder-hornet","name":"Murder Hornet","text":"Murder Hornet Take on the Killer B''s Routine from Iron Pax '19, but with a cinderblock coupon. Pax line up at the start. Murder Bunny 10 yards then: 10 Man Makers, 10 Lunges w/coupon, 10 BBS w/coupon. Repeat til 30 yard line. Once complete: Bear Crawl + Coupon Drag back to starting line. Rinse and Repeat the whole thing.","kind":"thang","emphasis":["cardio","heavy","lower"],"equipment":["coupon","field"],"tags":["routine"]},{"id":"x-musical-dora","name":"Musical Dora","text":"Musical Dora is Dora's fun and sinister sides put together. Partner up just like a Dora. Partner 1 does the selected exercise while partner 2 runs either a hill or circuit and back then flapjack. During this time you have your favorite play list going. All exercises are done for the time period of a song. Sandbags or kettle bells are good here for the exercises. Tailor your playlist and exercises to the length of time you want to take. Examples of exercises: Kettle bell swings, overhead press, curls, bent over row, goblet squats, thrusters, overhead tricep extensions and the crowd pleasers: burpees or merkins to finish done to the 6:05 minute version of MJ singing \"Don't Stop Till You Get Enough\". Doing the exercises to a time based count (song) keeps all PAX together and who doesn't love to work out to the Q's favorite play list?","kind":"thang","emphasis":["cardio","heavy","lower","upper"],"equipment":["sandbag","speaker","swing"],"tags":["finisher","partner","routine"]},{"id":"x-m-nage","name":"Ménage","text":"Teams of three. Each team does 90 of selected exercise as a group. Planks in between exercises. Repeat times 6.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["core"],"equipment":[],"tags":["team"]},{"id":"x-nadal","name":"Nadal","text":"Running the lines of a tennis court.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["cardio","run"],"equipment":[],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-navy-seal-burpee","name":"Navy Seal Burpee","text":"This is a classic exercise that can be worked into any THANG you might have in mind (or even a warmup or MARY). The Navy Seal burpee (or Seal Burpee) is a standard burpee but on the down you are executing a sequence of three merkins where on the first two, execute a knee-tuck on the up.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["cardio","upper"],"equipment":[],"tags":["mary","warmup"]},{"id":"x-necro-bunny","name":"Necro Bunny","text":"Perform a Murder Bunny and after each \"hop,\" remain with hands on Cindy (coupon). Without standing up, perform 5 squats or \"Frog Squats.\" Distance set by Q","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["heavy","lower"],"equipment":["coupon"],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-nemos","name":"NEMOs","text":"This routine mixes a get-up with a blockee. Start laying flat on your back, with a cindy on the ground above your head. Grasp the cindy, bring to your chest, perform one press straight up. Place cindy to one side, then kick out your legs or flip over to an inclined plank position. Perform one incline merkin, then without releasing the cindy, stand up and perform an overhead press. Return to inclined plank, perform another inclined merkin. Return to position on your back, perform one press straight up over chest with cindy. Return cindy to position over your head for one rep. Courtesy of Honker, F3 Pooler","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["core","lower","upper"],"equipment":[],"tags":["mary"]},{"id":"x-never-cross-dolly","name":"Never Cross Dolly","text":"On your 6 just like your going to do Dolly's but your upper body is in the iron cross position the whole time doing Dolly's. Only your 6 is touching the ground.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["core"],"equipment":[],"tags":["mary"]},{"id":"x-new-test","name":"New Test","text":"test\n@test\n• Bullet point 1\n• Bullet point 2\n• Number 1\n• Number 2\ntest\nthis is a test\nAnother\nAnd another\ntest\ntest\ntest\ntest\ntest\ntest","kind":"exercise","emphasis":[],"equipment":[],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-newton-s-cradle","name":"Newton's Cradle","text":"Just like your boss's favorite desk decoration ( https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=GyhaVaZgqTI ), get in plank position (with or without coupons) and extend your left arm perpendicular to your body until it is parallel to the ground. Return and repeat with the right arm to complete the four count cadence.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["core","heavy","upper"],"equipment":["coupon"],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-nicole","name":"Nicole","text":"Nicole is one of the girls of Crossfit. Set a timer for 20 minutes. Pax will complete AMRAP (As Many Rounds As Possible) of the following: Run 400m; Pull-ups AMRAP (As Many Reps As Possible) Mix up the pull-ups, chin-ups etc. as you see fit.; Repeato until the timer sounds.","kind":"thang","emphasis":["cardio","run","upper"],"equipment":["pull_up_bar","timer"],"tags":["routine"]},{"id":"x-ninnie-knockers","name":"Ninnie Knockers","text":"Sitting on picnic table, leaning back on elbows, toes pointed to the floor so that entire body is a straight line. The \"1\" count is bring knees as close to your chest as you can, \"2\" is to extend with your toes pointing straight to the floor, \"3 and 4\" is repeat. In 4-count cadence.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["upper"],"equipment":["bench_wall"],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-nipple-scraper-merkin","name":"Nipple Scraper Merkin","text":"(Also called a Half Moon push up.) With hands on a curb & butts high, drop knees down and to one side. Lower one nipple until it touches the curb, twist your body in the low plank position until the other nipple comes to the curb, and then press up. That is one rep. Reverse the motion.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["core","upper"],"equipment":["bench_wall"],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-no-cheat-merkin","name":"No Cheat Merkin","text":"A strict push-up variation that eliminates momentum and ensures full range of motion. At the bottom of each push-up, lift both hands completely off the ground before pressing back up. At the top of the movement, perform two shoulder taps (alternating hands tapping opposite shoulders) before descending into the next rep. This forces you to maintain tension throughout, prevents bouncing or cheating, and adds an anti-rotation core challenge with the shoulder taps. The result is a more difficult, higher-quality merkin that builds greater upper body strength and core stability","kind":"thang","emphasis":["core","mobility","upper"],"equipment":[],"tags":["routine"]},{"id":"x-no-surrender","name":"No Surrender","text":"Begin the no-surrender in the standing position with your hands locked behind your head and elbows pointing outward.4 count: 1.Go down on left knee, then 2. down on the right knee so now you're on both knees. 3.Then stand back up on left leg then 4. up with the right leg. After half the desired reps, switch the starting leg so that you don't favor one side. (also called Prisoner Get Ups)","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["lower"],"equipment":[],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-no-surrender-indian-plank","name":"No Surrender Indian Plank","text":"The entire PAX holds the full plank position. Starting in the down/rest position, Q gives the \"up\" signal and everyone assumes the full plank. The PAX at the rear then completes 5 no-surrenders, returns to the full up plank position, and gives the \"down\" signal. After a brief (approx. 5 second) rest, Q again gives the \"up\" signal, and the next PAX completes their no-surrenders. This continues until everyone had completed their no-surrenders.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["core"],"equipment":[],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-noho-row","name":"NoHo Row","text":"Stand in mid stance lunge with lead foot slight twist in. Hold Coupon where hand of the forward foot is thru Coupon holding bottom lip, other hand is atop the Coupon holding lip. Row Cindy in large circle bringing bottom hand in line with back foot and top hand to over forward knee.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["heavy","lower","upper"],"equipment":["coupon"],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-nolan-richardson","name":"Nolan Richardson","text":"Aka \"40 minutes of Hell.\"\nWarm-O-Rama:\nWindmills (20)\nAmerican Hammers( 20)\nMosey (Around Ballfield)\nRoutine:\nPartner 1 will perform each exercise denoted below as Partner 2 backpedals 50 yards, performs a @Bobby Hurley, then runs back to continue the exercise from the count accumulated by Partner 1. This will continue until the repetition count stated below is met.\n• Burpees (150).\n• Squats (300).\n• Big Boy Sit-Ups (150).\n• Little Baby Arm Circles (300).\n• Merkins (150).\n• Imperial Walkers (300).","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["cardio","core","lower","upper"],"equipment":["field"],"tags":["mary","partner","warmup"]},{"id":"x-nolan-ryan","name":"Nolan Ryan","text":"Start in a side plank position with your ungrounded arm extended. Complete a punching motion as if someone, namely Robin Ventura, were under your other arm.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["core","upper"],"equipment":[],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-non-alternating-shoulder-taps","name":"Non-Alternating Shoulder Taps","text":"Much like a combination of the Alternating Shoulder Taps (but you do not alternate) and a clap merkin (but rather than clap, you touch both shoulders). So, from the plank you go down as far as you need, probably halfway, to push up with enough force to be able to touch your right hand to your left shoulder and your left hand to your right shoulder AT THE SAME TIME, and then get your hands down in time to do some more. It is like the clap merkin, but since your hands are not under your body, it is a little scarier and you need a better push to have time to cross both arms and touch both shoulders and then get your hands down in time to not smash your face. Requires good explosive power. Good to call 10 OYO.","kind":"thang","emphasis":["cardio","core","upper"],"equipment":[],"tags":["routine"]},{"id":"x-noodling-for-catfish","name":"Noodling for Catfish","text":"Start in a plank position on an incline (bench, table, steps) do a merkin but when in down position, hold with one arm while other reaches down under bench, table, steps etc like your feeling for something for 3 seconds and then hand back to bench and finish the merkin.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["core","upper"],"equipment":["bench_wall","stairs"],"tags":["finisher"]},{"id":"x-noonan","name":"Noonan","text":"Running up stadium stairs with a ruck on. Any form of weighted ruck or coupon up and down stairs. In Honor of F3 Naperville's Steve Keough (F3 Noonan) who suddenly passed away while rucking.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["cardio","heavy","ruck","run"],"equipment":["coupon","ruck","stairs"],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-not-so-lazy-boys","name":"Not-So Lazy Boys","text":"On your six sitting upright with your legs straight out in front of you. Cross your arms and grab your sides, leaning back in your \"Lazy Boy\" as far as you can without your feet coming off the ground. Hold and engage your core for 10-15 seconds and rotate to your right, dropping your right elbow towards the ground (not letting it touch the ground), back to the middle (hold for 10-15 seconds, core still engaged) and then rotate over to your left, dropping your left elbow towards the ground (not letting it touch the ground). Do this for as long as you''d like..on the Q's lead and count!","kind":"thang","emphasis":["core","lower","mobility","upper"],"equipment":[],"tags":["mary","routine"]},{"id":"x-nutcracker","name":"Nutcracker","text":"Nutcracker With a brick in each hand held overhead, perform a lunge. At the same time, lower the arms and bring the bricks together between the legs. Return to the standing position, raising the bricks back overhead.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["lower","upper"],"equipment":[],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-o-p-p","name":"O.P.P.","text":"You down with O.P.P? Yeah you know me! Whose down with O.P.P? All of F3! Partner up. Partner 1 does Overhead Claps while in People's Chair (O.P.). Meanwhile Partner 2 does a set number of Plank Jacks. Switch. Can do multiple rounds, swapping out the Plank Jacks for Peter Parkers or Parker Peters or any exercise that starts with P.","kind":"thang","emphasis":["cardio","core"],"equipment":[],"tags":["partner","routine"]},{"id":"x-obama","name":"Obama","text":"In honor of the 44th POTUS, this traveling exercise consists primarily of a Bear Crawl, but after every 4 hand moves PAX must stop and perform 4 Merkins. (The 4 and 4 for the 44th, in case you needed that explained to you...)","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["upper"],"equipment":[],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-old-flame-drill-ofd","name":"Old Flame Drill (OFD)","text":"These 4 runner specific exercises done in sequence. runner's squat > scorpions > bulgarian split squat > bridges. All exercises done single leg 10 per leg (or more). Search youtube for a demonstration of these exercises.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["cardio","lower"],"equipment":[],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-old-town-pain-train","name":"Old Town Pain Train","text":"Every time you hear the train whistle, 10 burpees. Named for the AO in Rock Hill closest to the RR tracks.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["cardio","run"],"equipment":["field"],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-ollie-norths","name":"Ollie Norths","text":"Heaving a man over your back to carry him from the battlefield. ''Then carry him for a while. (f/k/a First Responders)","kind":"exercise","emphasis":[],"equipment":["field"],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-one-calls","name":"One Calls","text":"This is an 8-count IC exercise developed as a result of the sometimes horrible merkin form by some PAX, especially those claiming to do great #''s when in fact they didn't do any correctly. It was a way to force the PAX to have FULL extension both at the bottom and the top, which only makes them better (and stops the improper form). Since I work with OneCall and he would come to the office daily to complain about this, I developed this exercise and named it after him for my upcoming Q. Start in Merkin/Plank position. 1 '' Down; 2 '' Hand Release; 3 '' Up and hold; 4 '' Floyd Mayweather Punch Right arm; 5 '' Right arm down; 6 '' Floyd Mayweather Punch Left arm; 7 '' Left arm down; 8 (which would be the PAX count of 1, 2, 3, etc) '' Full plank. As you can see, this forces the PAX to go all the way down instead of the 1-2'' down that some claim count as a merkin, and it forces a locking of the elbows at the top. 10-15 of these are excellent. It has also been done with 2 PAX facing each other and keeping each other honest (Q choice with these to make the Floyd Mayweathers into Booyah Merkins or Slap 5's or anything like that where the PAX are mirroring each other).","kind":"thang","emphasis":["cardio","core","upper"],"equipment":[],"tags":["routine"]},{"id":"x-one-armed-pickle-pounder-with-coupon","name":"One-armed Pickle Pounder with Coupon","text":"Start with one arm on the ground in pickle pounder position, the other hand has the coupon (in Jacksonville we use a milk jug filled with water approx. 8lbs) Hold the coupon on the small of your back with the free hand during reps x20 in cadence, switch arms and repeat.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["heavy","upper"],"equipment":["coupon"],"tags":["mary"]},{"id":"x-one-legged-burpee","name":"One-legged Burpee","text":"Not enough exercises start with \"O\" so... the one-legged burpee is like a regular burpee, but with one leg that stays off the ground through the entire set. Best to do two balanced sets or one split set so you don''t look like a #Yepremian.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["cardio","lower"],"equipment":[],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-orangutans","name":"Orangutans","text":"A posterior chain exercise that targets the calves and hamstrings. Start in a standing position and plant your fingertips on the ground in front of your toes. Drop into a deep squat while keeping your fingers planted, then stand up by straightening your legs while maintaining finger contact with the ground. At the top, lift your heels as high as possible to engage the calves, creating strong activation in both the calves and hamstrings. Return to the deep squat position and repeat. This movement challenges flexibility, balance, and builds serious posterior chain strength","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["lower","mobility"],"equipment":[],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-outlaw","name":"Outlaw","text":"Sitting in the position for flutter kicks, keep your feet together and make a big \"O\" with them. 10 reps to the right and 10 reps to the left or as many reps as the Q deems necessary.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["core"],"equipment":[],"tags":["mary"]},{"id":"x-over-the-mountain-merkin","name":"Over the Mountain Merkin","text":"Start with an offset Merkin with one hand on the coupon, then a Merkin with both hands on the coupon, then an offset Merkin on the other side, with the other hand on the coupon. That is one rep. Rinse and repeat each direction over the mountain.","kind":"thang","emphasis":["heavy","upper"],"equipment":["coupon"],"tags":["routine"]},{"id":"x-pain-maker","name":"Pain Maker","text":"Two Merkins at the bottom of a Man Maker (Blockee) and a Thruster at the top","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["upper"],"equipment":[],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-painkillers","name":"Painkillers","text":"Painkillers Start with a Man-Maker ,then add a double merkin and plank jacks to it","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["core","upper"],"equipment":[],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-pamela-anderson","name":"Pamela Anderson","text":"Burpee with a nipple scraper merkin (with or without a curb). Performance in slow motion while in a bathing suit is purely optional!","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["cardio","upper"],"equipment":["bench_wall"],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-pansey","name":"Pansey","text":"Conduct pull up. While up, lift the legs to the 90 degree position or beyond. lower legs to perpendicular to the ground. Lower body to the down position. Repeat.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["lower","upper"],"equipment":[],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-parker-peter","name":"Parker Peter","text":"A @Peter Parker, except your knee crosses to the opposite elbow.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":[],"equipment":[],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-parking-space-tracer","name":"Parking Space Tracer","text":"For those participating in an AO with a parking lot, PAX starts at one point on a parking space line. PAX runs/sidesteps/runs backward while tracing the lines on the parking lot. Even better when double sided / open spaces.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["cardio"],"equipment":[],"tags":["competitive","game"]},{"id":"x-partner-carry","name":"Partner Carry","text":"Carry a partner either in a fireman hold or simply on your back some distance that Q calls out.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":[],"equipment":[],"tags":["mary","partner"]},{"id":"x-partner-coupon-swing","name":"Partner Coupon Swing","text":"A partner exercise where two PAX work together to swing a coupon (cinderblock, sandbag, or other weight) between them. Partners face each other at a safe distance, and one person swings the coupon using a kettlebell-style hip hinge motion to propel it toward their partner, who catches and controls it before swinging it back. This movement requires coordination, communication, timing, and trust between partners while building explosive hip power, grip strength, and cardiovascular endurance. The shared work creates accountability and camaraderie","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["heavy"],"equipment":["coupon","sandbag","swing","weights"],"tags":["partner"]},{"id":"x-partner-derkin","name":"Partner Derkin","text":"Merkin performed with your feet up on your planking partner's back.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["core","upper"],"equipment":[],"tags":["partner"]},{"id":"x-partner-plank-curls","name":"Partner Plank Curls","text":"Partner up. One partner gets in plank position. The other partner stands directly behind him and grabs planked partner's ankles and does bicep curls. Make sure partner in plank position keeps legs together.","kind":"thang","emphasis":["core","lower","upper"],"equipment":[],"tags":["partner","routine"]},{"id":"x-partner-shrug","name":"Partner Shrug","text":"Partner #1 assumes the plank position. Partner #2 grabs partner #1 by the ankles and commences shoulder shrug exercise using Partner #1 as weight. Flapjack and repeat.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["cardio","core","heavy","upper"],"equipment":["weights"],"tags":["partner"]},{"id":"x-pattycake-merkin","name":"Pattycake Merkin","text":"Two partners face each other in plank position and perform merkin together. On up movement, partners touch right hands in the middle. Repeat merkin and switch hands.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["core","upper"],"equipment":[],"tags":["partner"]},{"id":"x-paula-abdul","name":"Paula Abdul","text":"Any set in which you take 2 steps forward and then 1 step back and continue to do so until you reach a defined endpoint. For example: run up 2 ramps of a parking deck, perform an exercise, run down 1 ramp, perform an exercise, continue until you reach the top. Also works well with parking lot lines, speed bumps, light posts, flights of stairs, etc.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["cardio","run"],"equipment":["stairs"],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-paula-crabdul","name":"Paula Crabdul","text":"In a crab walk position; move forward or sideway 2 steps, then move backward or opposite sideway 2 steps - (I take two steps forward, I take two steps back)","kind":"exercise","emphasis":[],"equipment":["stairs"],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-pbk-patrick-brian-kenny","name":"PBK (Patrick Brian Kenny)","text":"First started in F3 Katy on the 20-year anniversary of Pat's death in Iraq (10-6-2005). The men of each Katy @AO honored the life of Pat's ultimate sacrifice. He died at age 20 from an improvised explosive device while conducting combat operations against enemy forces near Al Karmah, Iraq. Pat was an absolute legend and had an infectious personality. This BD/WOD honors his sacrifice and legacy.\nThe @BEAT DOWN is 11s of @Blockee and @Burpee. This is roughly a 30-minute circuit. Start with 1 Blockee, run a minimum distance of 30 yards, perform 10 Burpees. Run back to @Coupon and perform, 2 Blockees, run a minimum distance of 30 yards, perform 9 Burpees, all the way until @PAX perform 10 Blockees and 1 Burpee. This beat down can also be performed with sandbags.","kind":"thang","emphasis":["cardio","core","heavy","lower","run","upper"],"equipment":["coupon","sandbag"],"tags":["routine"]},{"id":"x-peeping-lipstick","name":"Peeping Lipstick","text":"A combination of a Turkish Getup and Star Jump. PAX performs the Turkish Getup and then immediately performs 1 Star Jump. The transition between TG and SJ should be done fluidly. This exercise name comes from the combination of 2 PAX names, \"Peeping Tom\" (who loves Turkish Getups) and \"Lipstick\" (who loves Star Jumps), who were once working out together as Co-Qs and decided to combine the two movements. The name Turkish Getup Star Jumps is just way too long to say.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["lower"],"equipment":[],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-people-s-air-presses","name":"People's Air Presses","text":"While squatting in the People's Chair, perform overhead air presses.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["lower","upper"],"equipment":[],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-people-s-chair","name":"People's Chair","text":"Sitting against a wall with knees bent at a 90-degree angle for a period of time TBD by the workout leader.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":[],"equipment":["bench_wall"],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-people-s-chair-modification","name":"People's Chair Modification","text":"Things to distract your mind while in the Peoples Chair - Overhead presses, holding arms horizontal, left and right punches, left or right leg off the ground, and wall/thigh/chest slaps.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["cardio","lower","upper"],"equipment":["bench_wall"],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-peter-parker","name":"Peter Parker","text":"In plank position move left knee toward left elbow with foot flared out.. then flapjack. You should look like Spider-Man climbing a wall.\nTo modify up, combine with @Merkin, so that when you go down you bring your leg in, and then straighten the leg as you return to plank.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["cardio","core","lower","upper"],"equipment":["bench_wall"],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-peter-parker-peter","name":"Peter Parker Peter","text":"Done by combining @Peter Parker and @Parker Peter. Do both on one leg before switching to other leg.\nOn count 1, Right Leg goes up into Peter Parker, 2 it comes back, then same leg goes into Parker Peter on 3, then back on the count, then do the same with left leg.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["lower"],"equipment":[],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-pick-your-poison","name":"Pick Your Poison","text":"Great routine to move PAX through an AO, test a new site, or show off seldom used features. Identify 4-5 \"stops\" you want to make around the AO and exercises to go with each.\nPAX get to choose their area of focus for day. There are Upper, Lower, and Core exercises for each stop on the AO tour. Depending on your focus, you'll perform 40, 30, or 20 reps of the prescribed exercises. If Upper is first priority, do 40 reps of upper, followed by 30 reps of second priority and 20 reps of third priority. Once done, begin heading to next spot with prescribed MOT. When finished, the 6 will mosey, collecting PAX doing MOT until all PAX are moseying to next location.\nSample routine:\nStop 1:\nUpper: Merkins\nLower: Jump Squat\nCore: BBSU\nMOT: Crawl Bear\nStop 2:\nUpper: Dips on bench\nLower: Monkey Humpers\nCore: American Hammer\nMOT: Lunge Walk\nStop 3:\nUpper: Derkin\nLower: Twinkle Toes\nCore: Hello Dollys\nMOT: Crab Walk\nStop 4:\nUpper: Dirty Hookups on picnic table bench\nLower: Step up on picnic table bench\nCore: LBCs\nMOT: Duck Walk\nStop 5:\nUpper: Rows on playground equipment\nLower: Apollo Ohno\nCore: Dying Cockroach\nMOT: Inchworm","kind":"thang","emphasis":["cardio","core","lower","upper"],"equipment":["bench_wall"],"tags":["mary","routine"]},{"id":"x-pickle-grinders","name":"Pickle Grinders","text":"Find a bench, box or low wall where Partner A lays face down over the edge of said device with the edge at hip level or slightly lower. Partner B holds Partner A's legs firmly down. Partner A drops torso below device and reverses to tight hold with back arched upward. Exercise name becomes evident very quickly with fast adjustments. Great with a modest coupon.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["heavy","lower"],"equipment":["bench_wall","coupon"],"tags":["partner"]},{"id":"x-pickle-pointers","name":"Pickle Pointers","text":"Hip bridges.\n• Lay on back.\n• Tighten core.\n• Legs shoulder width apart.\n• Push hips to the sky, not arching back, focus on glutes and slightly curling hips forward.\n• Do reps pushing hips to the sky then tapping glues to the ground.\n• Slow and steady, focus on form.\nModifiers:\n• Wide Leg Pickle Pointers\n• Butterfly Pickle Pointers","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["core","lower","upper"],"equipment":[],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-pickle-pounder","name":"Pickle Pounder","text":"Begin in an elbow plank then alternate hip flexion and extension in cadence. Best performed in front of store windows or in quiet neighborhoods.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["core"],"equipment":[],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-pickle-push-it","name":"Pickle Push It","text":"Play Salt-N-Pepa's \"Push It.\"\nGet in a tabletop position (feet and hands planted on your six, then hoist yourself to a flat core). \"Push it\" = 1 Pickle Pusher. Synth/Music = Tabletop Hold.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["core"],"equipment":["speaker"],"tags":["mary"]},{"id":"x-pike-pleaser","name":"Pike Pleaser","text":"Same format as a @exicon-1753308764010-crowd-pleaser except Carolina Dry Dock (pike pushup) and Alternating Toe Taps are substituted. 1:1 CCD to ATT, 2:2, and so on, up to 4:4 (or 5:5 if tough enough) and back down to 1:1","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["upper"],"equipment":[],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-pinocchio","name":"Pinocchio","text":"Pax circle up, get on their 6 with heads facing toward the circle, shoulder to shoulder. Q passes out two 40lbs sandbags on opposite sides of circle and instructs the Pax starts passing the bags ''Pax reacts gleefully saying, \"Is that it?\" then Q institutes a Low Slow Flutter AMRAP, then Freddy Mercury. Pax call Q a liar, just like Pinocchio.","kind":"thang","emphasis":["core","heavy","upper"],"equipment":["sandbag"],"tags":["mary","routine"]},{"id":"x-pinochle","name":"Pinochle","text":"Each PAX pickes a card from the pinochle deck. The card values represent the reps and the suit represented the exercise. 9 = x9, 10 = x10, Jack = x11, Queen = x12, King = x13, Ace = x20, Game instruction card = Dealers Choice x50 Hearts = Merkins Diamonds = Burpees Spades = Squats Clubs = American Hammers","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["cardio","core","lower","upper"],"equipment":[],"tags":["game","mary"]},{"id":"x-pistol-squats","name":"Pistol Squats","text":"One legged squats. Extend right leg out front. Lower and keep right leg extended out, then raise back up. Flapjack. Takes balance. Can be done in front of a pole for balance help","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["cardio","lower"],"equipment":[],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-piston","name":"Piston","text":"Starting in standing position and a Block/Coupon on the ground at your feet, squat and pick up block and return to standing position with it. Then perform a squat and place the block to its original position and return to original standing position w/out the block. Uncoordinated pax (almost everyone) will eventually get out of sync thereby looking like the pistons of that \"See-Thru\" engine block you see at the car parts store.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["heavy","lower"],"equipment":["coupon"],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-plank-compass","name":"Plank Compass","text":"From plank position, Q calls out direction such as 90 degrees right or 180 degrees left. Pax rotates accordingly, walking hand over hand to the location designated by the Q (staying in plank), with toes acting as the center of the compass (stationary), and hands and head moving around the arc of the circle. Mix in Merkins at each stop. Do as many rotations as you like.","kind":"thang","emphasis":["core","upper"],"equipment":[],"tags":["routine"]},{"id":"x-plank-destroyer","name":"Plank Destroyer","text":"Plank Destroyer All the fun you can have with a Plank, mashed up into one exercise. Begin in Plank position, perform a Makhtar N''Diaye ending back in Plank position, perform a Merkin, perform alternating Shoulder Taps, perform a Plank Jack. That''s one rep. Ideal entry in a sequence of low-rep exercises.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["core","upper"],"equipment":[],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-plank-dips","name":"Plank Dips","text":"Steamer's M introduced him to plank dips and he brought them to PowderKeg. It can be done from regular plank or elbow plank position. From plank rotate your hips down to the ground on each side. 1 left, 2 regular, 3 right, regular for cadence count.","kind":"thang","emphasis":["core","upper"],"equipment":[],"tags":["routine"]},{"id":"x-plank-fonda","name":"Plank Fonda","text":"Side plank, arm extended (on elbow to modify), lift upper leg in Jane Fonda motion, switch sides and repeat. Done in cadence... with enthusiasm...","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["core","lower","upper"],"equipment":[],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-plank-hurdles","name":"Plank Hurdles","text":"Done on a football field. In small groups of 5-6, everyone starts in the plank position in the end zone. 1st man from each group sprints to the 10 and planks, 2nd sprints, hurdles him, planks on the 20, 3rd man hurdles each, planks on the 30, etc. At the end of the group, 1st man sprints, hurdles everyone, etc. Everyone should finish in a plank in the opposite end zone.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["cardio","core","run"],"equipment":["field"],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-plank-jacks","name":"Plank Jacks","text":"Jumping Jacks while in the plank position.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["cardio","core","lower"],"equipment":[],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-plankorama","name":"Plankorama","text":"A routine; any kind of plank strung together until TBQ.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["cardio","core"],"equipment":[],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-plankorama-mama","name":"Plankorama-mama","text":"This is a series of exercises that alternate between plank position and seated position with no rest between. Ex. Hydraulics x 20 IC/LBCs x 20 IC/Shoulder taps x 20....etc. The name derives from a couple of AOs that have begun to shorten 6 minutes of mary to 6mom and then into momma.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["core","upper"],"equipment":[],"tags":["mary"]},{"id":"x-play-it-cool","name":"Play it Cool","text":"This is meant for those 5:30 AM workouts where there aren't many cars driving by (but some). Anytime some sees a car drive by, they shout \"Play it cool!\" and you stop what you're doing and hold a squat while pretending to read the paper. Once the car leaves, you resume what you were doing.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["lower"],"equipment":[],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-poker-chips","name":"Poker Chips","text":"Moving an 8x8x16 concrete block forward one parking space at a time, shifting right/left and moving the next chip/block forward. At the last chip, cycle back to the front of the line. Exercise goes the length of parking lot or until the PAX yields.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["heavy"],"equipment":["coupon"],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-pole-dancing","name":"Pole Dancing","text":"Lay on your 6 under a handrail, parallel to the rail, grab rail with both hands and pull yourself up alternating sides. For extra effort, wrap your legs around the rail.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["lower"],"equipment":[],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-pop-up-merkins","name":"Pop-up Merkins","text":"Merkin in which a powerful push from arms and toes causes all fours to leave the ground to complete the upward motion. Resembles a hopping cricket and inspires #respect for its bug-sized athleticism.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["upper"],"equipment":[],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-popeye-carry","name":"Popeye Carry","text":"A variation of the Coupon Carry (transportation) to torch the forearms. Carry the coupon by the center cross section as a transportation in between exercise stations. It will feel like you are pinching the center section with your thumbs and four fingers. Carry until forearm burnout/exhaustion. Alternate the carry between the left and right hands so that you don’t end up lop sided.","kind":"thang","emphasis":["heavy","upper"],"equipment":["coupon"],"tags":["routine"]},{"id":"x-popeye-punches","name":"Popeye Punches","text":"This is a warm up for the shoulders. Starting position is feet shoulder width apart, knees slightly bent, fists clenched at hips. Exercise is four count, with exaggerated, alternating right and left punches over the same side shoulder. (Alternatively, punches may be executed over each opposite shoulder, diagonally.)","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["upper"],"equipment":[],"tags":["warmup"]},{"id":"x-post-hole-diggers","name":"Post Hole Diggers","text":"Using your log, pole, post, etc. (Fault Line has two-man poles) stand it on its end and squat and lift using your legs, shoulders and arms to lift the pole until your arms are extended over head. Then reverse the upper body portion to bring the pole down. That's one rep! This is a great full body exercise when done correctly.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["lower","upper"],"equipment":[],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-power-merkin","name":"Power Merkin","text":"Power Merkin Merkin performed with your planking partner''s feet up on your back. The bigger your partner, the more power required to complete the merkin.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["core","upper"],"equipment":[],"tags":["mary","partner"]},{"id":"x-prayer-squat","name":"Prayer Squat","text":"A body-weight squat performed with hands clasped in front of your chest. Just like a goblet squat with a dumbbell, just without the dumbbell.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["heavy","lower","upper"],"equipment":["weights"],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-preposturous","name":"Preposturous","text":"Stand with back, butt, head, shoulders, elbows, and backs of wrists pressed against a wall, feet slightly forward. Start with arms in a “W” (elbows bent ~90°). Keeping every point in full contact with the wall, slowly raise arms into a “Y” (or overhead) position, then lower back to “W.”\nQ Tip: Because bad posture is preposterous. Call in sets of 5 (slow) or 20 (pulses). Pairs great with Back Widows, Prone T-Raises, and Supermans.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["upper"],"equipment":["bench_wall"],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-pretzel-crunch","name":"Pretzel Crunch","text":"Start on your six with legs bent, heels on the ground. Lift your left leg and put your left foot on your right knee. Put your left arm out straight and your right arm bent behind your head. In cadence, bring right elbow to left knee, then back down. Flapjack and repeato.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["cardio","core","lower","upper"],"equipment":[],"tags":["mary"]},{"id":"x-pretzel-stick","name":"Pretzel Stick","text":"Similar to the pretzel crunch, but more painful. This time start on your six with legs straight out and cross one foot onto the opposite knee. Upper body same as pretzel crunch. When you lift for the crunch move, raise both upper and lower body so that you are again trying to bring one elbow to the opposite knee. Flapjack and repeato. This one hurts!","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["cardio","core","lower"],"equipment":[],"tags":["mary"]},{"id":"x-primate-humper-o-rama","name":"Primate Humper O-Rama","text":"This riff on Moneky Humpers never disappoints. It''s 3-way monkey humpers...Spider Monkey, Chimp Humpers, Gorilla Humpers Spider Monkey Humpers - Standard Monkey Humpers but with feet together. PAX will complain about the family jewels, so expect some MC Chimp Humpers - Standard Monkey Humpers (feet shoulder width apart) Gorilla Humpers - Standard Monkey Humpers but with feet more than shoulder width apart. Start with Spider Monkey Humpers, then Chimp Humpers, then Gorilla Humpers. These are on Q and should be done in rapid succession (no gaps) similar to Bolt 45s. The rep count is up to the Q. 15 seems easy....","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["lower","upper"],"equipment":[],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-prime-time-merkin","name":"Prime Time Merkin","text":"Standard merkin position EXCEPT one leg up, toe off the ground. As PAX are pushing up, switch legs on each rep (in a plyometric fashion). Named after Neon Deion Sanders, and his celebratory shuffle to the end zone on breakaway runs.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["cardio","lower","upper"],"equipment":["field"],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-princess-tea-party","name":"Princess Tea Party","text":"PAX grab a partner and form two rows with partners facing each other in plank position. Partners do Pattycake Merkins for set number of reps, followed by a Partner People's Chair (Back to back wall sit) for set time. Rinse and repeat as necessary.","kind":"thang","emphasis":["core","lower","upper"],"equipment":["bench_wall"],"tags":["partner","routine"]},{"id":"x-prisoner-cell-merkin-burpees-aka-pcmbs","name":"Prisoner Cell Merkin Burpees aka PCMBs.","text":"Drop to Plank, do 1 Merkin then bring your right knee in and back, do 1 Merkin then bring your left knee in and back, do 1 Merkin then bring both feet in and jump up = 1 PCMB complete. Try 10 of these. You''ll wish you stopped at 5.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["cardio","core","lower","upper"],"equipment":[],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-prisoner-indian-run","name":"Prisoner Indian Run","text":"Standard Indian Run, but with your hands behind your head and elbows out in the \"peacock position\". Great mumble chatter reducer!","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["cardio","run"],"equipment":[],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-prisoner-s-squat","name":"Prisoner's Squat","text":"Body-weight squat performed with hands on your head or laced behind your head.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["heavy","lower"],"equipment":["weights"],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-protractor","name":"Protractor","text":"While on six, Q calls out various angles to hold legs at, such as 10, 30, 45, 90 degrees. Regular way is to hold legs together but Q may call split or 3 dimensional where legs are held at the angle called but apart.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["lower"],"equipment":[],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-proud-mary","name":"Proud Mary","text":"Proud Mary Performed to \"Proud Mary\" by Creedence Clearwater Revival. Perform Big Boy Situps until ''Rolling'', switch to Gas Pumps for each \"Rolling\", then to Flutter kick after \"Rolling\", then back to Gas Pumps during \"Rolling\", then back to Big Boy Situps. Repeat til song ends.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["core"],"equipment":["speaker"],"tags":["mary"]},{"id":"x-pseudo-planche-merkins","name":"Pseudo Planche Merkins","text":"Start in standard push-up position turning you hands until your fingers point to the toes. Next walk your feet up until you feel you are about to teeter over. Hands are as close to the belly as you can get. Perform 'Merkins. Great Bicep exercise.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["upper"],"equipment":[],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-pull-up-squats","name":"Pull-up Squats","text":"Do one pull-up. Drop down, squat once, then repeat. (Thanks Tiny Dancer in Swamp Rabbit.)","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["lower","upper"],"equipment":["pull_up_bar"],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-pullerama","name":"Pullerama","text":"A pull-up routine of no specific composition.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["upper"],"equipment":["pull_up_bar"],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-pump-jack","name":"Pump Jack","text":"Pax pair up and get in plank position. The Q chooses a number of merkins (we use 5) per set. Pax 1 does 5 merkins while pax 2 planks, then switch. Continue alternating merkins and planking until one pax in the pair reaches merkin failure. After failure each pair gets up and lunge walks in circles around the other pax pairs until the last team reaches failure. The pairs must encourage and push each other and then encourage others while lunge walking. Last team to fail wins. Named pump jack because all the pax going up and down during merkins looks like a field full of oil wells with pump jacks, and you are pumped when it is over. Proper merkin form must be used by all. With an uneven number of pax the Q does merkins on his own.","kind":"thang","emphasis":["core","lower","upper"],"equipment":["field"],"tags":["routine","team"]},{"id":"x-punch-up-merkin","name":"Punch-up Merkin","text":"In typical Merkin position go down and back up, then punch straight out, to the side, or up (for a real burn) 10 times with right arm. Do another merkin and repeat with left arm. Best done OYO or during a circuit routine.","kind":"thang","emphasis":["upper"],"equipment":[],"tags":["routine"]},{"id":"x-pure-burn","name":"Pure BURN","text":"1. Face a wall, fence....anything that you can hold onto; 2. Get in the squat position 3/4 up while holding the fence; 3. On the balls of your feet (tip toes); 4. Pulse 3/4 down to 1/2 (90 degrees) X 10; 5. Pulse 1/2 all the way down X10. Repeat until PAX complains... it wont take long.","kind":"thang","emphasis":["lower"],"equipment":["bench_wall"],"tags":["routine"]},{"id":"x-pusherama","name":"Pusherama","text":"A chest routine of no specific composition, done to TBQ.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["upper"],"equipment":[],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-quadraphilia","name":"Quadraphilia","text":"Find a steep hill (Hill of pain). Set a timer, i.e. 4 minutes. Run forward down the hill and run backwards up the hill repeato until the timer runs out.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["cardio","lower","run"],"equipment":["timer"],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-quarter-pounder","name":"Quarter Pounder","text":"Done on a Football field or a large parking lot. Sprint to the 25 yards and Do 25 merkins, Run backwards to Goal And Sprint to the 50 and do 50 squats, Backwards to Goal Line sprint to the 75 and do 75 Mountain Climbers, Run backwards to the goal line and sprint to the hundred and do 100 SSH. mix and match exercises for the reps. Do it with a Bricks for a Quarter Pounder with cheese. Rinse and repeat for a Double Quarter Pounder.","kind":"thang","emphasis":["cardio","core","lower","run","upper"],"equipment":["field"],"tags":["routine"]},{"id":"x-racoon-crawl","name":"Racoon Crawl","text":"Narrow-grip crawl done along the top of a short wall or stadium bench.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["upper"],"equipment":["bench_wall"],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-railroad-tracks","name":"Railroad Tracks","text":"The twisted sister of the Indian Run. Pax start in single file line. First pax drops to low plank, second pax jumps over first pax runs 5 yards and gets in low plank. Third pax jumps over both pax runs 5 yards and gets in low plank. After all pax have gone, the first pax jumps over all the pax and returns to low plank. This is continued until the destination is reached. The name derived from the pax looking like Railroad ties as you continuously hop over one another.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["cardio","core","lower","run"],"equipment":["field"],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-railroaders","name":"Railroaders","text":"One or more railroad ties needed. Split into 2-3 people per group. Each group takes turns on the railroad ties. 1st Round - Each group performs 20 overhead presses, while everyone else planks. 2nd Round - Each group performs 20 curls, while everyone else holds Al Gore. 3rd Round - Each group performs 20 dips, while everyone else performs flutter kicks. 4th Round - Each group performs 20 bent over rows, while everyone else lunges. Rinse & repeat as needed or change out exercises and reps as needed.","kind":"thang","emphasis":["core","lower","upper"],"equipment":[],"tags":["mary","routine"]},{"id":"x-rampage","name":"Rampage","text":"Performed at nearest hill or stairs. Starting at top, perform exercise of choice with X amount of reps. Once complete, bear crawl down the hill/stairs. At bottom, perform exercise of choice with X amount of reps. Once complete, crawl bear up the hill/stairs to the top. Down/up = 1 round. No limits on Q's choice of rounds.","kind":"thang","emphasis":[],"equipment":["stairs"],"tags":["routine"]},{"id":"x-randorama","name":"Randorama","text":"A series of completely unrelated and seemingly disjointed exercises done at an exhaustively rapid pace.","kind":"thang","emphasis":[],"equipment":[],"tags":["routine"]},{"id":"x-randys","name":"Randys","text":"You've seen A Christmas story, poor Randy can't put his arms down. With arms straight out but with palms face down, move arms up and down 6 to 12 inches in cadence. Best used following Moroccan night clubs or similar shoulder exercise i.e. overhead claps, Jack Webb's.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["cardio","upper"],"equipment":[],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-ranger-merkins","name":"Ranger Merkins","text":"Merkin position - however, your hands should be placed back more in line with your rib cage instead of your shoulders.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["upper"],"equipment":[],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-rapid-fire-rock-set","name":"Rapid Fire Rock Set","text":"Grab exercise rock. Exercises done in civilian cadence with Q calling up or down and PAX calling number. Do exercise to predetermined number (15 or 20 is good). No rest between sets. Example is curl, tri extension, overhead press done twice. Can follow press with overhead hold.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["upper"],"equipment":[],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-red-bull-smurf-jack","name":"Red Bull Smurf Jack","text":"Same as the standard smurf jack, except high-tempo cadence at 2 or 3 times the speed of a normal cadence. Always done in cadence, no less than 20. 20 is challenging, 30 will take your breath away, and 40 would be a very high level of achievement. Heart rate spikes, so be mindful of what the PAX can handle.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":[],"equipment":[],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-redrum","name":"Redrum","text":"Redrum Murder Bunny up a hill, 10 Blockees at top, Rifle Carry down","kind":"exercise","emphasis":[],"equipment":[],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-redrum-bunnies","name":"Redrum Bunnies","text":"Redrum Bunnies Similar to the way a bear crawl backwards is a crawl bear, a redrum bunny is the reverse of a murder bunny.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":[],"equipment":[],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-reverse-crunch","name":"Reverse Crunch","text":"Same position as LBC. Head and back stay on the ground. Bring knees to chest to work lower abs.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["cardio","core","upper"],"equipment":[],"tags":["mary"]},{"id":"x-richard-petty","name":"Richard Petty","text":"Hold coupon in both hands with arms at a 90 degree angle in a static bicep curl, and walk a specified distance.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["heavy","upper"],"equipment":["coupon"],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-richard-simmons","name":"Richard Simmons","text":"A core and shoulder stretch and warmup that resembles a move by the iconic 1980's Sweatin' to the Oldies fitness guru.\nIn standing position, start with arms raised and bent so your thumbs are touching the tops of your shoulders. Bend to your left at your waist and extend your right arm over your head, stretching your right oblique. Return to starting position and repeat in opposite direction. Repeat back and forth in a 4-count cadence. 1 (bend left), 2 (return to start), 3 (bend right), 4 (return to start).","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["core","mobility","upper"],"equipment":[],"tags":["warmup"]},{"id":"x-robert-plants","name":"Robert Plants","text":"Running up a stairway, often in a urine-stinking parking garage.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["cardio","run"],"equipment":[],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-rochamburpees","name":"Rochamburpees","text":"Choose a partner. Both in chillcut plank position. Play Rochambeau (rock, paper, scissors) while in chillcut. Round 1: loser does 1 Burpee, winner does 1 Merkin. Stay in chillcut and play 10 total rounds, adding an additional Burpee/Merkin every round. EC: every tie, both do a Merkin.","kind":"thang","emphasis":["cardio","core","upper"],"equipment":[],"tags":["competitive","game","partner","routine"]},{"id":"x-rock-a-bye-baby","name":"Rock-a-bye Baby","text":"People's chair with a rock, block or any other heavy object. Chair position, starting with the heavy object over your head, bring down to chest, push object straight out (chest high) and then left to right (1 each) for russian twist, bring back to starting position over head. Repeat until Q sees fit.","kind":"thang","emphasis":["heavy","upper"],"equipment":["coupon"],"tags":["routine"]},{"id":"x-rock-ee","name":"Rock-ee","text":"A burpee with a rock. Invented during Saturday workouts at Pullen Park in Raleigh. Drop down with rock for burpee, leaving hands on the rock on the ground for the push-up and then lifting the rock overhead for finishing part of the burpee. Repeat.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["cardio","upper"],"equipment":[],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-rocket-merkins","name":"Rocket Merkins","text":"Similar to a regular 4-count Merkin, where counts 1-3 are in a slow downward motion. Then, on count 3, you explode upward with your hands coming off the ground for count 4.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["upper"],"equipment":[],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-rocket-squats","name":"Rocket Squats","text":"With your arms behind your back, squat down beyond 90 degrees at the knees, then rapidly jump up into the air. Based on the movie, Rocket Man.\nWorks well with a 4-count cadence.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["lower","upper"],"equipment":[],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-rockette-dips","name":"Rockette Dips","text":"Perform dips with alternating leg kick at the nadir of the dip.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["lower","upper"],"equipment":[],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-rockette-hillbillies","name":"Rockette Hillbillies","text":"As in Hillbillies, bring a knee up to elbow on same side of body (e.g. left knee to left elbow), set the foot down, then follow it by a high kick with the same leg. Repeat with the next leg.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["lower"],"equipment":[],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-rocking-chairs","name":"Rocking Chairs","text":"Imagine Grandma and Grandpa sipping sweet tea and rocking the summer day away on their front porch. Hold coupon above head and rock it back and forth with a four count. Rock until arms burn.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["heavy","upper"],"equipment":["coupon"],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-rocks-up","name":"Rocks Up","text":"Modified Homer to Marge - while on back with feet flat on ground raise hips so that only feet and shoulders are touching the ground. In unison, raise hips and the rock to overhead position [through tricep extension from ground position to overhead]. All rocks are then lowered back towards ground. Repeat.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["upper"],"equipment":[],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-rocky-balboa","name":"Rocky Balboa","text":"AKA curb kick or Riverdance. Start near a curb or other raised element, and with a barely rhythmic motion, alternately tap the toe from each foot on the curb. Best in cadence, as in the extensive exercise scene between Rocky and Drago in Rocky IV.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":[],"equipment":["bench_wall"],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-romanian-deadlift","name":"Romanian Deadlift","text":"Holding a coupon, extend your arms straight, down below your belt line. Then, keeping your legs and back straight, hinge your hips and bend down as far as you can go, then come back up. You should feel a strain in the legs. These are good in high reps to get that lower back burning!","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["heavy","lower","upper"],"equipment":["coupon"],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-rosalita","name":"Rosalita","text":"Ab exercise done laying on back, legs raised to 90 degrees. Keeping legs perpendicular to ground, separate legs outward then return to start.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["lower"],"equipment":[],"tags":["mary"]},{"id":"x-rosalita-wip","name":"Rosalita Wip","text":"Ab exercise from Rosalita position. Legs together at 90 degrees. Cadence count. Out for 1, together for 2, legs down to 6 inches for 3, back to 90 degrees for count. Burns more when done slow.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["lower"],"equipment":[],"tags":["mary"]},{"id":"x-route-66","name":"Route 66","text":"Made infamous along Water Oak Road in Charlotte, an exercise in which you start with 1 rep at a predefined stopping point, then add one additional rep at intervals until you hit 11 stops. Example: Route 66 along the light posts starts you with 1 exercise, like a burpee, at the first light pole. Then do 2 at the next, 3 at the third, etc. until you reach 11 light posts / 11 burpees. The sum total of all reps is 66.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["cardio"],"equipment":["timer"],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-rowboat","name":"Rowboat","text":"Hold 6in with your torso raised slightly and your hands raised at your sides. Bend knees towards your body and arms towards your chest. Like rowing the oars of a boat. Done IC; 1-Bend knees towards body and move arms like rowing a boat 2-Return to 6in 3-perform rowing motion again 4-return to 6in.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["upper"],"equipment":[],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-roxanne","name":"Roxanne","text":"Roxanne The Q plays \"Roxanne\" by The Police. While staying in the plank position for the entire song, perform a merkin at every \"Roxanne\" (26 times total) and a plank jack at every \"red light\" sung (26 times total). Alternatively, while running in place at a high cadence for the entire song, perform a burpee at every \"Roxanne.\"","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["cardio","core","run","upper"],"equipment":["speaker"],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-ruck-hammer","name":"Ruck Hammer","text":"A rotational core exercise performed with a weighted rucksack instead of a traditional weight plate or coupon. Sit on your six with legs extended in front of you (or feet raised for added difficulty), hold the rucksack with both hands, and rotate your torso from side to side, tapping the ruck on the ground beside your hips in a sweeping motion. The movement resembles swinging a sledgehammer, hence the name. This exercise builds rotational core strength, oblique endurance, and grip strength. Modify the ruck weight as needed to maintain proper form throughout the set.","kind":"thang","emphasis":["core","heavy","lower","ruck"],"equipment":["coupon","ruck","weights"],"tags":["mary","routine"]},{"id":"x-rucking-bricks","name":"Rucking Bricks","text":"A versatile rucking variation where you carry bricks in your rucksack and use them for various exercises during your workout. The bricks serve dual purposes: adding weight to your ruck for the march/walk portions, and functioning as portable workout equipment that can be quickly pulled out for strength exercises like presses, rows, curls, or other movements. This setup gives the Q flexibility to seamlessly transition between cardio/endurance rucking and strength training evolutions without needing additional equipment. Simply stow the bricks back in the ruck when returning to movement","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["heavy","mobility","ruck","upper"],"equipment":["ruck","weights"],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-run-dmc","name":"Run DMC","text":"Similar to the @DMC , but with an added run. Best on a football field, but can be done with any designated points or posts.\nFrom the goal line, 50-yard sprint to the 50-yard line. Then, Duck Walk to the 40-yard line, do 5 Merkins, Reverse Bear Crawl back to the 50-yard line. Followed by a run back to the starting goal line. Repeat with a run to the 50-yardline, then Duckwalk to the 30, 20, 10, and opposite goal lines, increasing # of Merkins by 5. Reverse Bear Crawl back to the 50-yardline, then run back to the starting goal line.\nRun-Duckwalk-Merkin-Reverse Bear Crawl-Run.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["cardio","run","upper"],"equipment":["field"],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-runaway","name":"Runaway","text":"A musical beatdown set to Kanye West’s Runaway. Perform one rep of an exercise on every piano note. Continue the same exercise until failure or until you fall off tempo.\nRotate exercises in the following order:\nMerkins → Air Squats → Big Boi Sit-ups\nContinue cycling through the rotation until the song ends.\nThere are about 750 beats in this 9 minute song.\nYou won’t beat the song… the song beats you.\nOptional:\nAdd Burpees for increased difficulty (for the truly deranged). Modify exercises as needed.","kind":"thang","emphasis":["cardio","core","lower","upper"],"equipment":["speaker"],"tags":["routine"]},{"id":"x-runny-joggy","name":"Runny-Joggy","text":"Single-file line of runners in which the last guy runs to the front. Rinse, repeat. Also known as Swedish Mile, Geese Run, and Indian Run","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["cardio","run"],"equipment":[],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-russian-dips","name":"Russian Dips","text":"Like a regular dip, extending one leg at a time on each down dip - Cossack-style. 1 rep: down with left leg extended, back up, down with right leg extended, back up. For solid back and shoulder burn do minimum 30-40 rapidly IC (4-count).","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["lower","upper"],"equipment":[],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-russies","name":"Russies","text":"Named after Russdiculous (F3 Louisville), a close/narrow stance squat with your hands on your knees. Pax should look like they are posing for a sorority group pic once down in the squat position.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["lower","upper"],"equipment":[],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-san-antonio-shuffle","name":"San Antonio Shuffle","text":"Left Leg Lunge, Right Leg Lunge, Burpee, Plankjack.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["cardio","core","lower"],"equipment":[],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-sandbag-is-friend","name":"Sandbag is Friend","text":"On a track works best. 50lbs bag In a circle pass the sandbag to the right in unison squats. 4x around Single file run with the sandbag. Twice through In a circle pass the sandbag to the right in unison American Hammers. 3x around. Single file right arm farmers carry run with the sandbag. Twice through In a circle merkin position, slide the bag across to the right after the up position. 2x around In a circle merkin position, slide the bag across to the left after the up position. 2x around Single file left arm farmers carry run with the sandbag. Twice through In a circle pass the sandbag to the left in unison American Hammers. 3x around. Single file run with the sandbag. Twice through In a circle pass the sandbag to the left in unison squats. 4x around You will never want to touch sandbag again","kind":"thang","emphasis":["cardio","core","heavy","lower","run","upper"],"equipment":["field","sandbag"],"tags":["mary","routine"]},{"id":"x-sandstorm","name":"Sandstorm","text":"Just as the Gamecock defense gets excited on 3rd down, pax jump continuously with arms overhead for 1 minute.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["lower","upper"],"equipment":[],"tags":["game"]},{"id":"x-santa-s-ladder","name":"Santa's Ladder","text":"Pick a spot in the distance. Run from your starting point to that spot and do 10 Burpees. Return to start. Turnaround, run back to your spot, now do 9 Burpees. Continue this running and rep routine, downward counting through to completing 6 burpees. Then, as you hit the 5-1 count reps, do Merkins instead of Burpees. After the entire 10-1 set is over, pause. Make it appear you're done. Then announce that you're reversing the order. In this new set, now you start with Merkins as your 10-6 set and finish with Burpees as 5-1. This routine started when a Jacob's Ladder was about to occur, and the Q asked since we were going to 10, which would the PAX prefer - Merkins or Burpees? Santa answered he''d like to split halfway, so the Q obliged. Then the Q announced uneven gains required doing it again in reverse. If executed properly -- with the thought it's only a single 10-1 set -- it's even more of a real crowd pleaser.","kind":"thang","emphasis":["cardio","run","upper"],"equipment":[],"tags":["routine"]},{"id":"x-sauron-s-ladder","name":"Sauron's Ladder","text":"A challenging workout routine, based on @Elevens.\nAt the base of a steep hill or stairway, start with one Blockie.\nRun to the top of the hill or stairway, do 10 Burpees.\nRun back to the bottom for two Blockies.\nThen back to the top for 9 Burpees.\nRinse and Repeat to 10 Blockies and 1 Burpee.\nPAX who finish early head back down the other side of the ladder.","kind":"thang","emphasis":["cardio","run"],"equipment":[],"tags":["routine"]},{"id":"x-scissor-lifts","name":"Scissor Lifts","text":"Start in a high plank hold, then transition to a low plank. Cross your arms in front of you, then do a Merkin from your fore arms. Once fully extended your arms look like the beams of a Scissor Lift when it is fully extended.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["core","upper"],"equipment":[],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-scissor-me-janets","name":"Scissor Me Janets","text":"Partner up. One HIM starts in a high side plank. His partner holds the top leg elevated. The HIM in the plank raises his bottom leg upward to meet the held leg, then lowers it back to the ground (1 rep). Perform in cadence or OYO for reps, then switch sides and roles.","kind":"thang","emphasis":["core","lower"],"equipment":[],"tags":["partner","routine"]},{"id":"x-scorpion-dry-dock","name":"Scorpion Dry Dock","text":"A variation of the Carolina Dry Dock where one leg is hoisted in the air, higher than your six. Perform a specified number of reps, then switch legs. For reference, a Carolina Dry Dock is a modified push-up where you bend only your elbows, lowering your head toward your hands without lowering your six.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["lower","upper"],"equipment":[],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-scout-run","name":"Scout Run","text":"Scout Run Same basic idea as an apache or Indian run. Pax form a line and set a decent to slow pace. The front man takes off forward in a sprint to a self decided time or landmark and then turns around and sprints back to rejoin the pax at the back of the line.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["cardio","run"],"equipment":[],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-scrum-pointers","name":"Scrum Pointers","text":"Method:\nLie supine with the soles of both feet flat on a wall, knees bent to roughly 90 degrees, arms flat at your sides. Drive the heels into the wall and raise the hips until the body forms a straight line from knees to shoulders. Pause at the top, lower under control until the six is just off the deck, and repeat. Can be used as a beatdown finisher in cadence.\nOrigin:\nNamed for F3 Blue Ridge's Scrum, who modified a set of burpees into this considerably more restful movement.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["cardio","upper"],"equipment":["bench_wall"],"tags":["finisher"]},{"id":"x-seal-crawl","name":"Seal Crawl","text":"Bear crawl using only your arms. Drag your feet like a seal's flipper!","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["upper"],"equipment":[],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-seal-jacks","name":"Seal Jacks","text":"Side-straddle hop but with arms in front instead of overhead.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["upper"],"equipment":[],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-shehateme","name":"SheHateMe","text":"10 Lunges (20 movements)/10 Burps (Burpees without the pushup and the standing)/10 Pushups. No rest, as many sets as you can, for as long as the QIC deems necessary.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["cardio","lower","upper"],"equipment":[],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-sheriff-woody","name":"Sheriff Woody","text":"“Reach for the Sky”\nUtilized primarily as an addition to squats or other exercises during the warm-up phase.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["lower","upper"],"equipment":[],"tags":["warmup"]},{"id":"x-shoots-and-ladders","name":"Shoots and Ladders","text":"This exercise is best performed on a basketball court. Create a list of ''ladders'' beforehand and use a basketball and have the PAX ''shoot'' to determine the type of ladder that will be performed. Suggested ladder options: merkin, burpee, suicide, flutterkick, sweat angels, squats, etc. Variants to the run portion of the ladder can include sprints, lunge walks, bear crawls, backwards runs, etc.","kind":"thang","emphasis":["cardio","core","lower","run","upper"],"equipment":[],"tags":["mary","routine"]},{"id":"x-shortcake-special","name":"Shortcake Special","text":"A gathering of Pax prior to any bootcamp, for an out and back run of various times and or lengths.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["cardio","run"],"equipment":[],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-shortie-squats","name":"Shortie Squats","text":"Pick up your 2.0, put them over your shoulder in a fireman carry position, perform a standard partner squat. Useful for waking sleepy 2.0s. For next level, and if a HIM has multiple shorties, see how many he can pick up and squat at the same time.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["lower","upper"],"equipment":[],"tags":["partner"]},{"id":"x-shots-fired-moment-of-zen","name":"Shots Fired! Moment of Zen","text":"Take a meditation pose and go through a guided meditation, focusing on breathing and things to be thankful for, for 1 minute. Q decides a good point, typically at the end of the BD. Our boy Shots found Buddhism and has shared how to strengthen our minds with our body. An inspiration to all, never yield!","kind":"exercise","emphasis":[],"equipment":[],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-shoulder-blaster-special","name":"Shoulder Blaster Special","text":"Set of shoulder exercises done without rest, in cadence, and reps are at Q's discretion. Exercises are as follows in this order: Baby Arm Circles, Reverse Baby Arm Circles, Moroccan Night Club, Bent Arm Moroccan Night Club, Chinooks, Shoulder Press, Seal Claps, Overhead Claps, Albatross (wing flaps), Cherry Pickers, and Cherry on Top (Hold at 45 Degree Angle in cadence.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["cardio","upper"],"equipment":[],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-side-straddle-burpkin","name":"Side Straddle Burpkin","text":"Side Straddle Burpkins\nBurpee but replace hop w/ SSH. Increase merkin by one each down and increase SSH by one each hop. Do this up to the number called by Q","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["cardio","upper"],"equipment":[],"tags":["warmup"]},{"id":"x-side-straddle-hop","name":"Side Straddle Hop","text":"AKA Jumping Jack. A classic full-body cardio exercise performed by jumping your feet out to the sides while simultaneously raising your arms overhead, then jumping back to the starting position with feet together and arms at your sides. This simple but effective movement elevates heart rate, warms up the body, improves coordination, and engages the shoulders, legs, and core. Jumping jacks are a staple warm-up exercise and can also be used for cardio intervals or active recovery between strength movements","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["cardio","core","lower","upper"],"equipment":["timer"],"tags":["warmup"]},{"id":"x-side-straddle-hop-burpees","name":"Side Straddle Hop Burpees","text":"Perform 5 Side-Straddle Hops in cadence, then drop and do 2 Burpees. Once you are finished with Burpees, continue Side-Straddle Hops in cadence. Normally done in F3 Columbia in sets of 25.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["cardio"],"equipment":[],"tags":["warmup"]},{"id":"x-side-straddle-hop-jumps","name":"Side Straddle Hop Jumps","text":"This is a side straddle hop beginning in a squat with a jump all in one motion. best done in cadence. Start in Chair position with your hands by your side. One is a jump to split legs with hands and arms up (like the top of the side straddle hop but you are in the air). Two is the landing, back to where you started with a legs together squat (chair position), three is another jump, four is another squat. If you can get to 15 IC then you're killin it.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["lower","upper"],"equipment":[],"tags":["warmup"]},{"id":"x-side-straddle-squats","name":"Side Straddle Squats","text":"This is a side straddle hop while in chair position. Begin in Chair position (a squat with your legs together) and arms to your side. Jump to the squat position with your legs apart and raise your hands up like a side straddle hop while in a squat.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["lower","upper"],"equipment":[],"tags":["warmup"]},{"id":"x-sideways-shoulder-stands","name":"Sideways Shoulder Stands","text":"Progressive Shoulder Stands, incrementing from prone plank or merkin position until gradually holding a near handstand position for maximum TUT.\nExercise is performed typically starting on a curb, then moving feet up a wall or landscaping blocks of a retainer wall; holding at each level at each angle for some allotted time (ex. 10sec count before moving to the next), where finally the PAX are holding their bodies upside down in a headstand (or near so). This is typically 4-6 positions but can be flexed +/- for added or reduced difficulty.\nFor added complexity, the Q can have the PAX come down the wall in reverse, adding 10sec counts until the PAX return to prone merkin position often having the entire PAC count out the last 10 'all together' before recovering up.","kind":"thang","emphasis":["core","upper"],"equipment":["bench_wall"],"tags":["routine"]},{"id":"x-sinatras","name":"Sinatras","text":"This is a mix of a Leg Raise and @Dolly. Begin laying on your back with your feet six inches off the ground counts 1 and 2 are raising your legs to 90-degrees and back to 6 inches followed by counts 3 and 4 keeping legs parallel to ground, separate legs outward then return to start.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["core","lower"],"equipment":[],"tags":["mary"]},{"id":"x-single-arm-row","name":"Single Arm Row","text":"A unilateral pulling exercise where you row a weight (coupon, dumbbell, or kettlebell) toward your hip while supporting yourself with the opposite hand. Start in a staggered stance or bent-over position with one hand braced on a stable surface. Pull the weight up toward your hip, keeping your elbow close to your body and squeezing your shoulder blade back at the top of the movement. Lower with control and repeat. This exercise builds back strength, improves muscular imbalances, and engages the core for stability","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["core","heavy","upper"],"equipment":["coupon","weights"],"tags":["competitive","game"]},{"id":"x-single-leg-pickle-pusher","name":"Single Leg Pickle Pusher","text":"In the @Pretzel Crunch position, execute a Pickle Pusher. Flapjack.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["cardio","core","lower"],"equipment":[],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-singlet-merkin","name":"Singlet Merkin","text":"6-count merkin. 4 counts are a Makhtar N''diaye. The other 2 are a standard merkin.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["upper"],"equipment":[],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-sit-up-scuttle","name":"Sit up & Scuttle","text":"Start with a situp with a block. On the up you need to chuck that block as far as you can. Then you crab walk to where your block landed and repeat","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["core","heavy"],"equipment":["coupon"],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-six-minutes-of-mary","name":"Six Minutes Of Mary","text":"aka 6MOM An abdominal #Routine of no specific composition as long as it promotes #TBQ. ''Inspired by psycho-killer with the 7-minute ab workout in the movie, Something About Mary.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":[],"equipment":[],"tags":["mary"]},{"id":"x-six-minutes-of-uncle","name":"Six Minutes of Uncle","text":"A cousin of Six minutes of Mary. A pull up #Routine of no specific composition that like it's cousin will promote #TBQ. Some goods ones include: pull-ups, chin-ups, Panseys, hanging leg lifts, and Mexican Jumping Beans. By the end of six minutes the PAX will be crying UNCLE to the QIC.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["core","lower","upper"],"equipment":["pull_up_bar"],"tags":["mary"]},{"id":"x-six-pack","name":"Six Pack","text":"1 pull-up, 5 merkins (11's style but with 6's). Once at 5 pull-ups 1 merkin, go back down to 1 pull-up, 5 merkins.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["upper"],"equipment":["pull_up_bar"],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-sixty-second-arm-circles-aka-ssacs","name":"Sixty Second Arm Circles aka SSACs","text":"aka SSACs Start in T Plank (left arm up) 15 IC roll to back for LBCs 15 IC roll to T Plank(right arm up) 15 IC roll to back for merkin 15 IC More than 60 seconds but catchy name","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["core","upper"],"equipment":[],"tags":["mary","warmup"]},{"id":"x-slaughter-starter","name":"Slaughter Starter","text":"20 burpees OYO in the AO parking lot before any other exercises or running is completed.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["cardio","run"],"equipment":[],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-sleep-walkers-123","name":"Sleep Walkers 123","text":"3 part Routine. Start with 1 Squat, 2 Toe Touches (each leg 1), 3 Lunges. Then increase in the same ratio (2 squats, 4 toe touches, 6 lunges, etc.) upward to 10 squats, or number of your choosing.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["lower"],"equipment":[],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-sleeping-bunny","name":"Sleeping Bunny","text":"Murder Bunny exercise performed in a ZigZag route. Murder Bunny out \"X\" distance set by Q, rotate body and cindy 45 degrees, Murder Bunny out \"X\" distance set by Q, rotate body and Cindy opposite 45 degrees. Rinse and Repeat.","kind":"thang","emphasis":[],"equipment":[],"tags":["routine"]},{"id":"x-sleeping-hillbillies","name":"Sleeping Hillbillies","text":"Lay on either your right or left side - do unilateral Hillbillies with one arm and one leg ... one hand behind your head and same side knee comes up to elbow. Flapjack.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["cardio","lower","upper"],"equipment":[],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-sliders","name":"Sliders","text":"Set your coupon down and high plank with your coupon close to the outside of one hand.\nGrab your coupon with the hand further from the coupon and slide past your opposite shoulder.\nPlant your hand back to high plank with the coupon now to the outside of the other hand.\nRepeat.\nWorks best with Kettle Bell","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["core","heavy","upper"],"equipment":["coupon"],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-slinky","name":"Slinky","text":"Modified bear crawl. In bear crawl position, extend arms out, then pull legs in. Keep legs straight. Do not extend all the way out as in an Inch Worm.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["lower","upper"],"equipment":[],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-slugger","name":"Slugger","text":"Run DMC's: Run a series of laps around the Q as designated. After the first lap, do 20 Diamond Merkins (D); after the second lap, do 20 Merkins (M); after the third lap do 20 Carolina Dry Docks (C) to complete a round. Rinse and Repeat as desired.","kind":"thang","emphasis":["cardio","run","upper"],"equipment":[],"tags":["routine"]},{"id":"x-smurf-jacks","name":"Smurf Jacks","text":"Side straddle hop performed in the squat position. Can be done in cadence or OYO.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["lower"],"equipment":[],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-snapper-burpee","name":"Snapper Burpee","text":"An explosive 6-count burpee variation that combines multiple challenging elements. The sequence: (1) squat down and place hands on ground, (2) jump feet back to plank position, (3) perform a hand-release merkin where you lift hands off the ground and clap at the bottom, (4) perform a standard merkin (push-up), (5) jump feet back to hands, (6) explode into a tuck jump, bringing your knees up toward your chest at the top. This high-intensity movement builds upper body strength, explosive leg power, cardiovascular endurance, and total body conditioning. The combination of hand-release merkin, standard merkin, and tuck jump makes this significantly more challenging than a standard burpee.","kind":"thang","emphasis":["cardio","core","lower","upper"],"equipment":[],"tags":["routine"]},{"id":"x-snapshot","name":"Snapshot","text":"Grab a sandbag (pavers or other beefy coupon possible, but only with wide separation between pax and done on a forgiving surface). Pax line up shoulder to shoulder with generous spacing between. Squat and shot put the weight with both hands. Broad jump forward. Lunge. Pick up sandbag and repeato for 50-100 yards. / Hit your neighbor with the sandbag? 10 burpees OYO then continue. Hit the Q? 20 burpees OYO. The same with a paver? Dial 911. / Named after a submariner's \"oh, damn!\" act of knee-jerk launching a torpedo without looking where it's going.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["cardio","heavy","lower","upper"],"equipment":["coupon","sandbag","weights"],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-sneaky-gorilla","name":"Sneaky Gorilla","text":"Facing the side, drop to a low squat and put knuckles on ground. Kick one leg out to the side in the direction you will be traveling (you'll be in a low lateral lunge). Slide across to a lateral lunge with the other leg straight, keeping knuckles on the ground as you slide. Now spin around 180 degrees, kick the new front leg out to a lateral lunge, slide across, spin, etc. The longer the distance to travel, the greater the burn. Resembles a gorilla trying to tip-toe/sneak into a room.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["lower"],"equipment":[],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-snowflake-plank","name":"Snowflake Plank","text":"A variation of the high plank. Start in high plank with back straight, but bend knees to 90 degree angle, keeping them as close to the ground as possible without touching the ground. Hold for as long as Q deems necessary. Great for obliques. Named Snowflake, because they're ''special'', and for an M named Snowflake that suggested them.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["core","mobility"],"equipment":[],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-snowman-shuffle","name":"Snowman Shuffle","text":"Mosey between pain stations while shaking and extending arms down by your side. Move improves blood flow past unbent elbows. Excellent for recovery between pain stations of repeated arm exercises.","kind":"thang","emphasis":["cardio","upper"],"equipment":[],"tags":["routine"]},{"id":"x-snuffy","name":"Snuffy","text":"Named in honor of our dear Snuffalofagus. While performing a Chinook, the Pax will also simultaneously perform a standing Pickle Pounder.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":[],"equipment":[],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-solo-tesh","name":"Solo Tesh","text":"While standing, begin with the kettlebell in the clean position. Single-arm overhead press the kettlebell and hold for 10 seconds. Return kettlebell to clean position and hold for another 10 seconds. As many reps as desired: repeat with other arm.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["heavy","mobility","upper"],"equipment":["weights"],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-solstice-burpee","name":"Solstice Burpee","text":"A 9-count burpee variation that incorporates stretching and yoga-inspired movements, making it easier and more recovery-focused than a standard burpee. The sequence: (1) squat down and place hands on ground, (2) step or jump feet back to plank, (3) lower fully to the ground, (4) push up into upward dog/cobra stretch, (5) push back into downward dog stretch, (6) extend and hold the downward dog, (7) jump or step feet back to hands, (8) return to squat position, (9) stand up. This 'stretchy burpee' can be used during rest periods, as active recovery, or as a gentler alternative to traditional burpees while still providing full-body movement","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["cardio","core","lower","mobility","upper"],"equipment":[],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-spam","name":"SPAM","text":"Squats\nPull-ups\nAbs\nMer’cans\nDesignate a route of about 100-150 meters to run at the end of each round. Adding in stairs gives a bonus.\nPAX perform as many of each SPAM exercise for 1:30 with no rest in between. Start with 1:30 of Squats then 1:30 of Pull-ups, 1:30 Abs (can decide a specific ab exercise or let PAX choose their own), 1:30 Mer’cans. After completing SPAM they have 1:30 to run the designated route and return. The PAX that make it back before the end of the timer can rest until the next beep and then start over at S. Any straggling PAX will jump back in to the current exercise when they return and continue .\nEach set takes 7:30 for SPAM and the run so you can decide beforehand how many rounds you’d like to do and set your TABATA for the number of sets. 5 sets is 37:30 which is optimal for a complete workout with a disclaimer and warmup.\nSmartWOD Timer is a good free app to use. Set a TABATA timer up as follows:\n5 Rounds\n1:30 Work\n00:00 Rest\n5 Sets\n0 Rest\nReduce sets as desired to use this is a part of your workout alongside other things.","kind":"thang","emphasis":["cardio","core","lower","run","upper"],"equipment":["pull_up_bar","stairs","timer"],"tags":["routine","warmup"]},{"id":"x-spartan","name":"Spartan","text":"PAX line up and sprint 100 yrds, do 10 merkins at the finish and walk back to the start all together. Q starts each sprint race with a verbal call. Continue until you have done 30 x100 yrd sprints and 10x30 = 300 Merkins. PAX will be nursing home walking for several days.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["cardio","run","upper"],"equipment":[],"tags":["competitive","game"]},{"id":"x-spartan-hammer","name":"Spartan Hammer","text":"Spartan Hammer: A four-count core exercise consisting of two @American Hammer L+R, followed by two Toe Taps, right hand to left toe, then left hand to right toe. Feet always off the ground.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["core"],"equipment":[],"tags":["mary"]},{"id":"x-special-merkins","name":"Special Merkins","text":"Named after Special Delivery of Stronghold.\nThis merkin is no cheat.\nHand release at the bottom\nHand release at the top, meaning explode upward. Bonus points if you add a clap but not needed.\nEmphasize full range of motion for those PAX whose merkin range of motion is 2 inches total.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["cardio","mobility","upper"],"equipment":[],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-speed-humpers","name":"Speed Humpers","text":"Speed Humpers 60 seconds straight of Monkey Humpers, as fast as possible. Preferably done in an area with multiple Speed Humps and with signs pointing out said Speed Humps as this is the perfect place to do them.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["lower"],"equipment":[],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-sphinx-merkin","name":"Sphinx Merkin","text":"Start in a low plank with your elbows on the ground, looking like the Sphinx. Push your self up using your triceps only. Your hands should never leave the ground. The merkin is complete when your elbows are locked. Then return to the starting position with your elbows on the ground once agin not moving your hands and using your triceps.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["core","upper"],"equipment":[],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-spiced-rum-squat","name":"Spiced Rum Squat","text":"Spiced Rum Squat Raise one leg and place on a surface 18-24 inches off the ground, think Captain Morgan stance; then perform a squat. Your 6 should touch your raised leg heel for maximum impact. Alternate between left and right leg being raised. Benches and Picnic Table Seats work very well.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["lower"],"equipment":["bench_wall"],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-spiderman-crawl","name":"Spiderman Crawl","text":"Similar to @Peter Parker (and Parker Peter) and a @Bear Crawl combination. It's a low crawl similar to the way Spiderman climbs a wall.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":[],"equipment":["bench_wall"],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-spiderman-merkin","name":"Spiderman Merkin","text":"Starting position in high plank, bring right knee to right elbow and hold. Perform Q's desired number of merkins either IC or OYO. Switch to left side and bring left knee to left elbow and hold. Perform Q's desired number of merkins either IC or OYO.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["core","upper"],"equipment":[],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-sprinkler","name":"Sprinkler","text":"Extend arms straight out in front of the body. Twist arms to one side of the body while raising and twisting the knee and hip the opposite direction. Can be done IC or OYO. Repeat both sides until the Q halts. Like a pretzel, twisting, sprinkler head thingy. Good back and hip stretch. Sound effects optional.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["mobility","upper"],"equipment":[],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-squat-jacks","name":"Squat Jacks","text":"It's an Air Squat, but each time you come up, you jump your feet out wider (like a jumping jack), then return to your original narrow Squat stance to squat again. In cadence: 1 - Squat, 2 - up, 3 - feet out wide, 4 - back to Squat stance. Can be reversed so that you start in a wide stance, Squat, jump to a narrow stance, jump out wide, Squat, repeat.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["cardio","lower","upper"],"equipment":[],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-squat-potato","name":"Squat Potato","text":"Hot potato in squat position. PAX form a circle with everyone facing out. PAX then pass a heavy object around the outside of the circle while in squat position until the Q says halt. Add more objects in depending on the size of the circle.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["lower"],"equipment":[],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-squat-rocket","name":"Squat Rocket","text":"A combination strength exercise using two stacked coupons (cinderblocks, sandbags, etc.) that trains legs, arms, and core simultaneously. Start with two coupons stacked vertically on one side of your body. Drop into a mid-squat position, grab the top coupon, perform a one-arm curl to bring it above waist height, then pass it to the opposite hand and place it down on the other side of your body - all while maintaining the squat position. Repeat with the second coupon to complete the transfer. Once both coupons are stacked on the opposite side, flap-jack (switch sides) and repeat. This exercise builds functional strength, grip endurance, and leg stamina while challenging coordination.","kind":"thang","emphasis":["cardio","core","heavy","lower","upper"],"equipment":["coupon","sandbag"],"tags":["routine"]},{"id":"x-squat-thrust","name":"Squat Thrust","text":"Begin from a standing position. Move hips back and lower the torso to \"sit\" as deeply as possible while maintaining an upright position. Return to a full standing position while also mimicking arms pressing upward as if to thrust weight over your head.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["heavy","lower","upper"],"equipment":["weights"],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-squat-walking-rockette","name":"Squat Walking Rockette","text":"Start in a parallel squat with arms in front and kick your left leg toward your right hand, squat back down, kick your right leg toward your left hand, squat back down and repeat.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["lower","upper"],"equipment":[],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-squat-wall-taps","name":"Squat Wall Taps","text":"Start with your back to a wall… Squat, then twist until you can touch your right hand to the wall behind your left shoulder. Squat again, then twist until you can touch your left hand to the wall behind your right shoulder. Control every rep.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["lower","upper"],"equipment":["bench_wall"],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-squeezer","name":"Squeezer","text":"Similar to the @Juicer , but on your belly.\nAll pax come together in a hugging circle, drop to your 6 and lay back, then roll over prone. Place right ankle over the left ankle of the person to your right. Lift left ankle while the other pax applies downward force with their right. Straight count as along as the Q calls it, then switch ankles and repeat.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":[],"equipment":[],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-squerkin","name":"Squerkin","text":"Two man teams. First man in merkin position with second man behind holding first mans legs at his waist. First man does one merkin with his legs elevated. Second man performs one squat using the body weight of the first man's legs. Begin again for # of reps called by Q.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["heavy","lower","upper"],"equipment":["weights"],"tags":["team"]},{"id":"x-squirrel","name":"Squirrel","text":"Squat + coupon (or sandbag) curl. Done \"on my down\".\nStarting position is the same as a coupon curl. Do a squat getting your legs to 90 degrees while doing a curl. Coupon should come up to chest/face. Elbows will likely touch your knees when you are squatting and at the top position of the curl. Stand back up while lowering coupon to starting position and repeat to desired rep count.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["heavy","lower","upper"],"equipment":["coupon","sandbag"],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-squirrel-splat","name":"Squirrel Splat","text":"military, hand-release merkin + frogger military, hand-release merkin: 1. down 2. arms in cross with chest on ground 3. up frogger 1. Plank in arms outstretched position 2. Jump both legs outside hands 3. Jump back to plank.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["core","lower","mobility","upper"],"equipment":[],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-stagger-merkins","name":"Stagger Merkins","text":"Merkins but with one arm positioned up and away from the body while the other hand is in its regular position.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["upper"],"equipment":[],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-stairbarrows","name":"StairBarrows","text":"Wheelbarrow position - up one flight of stairs. Space permitting the down partner then does 10 Derkins (partner holding legs). Flap Jack if another flight up. If not same partner return down the stairs and flap jack at bottom for another round.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["cardio","lower","upper"],"equipment":["stairs"],"tags":["partner"]},{"id":"x-stairway-to-seven","name":"Stairway to Seven","text":"Obvious derivative of the Robert Plant...At a stadium, wide stairwell or amphitheater, start with 1 Burpee at bottom, 1 incline push-up on first step, run to top, 1 squat on top step, then run back down. Repeat 7 times up increasing reps of each exercise by 1 each time, so you finish with 7 burpees, 7 incline push-ups, run to top, 7 squats at top. Other exercises ascending from 1-7 can be added or substituted, such as supine pull-ups if you have the apparatus available, like a stadium railing.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["cardio","lower","run","upper"],"equipment":["pull_up_bar"],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-star-jack-burpee","name":"Star Jack Burpee","text":"A burpee variation that includes a StarJack instead of the jump at the end. The StarJack is performed by jumping and raising your arms and legs out to your sides, so your body forms an ''X'' in mid-air.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["cardio","lower","upper"],"equipment":[],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-starfish-crunch","name":"Starfish Crunch","text":"The PAX lay spread eagle on their backs, feet just above ground. On count of 1, the PAX crunch at the core bringing the left leg and right arm together, On 2, return to start. On 3, crunch bringing the right leg and left arm together, on 4, return to start. Rinse and repeat many, many times.","kind":"thang","emphasis":["cardio","core","lower","upper"],"equipment":[],"tags":["routine"]},{"id":"x-steel-blades","name":"Steel Blades","text":"The evil twin of Blades of Steel - Laying flat on your back, push your upper body up using your elbows. If you are super BA, you push you six off the ground so you are in a reverse plank on your heels and elbows.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["core"],"equipment":[],"tags":["mary"]},{"id":"x-step-into-the-circle","name":"Step into the Circle","text":"Performed to the song Move by Thousand Foot Krutch, Pax plank up in a circle. Every time the song says move take one plank walk to the left then to the right the next time it says move. Whenever it says Circle the Pax spin in a circle. The progression goes: plank walk right one step, spin in a circle, plank walk left one step. For all the studs out there you can do merkins or plank jacks waiting on the verses, but for most 3 + minutes of plank-walking and spinning in circles is plenty. Great warm-up and will get the sweat dripping and the shoulders burning to start off the workout.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["core","upper"],"equipment":["speaker"],"tags":["warmup"]},{"id":"x-step-ups","name":"Step Ups","text":"On a low wall, raise each leg one at a time up on the wall. Sometimes the second leg can be brought up to the chest before placing on wall. Often times done in a ladder along with another exercise.","kind":"thang","emphasis":["lower","upper"],"equipment":["bench_wall"],"tags":["routine"]},{"id":"x-steve-earle","name":"Steve Earle","text":"Starting position is standing w/hands behind your head. In four-count cadence, perform Copperhead Squat with a Hillbilly thrown in on the 4th count of the cadence.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["lower","upper"],"equipment":[],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-still-c-a-l-v-e-s","name":"Still C.A.L.V.E.S.","text":"Play Dr. Dre's \"Still D.R.E.\"\nUse a curb, cindy, or just the ground for Calf Raises. Pulse the raises to the piano beat. Do not let heels touch the ground if possible.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["lower"],"equipment":["bench_wall"],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-stink-b-o-m-b-s","name":"Stink B.O.M.B.S.","text":"B.O.M.B.S. x 2 on reps + use a spoke layout. Set 5 cones out surrounding the Shovel Flag. Pax #1 starts the B.O.M.B.S. reps at the first cone while pax #2 goes to the Shovel Flag to do exercise chosen by the Q (for example 50 curls or 50 LBC's). Pax #2 then swaps with Pax #1. Work at same spoke until all reps are completed. Then move to next spoke. Q can change center exercise with each move to next spoke. B.O.M.B.S = 100 Burpees, 200 Over Head Presses, 300 Merkins, 400 Big Boy Sit-ups, 500 Squats.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["cardio","core","lower","upper"],"equipment":["cones"],"tags":["mary"]},{"id":"x-stirkin","name":"Stirkin","text":"Steps ups, one each leg, then irkin using same surface as used for the stepups","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["lower"],"equipment":["stairs"],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-stump-huggers","name":"Stump Huggers","text":"Start out in the bear crawl position hold in a plank. Come down to elbow (plank) on left arm then right, then up to hands.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["core","upper"],"equipment":[],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-sugar-bear-crawls","name":"Sugar Bear Crawls","text":"Modified bear crawl. In bear crawl position, legs stay straight and bounce side to side and propel the body forward.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["lower"],"equipment":[],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-sugar-cookie","name":"Sugar Cookie","text":"Works best on a baseball field with wet grass and a dirt infield. Do a called number of Supermans while kicking legs in cadence, as though you are swimming in the grass. Sprint to dirt infield and do called hand-release merkins followed by big boys. Rinse and repeat 3 rounds. Replicates a Navy punishment where you have to jump in the ocean followed by exercises on the beach. You get covered by sand and look like a sugar cookie.","kind":"thang","emphasis":["cardio","core","lower","run","upper"],"equipment":["field"],"tags":["mary","routine"]},{"id":"x-suicide-ladder","name":"Suicide Ladder","text":"A shuttle run with an exercise set after each return to the starting line. After each full shuttle run the exercise count goes up by five reps. Repeat until out of time or until no one can take it anymore.","kind":"thang","emphasis":["cardio","run"],"equipment":[],"tags":["routine"]},{"id":"x-suicide-squats","name":"Suicide Squats","text":"Start in normal starting squat position, squat, ~50% of regular squat, then back to normal starting position. Then go to full perpendicular regular proper squat, then back to normal vertical position, then finally go to full deep ankle squat before returning to vertical starting position. Q typically leads this exercise in a cadence of 1, 2, 3, or baby, regular, deep after which PAX reply with the rep count. Great towards the end of a warm-up to transition into the meat of the beatdown.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["cardio","lower","upper"],"equipment":[],"tags":["warmup"]},{"id":"x-suicides","name":"Suicides","text":"Done on basketball court or football field. On basketball court, start at end line, sprint to foul line, touch the ground, sprint back to end line touch the ground, sprint to mid court and touch line, sprint back to end line and touch line, sprint to far foul line and touch ground, sprint back to end line and touch the ground, sprint to far end line and touch the ground, sprint back to original end line. Rinse and repeat.","kind":"thang","emphasis":["cardio","run"],"equipment":["field"],"tags":["routine"]},{"id":"x-sumo-deadlift-high-pull-sdhp","name":"Sumo Deadlift High Pull (SDHP)","text":"Coupon exercise.\nStraddle your vertical coupon in sumo (wide; more than shoulder width apart) stance with feet pointed out. Keep your back straight. Cross your arms and grab the top of your coupon. Lift up and raise your elbows up to your eyes like deadlift. Lower arms until coupon hits the ground. Repeat.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["heavy","upper"],"equipment":["coupon"],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-sumo-squat","name":"Sumo Squat","text":"Feet in wide stance (like a sumo wrestler), squat down and touch ground with both hands. For added fun can add sumo sounds and sumo leg lift between each rep. Also done by some groups as a jump squat with the same touch of the ground.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["core","lower"],"equipment":[],"tags":["mary"]},{"id":"x-super-21","name":"Super 21","text":"Do 1 merkin followed by 1 situp; 2 merkins / 2 situps; 3 merkins / 3 situps, etc., etc. ....... up to 21 merkins/ 21 situps (total of 231 merkins and 231 situps). Insert other exercises in between to allow for recovery (i.e. - Super 21 #1 - #10, Monkey Humpers x 21, Super 21 #11-#13, Mountain Climbers x 21, Super 21 #14-#15, etc.).","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["core","lower","upper"],"equipment":[],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-superman","name":"Superman","text":"Lie prone on the ground with arms, legs, and head held up as high as possible. Hold position to tolerance.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["lower","upper"],"equipment":[],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-superman-merkin","name":"Superman Merkin","text":"Plank starting position. Combine a merkin with the superman move. Go down, superman (release hands, feet and hands up off the ground, move hands from over your head to beside you with arms bent at an angle), hands back under you and push up.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["core","upper"],"equipment":[],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-superman-yellow-sun-and-red-sun","name":"Superman Yellow Sun (and Red Sun)","text":"While in Superman position, perform sun gods. Yellow sun going forward, red sun going reverse. Usually done in cadence. Best when ground is wet or frozen to elicit maximum mumble chatter.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":[],"equipment":[],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-supines","name":"Supines","text":"A sit-up performed from lying flat on your back with your knees flat on the ground. Sit up until you touch your toes.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["core"],"equipment":[],"tags":["mary"]},{"id":"x-surfees","name":"Surfees","text":"This name has been submitted twice: 1) Burpees in the surf, or 2) Similar to a burpee, but you jump up into the surf position with the majority of your weight on your back foot.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["cardio","heavy","lower"],"equipment":["weights"],"tags":["mary"]},{"id":"x-surfer-merkin","name":"Surfer Merkin","text":"Perform a 360-degree jump, then go down for a merkin, pop back up, and repeat.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["lower","upper"],"equipment":[],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-surftanamo","name":"Surftanamo","text":"Surftanamo Similar to Guantanamo, but performed in a straight line along the surf, incorporating the ocean.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":[],"equipment":[],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-suzanne-somers","name":"Suzanne Somers","text":"Suzanne Somers Ode to the \"Thigh Master\" infomercial from everyone''s favorite girl on Three''s Company : Perform a regular squat but point your toes outward. This is a great exercise for the inner thigh. Ensure good form by keeping your stance wide, weight on your heels, and your back straight. Additionally, for a related exercise: All PAX circle up and get on their six. Lay on your right side with your right arm extended above your head. Bend your knees to bring your feet towards your rear with your heels in line with your spine. While maintaining this position, raise your left leg, keeping your knees bent and feet together, while your right leg remains on the ground. Lower your left leg back to the starting position to complete one rep. This can be done in cadence or OYO. After completing enough reps to feel the burn in your hip flexors and glutes, flapjack and repeat on your left side. These look almost as ridiculous as Monkey Humpers and result in a similar burn. Named after the star of the Thigh Master \"fitness\" craze commercials, this exercise is sure to get some mumblechatter flowing.","kind":"thang","emphasis":["cardio","heavy","lower","upper"],"equipment":["weights"],"tags":["routine"]},{"id":"x-sweat-angels","name":"Sweat Angels","text":"Sweat Angels On your six, perform a double dolly (arms and legs 6 inches off the ground) as if making a snow angel.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["core","lower","upper"],"equipment":[],"tags":["mary"]},{"id":"x-swerkins","name":"Swerkins","text":"Swerkins Pushup with feet in in a playground swing. As you complete the pushup, bring your knees into your chest and back out.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["upper"],"equipment":["swing"],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-swingset-orangutans","name":"Swingset Orangutans","text":"Jump up and grab the top of the swingset sideways, then walk hand over hand to the other end.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["lower"],"equipment":["swing"],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-swirley","name":"Swirley","text":"PAX holds the other's legs while they perform push-ups in a handstand position (as if receiving a swirly).","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["lower","upper"],"equipment":[],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-t-bomb","name":"T-Bomb","text":"Start in a crab position, feet together under your 6, hands and feet on the ground. IC feet go: 1) Legs straight, feet together 2) Legs straight and spread 3) Feet back together and legs straight 4) Feet together and back under your 6 That is one rep. Don't let your 6 touch the ground!","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["lower"],"equipment":[],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-taint-tappers","name":"Taint Tappers","text":"Squat with consistency over your cindy - squat and make sure that you get low enough to tap (not smash) your perineum (taint) on the block before rising.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["heavy","lower"],"equipment":["coupon"],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-tamaba","name":"TaMABA","text":"A 4-minute Tabata routine, 8-rounds, 20-second on, 10-second off...\n5 Burpees per round = 40 Burpees","kind":"thang","emphasis":["cardio"],"equipment":["timer"],"tags":["routine"]},{"id":"x-tammy-wynette","name":"Tammy Wynette","text":"Tammy Wynette''s country song hit ''Stand By Your Man'' inspires this exercise. Starting Position: PAX 1 assumes the merkin plank while PAX 2 stands beside \"his man.\" Exercise: PAX 1 performs merkins in sync with PAX 2, who does deep squats. Complete 10 reps either by Q call or on their own. At multiples of 10, partners switch, alternating between merkins and squats. For example: 1, 2, 3...10 (switch) 11, 12, 13...20 (switch) 21, 22, 23...30 (switch) Continue until reaching 200 reps, with 100 merkins and 100 squats per person. On each switch, the merkin participant should explode off the deck, similar to the 5-6 count of a burpee. The Q may substitute other standing or ground exercises as desired. An entire routine could consist of multiple ''Tammy Wynettes.''","kind":"thang","emphasis":["cardio","core","lower","upper"],"equipment":["speaker"],"tags":["partner","routine"]},{"id":"x-tappy-gilmore","name":"Tappy Gilmore","text":"Modified burpee:\nMerkin\nShoulder taps (both sides)\nComplete the burpee (feet forward, stand and jump with hands up)\nThat's one.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["cardio","lower","upper"],"equipment":[],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-tempo-merkin","name":"Tempo Merkin","text":"Regular Merkin, in cadence, with a 3-count down and a 1-count up.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["upper"],"equipment":[],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-tennessee-iditarod","name":"Tennessee Iditarod","text":"Tennessee Iditarod Like the Iditarod race but without snow, huskies, or sleds. Wrap a climbing rope around PAX One''s waist. PAX Two holds the rope, like reins, behind PAX One. PAX Two provides resistance while PAX One pulls \"the sled.\" This works best with an AYG sprint and maximum resistance.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["cardio","run"],"equipment":[],"tags":["competitive","game"]},{"id":"x-the-2020-gobbler-challenge","name":"The 2020 Gobbler Challenge","text":"5 Rounds for Time\nF3 Standard Coupon or equivalent\n• 10 Block Swings\n• 10 reps of associated exercise\n• 15 Block Swings\n• 15 reps of associated exercise\n• 25 Block Swings\n• 25 reps of associated exercise\n• 50 Block Swings\n• 50 reps of associated exercise\n• 400M Run\nRound 1: Hand Release Merkins\nRound 2: Body Weight Squats\nRound 3: Rows\nRound 4: Rowers\nRound 5: Overhead Press\nTotal of 500 Swings and 100 reps of each exercise.","kind":"thang","emphasis":["cardio","heavy","lower","upper"],"equipment":["coupon","swing","weights"],"tags":["benchmark","routine"]},{"id":"x-the-2021-gobbler-challenge","name":"The 2021 Gobbler Challenge","text":"10 Rounds for Time\n• 50M Bear Crawl\n• 10 Rowers\n• 50M Bear Crawl\n• 20 Hand Release Merkins\n• 50M Bear Crawl\n• 10 Rowers\n• 50M Bear Crawl\n• 20 Squats\nRinse and repeat for 10 rounds…","kind":"thang","emphasis":["lower","upper"],"equipment":[],"tags":["benchmark","routine"]},{"id":"x-the-2022-gobbler-challenge","name":"The 2022 Gobbler Challenge","text":"60-minute AMRAP\nF3 Standard Coupon or equivalent\n400M Mosey after each round\n• 10 T Merkins\n• 20 Body Weight Squats\n• 30 Rowers\n• 40 Overhead Presses\n• 50 Block Swings\n• 60 Flutter Kicks (Block Over Head)\n• 70 Rows\n• 80 Lunges\n• 90 Crunches\n• Run 400M or Walk 200M","kind":"thang","emphasis":["cardio","core","heavy","lower","run","upper"],"equipment":["coupon","swing","weights"],"tags":["mary","routine"]},{"id":"x-the-2023-gobbler-challenge","name":"The 2023 Gobbler Challenge","text":"60-minute AMRAP\nF3 Standard Coupon or equivalent\nThis year's workout is in honor of Gobbler’s father, who owned and operated his farm for 40 years. All exercises are inspired by farmwork.\n100m Asymentric Farmer's Walk (Right)\n(Round)*10x Overhead Press w/ Coupon\n100m Overhead Carry\n(Round)*10x Squats\n100m Asymentric Farmer's Walk (Left)\n(Round)*10x Rowers\n100m Overhead Carry\n(Round)*10x Block Swings","kind":"thang","emphasis":["heavy","lower","upper"],"equipment":["coupon","swing"],"tags":["routine"]},{"id":"x-the-2024-gobbler-challenge","name":"The 2024 Gobbler Challenge","text":"60-minute AMRAP\nF3 Standard Coupon or equivalent\n• 50 Sitdown Overhead Presses\n• Run 400M\n• 50 Cactus Squats\n• Run 400M\n• 50 BBSU\n• Run 400M\n• 50 Block Swings\n• Run 400M\n• 50 SSH\n• Run 400M\nRinse and repeat until the time is up...","kind":"thang","emphasis":["cardio","heavy","lower","run","upper"],"equipment":["coupon","swing"],"tags":["routine"]},{"id":"x-the-2025-gobbler-challenge-ladder-of-pain-amrap","name":"The 2025 Gobbler Challenge - “Ladder of Pain” AMRAP","text":"60-min Timer\nF3 Standard Coupon or equivalent\n400M Mosey after each round\n• 10 Overhead Squats\n• +20 HR Merkins\n• +30 Block Swings\n• +40 Front Squats\n• +50 OH Presses\n• +60 Rowers\n• +70 Sumo Squats\n• +80 High Rows\n• +90 LBCs\n• +100 Lunges (2x1)","kind":"thang","emphasis":["cardio","core","heavy","lower","upper"],"equipment":["coupon","swing","timer"],"tags":["mary","routine"]},{"id":"x-the-abdivator","name":"The Abdivator","text":"The Abdivator is an ab workout taking place entirely on the ground. It is a ladder of movements that you will do up and down the body, consisting of the following:\n-10 Flutter Kicks (2 is 1)\n-10 Heels to Heaven\n-10 LBC’s\n-10 American Hammers (2 is 1)\n-10 World War I’s\n-10 American Hammers (2 is 1)\n-10 LBC’s\n-10 Heels to Heaven\n-10 Flutter Kicks (2 is 1)","kind":"thang","emphasis":["core"],"equipment":[],"tags":["mary","routine"]},{"id":"x-the-bonnie-tyler","name":"The Bonnie Tyler","text":"Done to the song “Total Eclipse of the Heart” by Bonnie Tyler. Start in a hollow body hold. Every time the song says “turn around” roll to a Superman and then back to hollow body hold on the next “turn around” alternating between both. During chorus and bridge the Q gets to work the PAX as he sees fit as long they are moving; the only exception is every time the song says “total eclipse of the heart” the group does a burpee. If any PAX takes a rest during the song they must sing the song at the top of their lungs.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["cardio"],"equipment":["speaker"],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-the-bruce-and-the-cait","name":"The Bruce and the Cait","text":"This is a simple Merkin that incorporates elements of balance and core strength. For \"The Bruce,\" start in a regular Merkin position with one leg crossed over the other at the ankle. When you come back up from the Merkin, switch legs. \"The Cait\" is very similar, but you switch legs at the bottom of the Merkin, not the top.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["core","lower","upper"],"equipment":[],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-the-butkus","name":"The Butkus","text":"The Butkus The exercise is named after Rocky''s dog and resembles the rapid toe tapping Rocky Balboa exercise at curbside. Use the curb as a step and alternate stepping as quickly as possible for one minute, then rest for one minute. Continue this pattern for another minute. Complete the sequence in THREE ROUNDS, hopefully without a TKO.","kind":"thang","emphasis":[],"equipment":["bench_wall"],"tags":["routine"]},{"id":"x-the-cooper","name":"The Cooper","text":"Run one lap around the track. Then perform 10 burpees, 10 squats, and 10 merkins. Run another lap, then do 9 burpees, 9 squats, and 9 merkins. Continue this pattern, counting down to 1. It gets pretty brutal when you reach around 5.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["cardio","lower","run","upper"],"equipment":["field"],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-the-cycle","name":"The Cycle","text":"From home plate, bear crawl to 1st base, do 3 burpees, then bear crawl back to home plate. From home plate, bear crawl around the bases to 2nd base, do 6 burpees, then bear crawl back to home plate. From home plate, bear crawl around the bases to 3rd base, do 9 burpees, then bear crawl back to home plate. From home plate, bear crawl around the bases back to home plate.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["cardio"],"equipment":[],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-the-dab","name":"The Dab","text":"10 burpees per minute for 5 minutes, then run 1/4 mile. Repeat this cycle 4 times.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["cardio","run"],"equipment":[],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-the-dirty-dog","name":"The Dirty Dog","text":"The Dirty Dog is a leg and core exercise. It is performed by being on all fours and executed one leg at a time. From the starting position the leg is raised to be parallel to the ground and then brought back to the start position. Proper form requires the leg to be fully parallel to the ground before returning to the starting position. The exercise is done one leg at a time. Pro Tip: the opposite leg can be moved to be more centered under your body to better support your weight and balance.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["core","heavy","lower"],"equipment":["weights"],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-the-donatello","name":"The Donatello","text":"The Donatello To end a workout with suicides on a long set of stairs (e.g., Snake Pit''s Big Boy Stairs, which has 83 stairs and 7 landings).","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["cardio","core"],"equipment":["stairs"],"tags":["mary"]},{"id":"x-the-doogie","name":"The Doogie","text":"It’s like murder bunny minus the coupon. It’s a 4 legged frog hop. It could also be called a “murder frog”. But I like the Doogie.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["heavy","lower"],"equipment":["coupon"],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-the-dumbledore","name":"The Dumbledore","text":"A Dumbledore is an exercise combination compiled of 1 Burpee, 1 Inch Worm, 4 Merkins (2 Shoulder Tap, 2 Knee Tap), 3 Squats.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["cardio","lower","upper"],"equipment":[],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-the-elwood","name":"The Elwood","text":"The Elwood Like High Knees or Chopping Feet, but keep your arms in sync and symmetrical with your feet. When your right hand and right knee are up, your left hand and left knee are down, and vice versa. The PAX can settle into a steady driving quarter-note 4/4 rhythm with this. It''s a great way to bring in the six while keeping heart rates elevated.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["cardio","upper"],"equipment":[],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-the-grateful-dead-aka-dancing-bear","name":"The Grateful Dead (aka Dancing Bear)","text":"Basically, it's a plank-o-rama with a bit of added silliness. Start with 5 Merkins. Rotate 360° in place to the left, raising your left arm, then right arm, and so on. Do 5 Werkins. Rotate 360° in place to the right, raising your left arm, then right arm, and so on. Next, perform 5 Diamond Merkins. While in place, lift your left arm and leg up, then quickly swap to your right arm and leg up. Continue this back and forth as quickly as you can, making sure to fully extend each limb. Now you look like a Dancing Bear!","kind":"thang","emphasis":["core","lower","upper"],"equipment":[],"tags":["routine"]},{"id":"x-the-gross","name":"The Gross","text":"The Gross The beauty of this workout is that you can adjust the intensity based on the level of pain you want to inflict. Pick 12 exercises and perform 12 reps of each. That''s 12x12=144, which is known as a Gross. This workout was first done by Barry Manilow and YHC to showcase the exercises we hate the most, all in one session. It''s guaranteed to generate fantastic mumble chatter.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":[],"equipment":[],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-the-hightower","name":"The Hightower","text":"As the Nation knows, F3 Grand Strand lost Jacob \"Hightower\" Hancher this past weekend while he was serving as a Myrtle Beach Police Officer. End of Watch: 10/03/20. We honored him with a full workout, and this is a part of it, based on a very fitting Bible verse: Matthew 5:9 - \"Blessed are the peacemakers, for they will be called children of God.\" Here are the 5 exercises, each done for 9 reps: Burpees Bodybuilders (a burpee with a plank jack) Triple Merkin Burpees (a burpee with 3 hand-release merkins) Triple Jump Squat Burpees (a burpee with 3 jump squats) Combining them all: Triple Merkin, Triple Jump Squat Bodybuilders (a burpee with 3 hand-release merkins, a plank jack, and 3 jump squats)","kind":"thang","emphasis":["cardio","core","lower","upper"],"equipment":[],"tags":["routine"]},{"id":"x-the-hodor","name":"The Hodor","text":"The Hodor Inspired by Hodor from Game of Thrones and his sole purpose in life to carry a crippled boy. With a cinder block held in front of you, squat until the block touches the ground, stand, rotate the block over your head into a triceps extension, squat again, stand, and rotate the block back in front. That''s 1 rep. Repeat for 30 reps, followed by 1 lap around a 1/4 mile trackâ€''carrying the block.","kind":"thang","emphasis":["cardio","heavy","lower","run","upper"],"equipment":["coupon","field"],"tags":["game","routine"]},{"id":"x-the-incredible-murder-bunny","name":"The Incredible Murder Bunny","text":"Mark a distance of 20 yards from a start line. To the tune of “Incredible” by Oh The Larceny, from the start line perform Murder Bunnies towards the 20 yard marker and once you reach the 20 yard point, perform a Redrum Bunnies back to the start line. During the exercise, anytime the word “incredible” is sung, step to the side of your coupon and perform a burpee. If you don’t finish on the start line, overhead carry your coupon back to the start line if needed when the song ends.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["cardio","heavy"],"equipment":["coupon","speaker"],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-the-jack-squat","name":"The Jack Squat","text":"Start standing with your arms at your sides. As you sink down into your squat, sweep your arms up to clap overhead. Return your arms to your sides as you stand back up. Repeat for reps.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["cardio","lower","upper"],"equipment":[],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-the-jeffrey-leonard","name":"The Jeffrey Leonard","text":"Done either on a baseball diamond or with cones set up like bases. PAX lines up single file at home plate and proceeds to sprint out a single, double, triple and home run with a jog back to home in between each sprint. Can be done as a quick warm up or dragged out to 1 single, 2 doubles, three triples and 4 home runs (done with flaps down of course).","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["cardio","run","upper"],"equipment":["cones"],"tags":["warmup"]},{"id":"x-the-killer-gnat","name":"The Killer Gnat","text":"The Killer Gnat: A small exercise routine attracted to the lights in the park…\nStart with:\n1 Burpee with 1 Merkin\n1 Imperial Squat Walker, each with 1 Squat, 2x1\nMotivators from 1\nMosey to the next light post and add 1 rep.\n.\n2 Burpees, each with 2 Merkins\n2 Imperial Squat Walkers, each with 2 Squats, 2x1\nMotivators from 2\nMosey to the next light post and add 1 rep.\n.\n.\n.\n10 Burpees, each with 10 Merkins\n10 Imperial Squat Walkers, each with 10 Squats, 2x1\nMotivators from 10\nOptions:\nGo to 5 and head back down to 1, or take it all the way to 10.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["cardio","lower","upper"],"equipment":[],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-the-lion-king","name":"The Lion King","text":"The Lion King Start with a coupon held tightly to your chest. Move into a low squat position, lowering the coupon between your knees. As you come up out of the squat, raise the coupon high above your head, thrusting it upward so that it becomes weightless for a fraction of a second. Think of Simba being presented in The Lion King .","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["heavy","lower","upper"],"equipment":["coupon"],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-the-maggie","name":"The Maggie","text":"Coupon chest press while doing flutter kicks.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["core","heavy","upper"],"equipment":["coupon"],"tags":["mary"]},{"id":"x-the-man-from-laramie","name":"The Man from LARAMIE","text":"A stations/circuit workout created by the first Nantan at the Laramie, WY F3 location start, this workout contains seven stations, ideally located in a circle with about 5 yards (minimum) between stations. Mark the stations with cones. Using printed signage for the exercises at each station is helpful.\nPAX start at any station they desire, and complete the exercise at that station, then bear crawl or crab walk to the next station. Rotation is clockwise around the circle. The exercises are done AMRAP based on the Q's choice of duration. 60-90 seconds at each station with 10 seconds to rotate to next station works well for the first round.\nRinse and Repeat as many times as desired, reducing the exercise time at each station for subsequent rounds, with an optional run loop around the larger area between rounds.\nThe exercise stations each start with one of the letters in LARAMIE:\nL-unges; A-merican Hammers; R-everse Crunches; A-lternating Shoulder Taps; M-erkins; I-mperial Squat Walkers and E-leven Burpees.\nQ Tip: Using the Tabata app with a Bluetooth speaker to set the exercise timer and the \"rest\" timer for the rotation makes the rotation rhythm smooth and allows the Q to not be overly encumbered with watching a timer and calling out start, stop, rotate. This circuit pairs nicely with the 7220 (Laramie's Elevation) workout and a 2ndF option of watching the 1955 James \"Jimmy\" Stewart western movie, \"The Man from Laramie\" for a Wyoming trifecta.","kind":"thang","emphasis":["cardio","core","lower","run","upper"],"equipment":["cones","speaker","timer"],"tags":["routine"]},{"id":"x-the-oddjob","name":"The Oddjob","text":"Was introduced to this fantastic warmup by a PAX member named Oddjob and started using it. Great for warmo's or just addition to The Thang. Being in a colder climate area this is a goto for me to get the body warmed up.\n5 burpees | 10 SSH | 4 Burpees | 10 SSH | 3 Burpees | 10 SSH | 2 Burpees | 10 SSH | 1 Burpee | 20 SSH\nBurpees I usually do OYO and SSH are IC. Just wanted to share a fantastic 1-2 combo to get the blood pumping and have many sucking for air.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["cardio","upper"],"equipment":[],"tags":["warmup"]},{"id":"x-the-sheldon-cooper","name":"The Sheldon Cooper","text":"Same as the Cooper just add big boy sit ups. Cooper = Run one lap around the track. Then perform 10 burpees, 10 squats, and 10 merkins. Run another lap, then do 9 burpees, 9 squats, and 9 merkins. Continue this pattern, counting down to 1.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["cardio","core","lower","run","upper"],"equipment":["field"],"tags":["mary"]},{"id":"x-the-sketch","name":"The Sketch","text":"Start face down raised up on hands and feet with knees bent. Pick up opposite hand and foot and pass foot under your body and through until you can touch your butt to the ground then back to where you started. That''s ''one''. Repeat on other side.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":[],"equipment":[],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-the-swimmer","name":"The Swimmer","text":"Using a brick in each hand, the PAX performs the freestyle stroke.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":[],"equipment":[],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-the-w-a-s-h","name":"The W.A.S.H.","text":"The W.A.S.H. Werkins (50, preferably hand-release), American Hammers (100), Step-Ups (150), and Hip Thrusts (200). Perform these exercises either OYO (on your own) or in pairs. If done in pairs, one partner runsâ€''either laps or designated sprintsâ€''while the other completes the exercise. Switch as needed until all exercises are completed.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["cardio","core","lower","run"],"equipment":[],"tags":["mary","partner"]},{"id":"x-the-wifey","name":"The Wifey","text":"Pilates-inspired plank. Shift to one supporting arm, raising the other straight in the air. Switch and do the opposite side. Repeat as necessary.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["core","upper"],"equipment":[],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-the-wolverine","name":"The Wolverine","text":"A big-boy burpee fit for a superhero: From a standing position, drop to plank, do one merkin, tuck your left knee to your chest, do another merkin, tuck your right knee to your chest, perform one more merkin, then stand, jump, and do an overhead clap. That's one rep. Rinse and repeat.","kind":"thang","emphasis":["cardio","core","lower","upper"],"equipment":[],"tags":["routine"]},{"id":"x-theresa","name":"Theresa","text":"Theresa The runner''s version of Mary, primarily consisting of stretching exercises led by the Q to promote optimal recovery and prevent injury after some intense street pounding.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["cardio","mobility"],"equipment":[],"tags":["mary"]},{"id":"x-thigh-master","name":"Thigh Master","text":"Thigh Master Starting position: Begin in a forward lunge with knees slightly bent. Perform the standard lunge movement by bending the back knee until it touches the ground, then return to the starting position. This is done in cadence: count 1 down, 2 up, 3 down, 4 up equals 1 rep. Continue for the set number of reps on the same leg, then switch legs and repeat. The exercise can be performed slowly (with the knee reaching the ground) or quickly, ultimately resulting in an intense \"burn\" in the thighs.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["lower"],"equipment":[],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-three-amigos","name":"Three Amigos","text":"Three members of the PAX assume the air chair position, standing back-to-back-to-back and leaning on each other. Hold this position as you would with wall sits. You can either drop lower and hold or begin to walk as a group in the direction of your choosing. If the group fails to reach the destination, all three must do 10 burpees.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["cardio","lower"],"equipment":["bench_wall"],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-thruster-mountain","name":"Thruster Mountain","text":"A 45 minute mental + physical workout burner. Completed in 1 space the whole time. Used with a coupon or sandbag and a timer. 45 minute workout so be ready for a hot start and no Mary unless it is a 1 hour Black Diamond workout.\nThe entire workout is thrusters. Make sure to use good form and keep back straight and go down to at least your knees with your elbows.\nMinute 1 = 1 Thruster.\nMinute 2 = 2 Thrusters.\nMinute 3 = 3 Thrusters\nContinue until Minute 23 (23 reps) which is the peak of the mountain.\nMinute 24 = 22 Thrusters and continue down the mountain each minute until you are back to 1 rep at the 45 minute mark.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["heavy"],"equipment":["coupon","sandbag","timer"],"tags":["mary"]},{"id":"x-thrusters","name":"Thrusters","text":"Begin from a standing position with block. Move hips back and lower the torso to \"sit\" as deeply as possible while maintaining an upright position. Return to a full standing position while also pressing arms upward to thrust block over your head.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["heavy","upper"],"equipment":["coupon"],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-thunderstruck","name":"Thunderstruck","text":"Thunderstruck The Q plays \"Thunderstruck\" by AC/DC. PAX complete one standard merkin for every \"thunder!\" heard in the song and hold a plank during the rest of the song. It''s an awesome way to end a workout and ensure any remaining energy is fully burned away.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["core","upper"],"equipment":["speaker"],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-tie-fighters","name":"Tie Fighters","text":"In lunge position, perform Baby Arm Circles. Forward BACs with right leg forward. Backward BACs with left leg forward. Switch legs as needed to balance the Force. Repeat for reps.\nAlternate:\nWith a standard four-count, count 1-3, lower the rear knee to the ground. On 4, pop back up.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["lower","upper"],"equipment":[],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-till-i-collapse","name":"Till I Collapse","text":"Play Eminem's \"Till I Collapse\"\nStart in Plank. When Nate Dogg sings the hook (\"Till the roof comes off...\"), do Merkins AMRAP. When Eminem raps, hold the Plank.","kind":"thang","emphasis":["cardio","core","upper"],"equipment":[],"tags":["routine"]},{"id":"x-tippin-coupons-workout","name":"Tippin' Coupons Workout","text":"A competitive team-based workout game played in 3-4 rounds of 5-7 minutes each, requiring ideally two coupons per PAX (minimum one per PAX). Count off by twos to split into two teams: Team 1 tries to end each round with the majority of coupons standing upright on their edge, while Team 2 tries to have them laying flat on their side. To flip a coupon to your team's position, you must first execute the round's prescribed Mode of Transportation (MOT) to reach any coupon, then 'pay' by completing the round's prescribed exercise before flipping it. Start each round with coupons distributed across the field, half upright and half laying down. Example rounds: Sprint + 5 Manmakers Sprint + 5 Murder Bunnies Bear Crawl + 20 American Hammers. This creates constant movement, competition, strategy, and camaraderie while providing a full-body workout","kind":"thang","emphasis":["cardio","core","heavy","run"],"equipment":["coupon","field"],"tags":["competitive","game","mary","routine","team"]},{"id":"x-tony-hawk-burpee","name":"Tony Hawk Burpee","text":"A normal burpee but when you jump, do a 360/180 degree spin in the air each time.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["cardio","lower"],"equipment":[],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-tonya-harding","name":"TONYA HARDING","text":"Hand-release burpee combined with a single-leg vertical jump and an opposite-direction lateral skater hop. 2 sides = 1 complete rep.\nExecution: Descend into a burpee. Chest touches the ground. Hands fully release. Press to standing. Jump vertically off the right foot. Skater hop left. Land on left foot under control. Descend into next burpee. Jump vertically off the left foot. Skater hop right. Land on right foot under control. That is 1 complete rep.\nStandards: Chest must touch ground each rep. Hands must visibly release. Jump must be single-leg. Skater hop must be lateral and opposite direction of the jumping foot. Landing must be controlled before descending.","kind":"thang","emphasis":["cardio","lower","upper"],"equipment":[],"tags":["routine"]},{"id":"x-too-legit-to-quit","name":"Too Legit to Quit","text":"PAX circle up while “Too Legit to Quit” by MC Hammer plays. Every time the word “quit” is heard, PAX perform 1 burpee.\nFor added difficulty, between burpees, PAX continue moving with side straddle hops until the next “quit.”\nCan be modified using any legit movement that requires URGENCY!","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["cardio","core","lower"],"equipment":[],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-tooth-fairy","name":"Tooth Fairy","text":"Tooth Fairy With your feet at the bottom of a staircase (or other steep incline) and your hands on the 3rd or 4th step (depending on PAX height and step size), perform an incline Merkin. At the end of each Merkin, do a small hop with your hands and feet to the next steps (e.g., moving from steps 0 & 3 to steps 1 & 4). The longer the staircase, the better the burn. The name comes from PAX saying, \"If you don''t do this right, you might lose your teeth,\" and because the hop resembles a fairy-like movement.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["upper"],"equipment":["stairs"],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-top-gun","name":"Top Gun","text":"Perform 10 reps each of 5 standing coupon exercises (e.g., Curls, Rows, Deadlifts, Overhead Press, Squats, Lunges) for 10 minutes. Repeat the 5 coupon exercises throughout the entire 10 minutes. Every minute on the minute, the Danger Zone occurs: PAX drop their coupons and perform 3 Burpees, then pick up where they left off with the coupon exercises. To increase the challenge, extend the time, increase the number of Burpees, or raise the reps of the exercises. Acapella versions of Kenny Loggins'' classic tune \"Danger Zone\" are encouraged.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["cardio","heavy","lower","upper"],"equipment":["coupon"],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-tortoise-and-the-hare-b-o-m-b-s","name":"Tortoise and the Hare B.O.M.B.S.","text":"Buddy up with one rucksack per pair. Partner #1 puts on the rucksack and starts walking. Partner #2 performs the first exercise on the list and then chases down Partner #1. When Partner #2 catches up, they swap: Partner #2 takes the rucksack while Partner #1 does the same exercise. Repeat until each partner has completed all exercises 5 times. 5 Burpees (50 per pair) 10 Outlaws (100 per pair) 15 Merkins (150 per pair) 20 Big Boy Sit-ups (200 per pair) 25 Squats (250 per pair)","kind":"thang","emphasis":["cardio","core","lower","ruck","upper"],"equipment":["ruck"],"tags":["mary","partner","routine"]},{"id":"x-tour-de-humpers","name":"Tour de Humpers","text":"Tour de Humpers PAX run around a neighborhood where multiple F3 members live (preferably more than three). At every stop sign, perform a combination of three exercises with the following counts: 10, 20, and 30 (e.g., 10 Merkins, 20 Carolina Dry-Docks, 30 Squats). When passing by a house where an F3 member lives, everyone stops in front of their house and performs 25 Monkey Humpers. This works best if the house has a Ring Doorbell. Invented by Aquaman to prevent fartsacking in an F3-heavy neighborhood in Cherokee.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["cardio","lower","run","upper"],"equipment":[],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-towel-circuit-multiple-resistance-exercises","name":"Towel Circuit (Multiple Resistance Exercises)","text":"Need small hand towels (or larger) and a partner. Circuit of different alternating push-pull dynamic resistance exercises that will work your body from top to bottom if done in this rotation. PAX 1 does the exercises to desired rep count with PAX 2 providing the resistance before switching roles.\nShoulder Press (no towel) - PAX 1 sits down in squat rack shoulder press position with hands facing up. PAX 2 stands behind PAX 1 and presses down on hands providing resistance for PAX 1 while he pushes up like a shoulder press. Repeat to desired rep count.\nCurl (with towels) - PAX 1 Hold towel with palms up. PAX 2 links his towel over to interlock and goes to knee to provide resistance. PAX 1 does curls.\nTricep Extension (with towels) PAX 1 holds towel out with palms down and puts it behind head like a skull crusher. PAX 2 stands behind PAX 1 and links towel and places 1 hand on back of PAX 1. Provide resistance while PAX 1 does tricep extensions (standing skull crushers).\nMerkins (with towel) - lay towel on ground. PAX 1 does Merkins until failure. Once PAX 1 hits failure point; PAX 2 staddles PAX 1 and grabs the towel while providing just enough resistance to help PAX 1 do 5 more Merkins beyond failure point.\nSeated Row (with towels) - PAX 1 & 2 sit down facing each other foot to foot with bent legs. PAX 1 holds towel with hands down. PAX 2 links towels and provides resistance. PAX 1 does rows pulling arms to chest.\nFoot Throwdowns (no towel) -PAX 1 lays down. PAX 2 stands with foot by PAX 1 shoulders while facing PAX 1. PAX 1 holds PAX 2 ankles and does leg lifts while PAX 2 throws down PAX 1 feet. PAX 1 stops the throwdown before his feet hit the ground and proceeds to do a leg lift before PAX 2 stops his feet and throws them down again.","kind":"thang","emphasis":["core","lower","upper"],"equipment":[],"tags":["mary","partner","routine"]},{"id":"x-tower-of-power","name":"Tower of Power","text":"A challenging 9-count merkin variation using two upright coupons (cinderblocks) positioned slightly wider than shoulder-width apart. Execute a sequence of nine push-ups while your hands 'climb' up and down the towers. Start with hands on the ground, perform merkins with hands progressively moving up the coupon (bottom, middle, top), then back down, creating a pyramid pattern. Descend as low as possible on each rep for full range of motion - anything less is a modification. This exercise builds upper body strength, core stability, and challenges you with varying hand positions and heights throughout the sequence, making it significantly harder than standard merkins","kind":"thang","emphasis":["core","heavy","mobility","upper"],"equipment":["coupon"],"tags":["routine"]},{"id":"x-toxic-run","name":"Toxic Run","text":"Named after one of our Pax in the River City region who insists that jumping rope is the best way \"to regulate your heart rate\". This exercise can be part of a warm up or as a cardio element to a beat down.\nThe Q leads the Pax on a run with all Pax carrying a jump rope. At the Q's discretion, the Pax stop and do a number of jumps prescribed by the Q. Once all Pax have completed the required jumps, the run continues. Repeat as long as the Q deems necessary.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["cardio","lower","run","upper"],"equipment":[],"tags":["warmup"]},{"id":"x-traveling-side-straddle-hop","name":"Traveling Side Straddle Hop","text":"A @Side Straddle Hop while moving to a destination","kind":"exercise","emphasis":[],"equipment":[],"tags":["warmup"]},{"id":"x-travolta-merkins","name":"Travolta Merkins","text":"Travolta Merkins Picture Saturday Night Fever while doing Merkins. Start in plank position. The sequence is as follows: First move is a Merkin. 2nd move is right arm high. 3rd move is to reach under and across your body as far as you can. 4th move is to reach high again. 5th move is back to the Merkin. Flapjack with the left and then flapjack until you''re sick of singing \"staying alive, staying alive\"","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["cardio","core","upper"],"equipment":[],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-travoltas","name":"Travoltas","text":"Travoltas In the standard right/left arm-up plank position, lower the raised arm and reach as far as possible underneath and behind your body, then return it to the starting position. Think of the Stayin'' Alive move in the side plank position. Extra credit for using a pointed finger.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["core","upper"],"equipment":[],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-triad-burpee","name":"Triad Burpee","text":"From a standing position, drop down in a wide-arm merkin position and complete one, exploding up and moving hands into a standard merkin position. Complete the standard merkin, exploding up and moving hands into a diamond merkin position. After completing a diamond merkin, pull the feet in and complete the burpee.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["cardio","upper"],"equipment":[],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-triple-check","name":"Triple Check","text":"Teams of three: The first person holds a people's chair, the second person is in plank position in front of them, and the third person sprints 100 yards and back. Repeat this sequence three times.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["cardio","core","run"],"equipment":[],"tags":["team"]},{"id":"x-triple-nickel","name":"Triple Nickel","text":"Triple Nickel Find a hill. Start at the bottom, run to the top, and complete 5 reps of the called exercise. Run back to the bottom and complete 5 reps of the same exercise. This is known as a Triple Nickel (5/5/5). It can also be done on a flat surface with a launch point and a target point.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["cardio","run"],"equipment":[],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-triple-pump-squat-jumps","name":"Triple Pump Squat Jumps","text":"Perform a squat, then rise into a calf raise. Lower back down into the squat position, then come up halfway before returning to the squat position again. Finally, jump up to complete a squat jump.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["lower"],"equipment":[],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-tunnel-of-balls","name":"Tunnel of Balls","text":"Similar to the @Tunnel of Love , PAX line up Balls to the Wall (BTTW) against a long building/wall. The first PAX begins to bear-crawl through the “tunnel” of his BTTW brothers…the next PAX drops from his BTTW position and follows his fellow bear-crawling PAX, etc. Upon exiting the tunnel, each man immediately assumes the BTTW position to extend the tunnel. If the wall ends, turn the corner of the building or reverse direction. AMRAP until brothers step out and the last PAX remains.","kind":"thang","emphasis":[],"equipment":["bench_wall"],"tags":["routine"]},{"id":"x-tunnel-of-love","name":"Tunnel of Love","text":"Tunnel of Love While PAX are planking side by side, one by one, someone crawls under the tunnel formed by the planking PAX. This exercise is best done with a ruck on, in the snow, or anywhere there is accumulated mud.\nBest done for a pre-determined distance like 25 yards. If enough PAX; can be a race between teams to reach the finish line.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["cardio","core","ruck"],"equipment":["ruck"],"tags":["competitive","game","team"]},{"id":"x-turk-n-burp","name":"Turk n Burp","text":"A combination move of a Turkish Get Up and a Burpee: Perform a Turkish Get Up, then flip forward into the squat thrust of the Burpee. Follow with a push-up, complete the Burpee with a jump, and come back down to the ground to start your next rep with the Turkish Get Up. You really need to see it and find your own rhythm. Be the ball...","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["cardio","lower","upper"],"equipment":[],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-turkish-get-up","name":"Turkish Get Up","text":"Turkish Get Up Lying on your back, use only one arm and your legs to \"get up.\"","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["lower","upper"],"equipment":[],"tags":["mary"]},{"id":"x-twerkin","name":"Twerkin","text":"Twerkin Start in the Downward Dog position, with your butt high in the air. Lower your butt slightly and rotate forward while performing the downward half of a Merkin, lowering your head and chest just above the ground as if going under a fence. Continue forward into the Upward Dog position, with your head up and arms extended for the upward half of the Merkin, hands slightly behind your shoulders and chest forward. Return to the starting position by lowering your head and chest, bending your arms, and rotating your body backward, as if going back under the fence. Finish in the Downward Dog position with your butt high. This exercise was performed by Pale Rider and named by Nomaha.","kind":"thang","emphasis":["upper"],"equipment":[],"tags":["routine"]},{"id":"x-twin-tower-of-trust","name":"Twin Tower of Trust","text":"Twin Tower of Trust Each PAX member will hold a brick in each hand, facing another PAX member (for example, with 20 guys total, 10 line up facing each other about 3-4 feet apart). When the Q calls the exercise, they will hold the bricks straight out at eye level, with no touching of bricks or partners'' bricks. The person on the end will bear crawl under everyone holding the bricks (this is where the trust comes in). When they reach the end, they will pick a side and hold their bricks up. The next person then goes, and this process continues. This exercise will last for 25-50 yards, depending on what the Q specifies.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["cardio"],"equipment":[],"tags":["partner"]},{"id":"x-twinkle-toes","name":"Twinkle Toes","text":"Twinkle Toes This exercise is an Al Gore (holding a squat with your arms and hands extended in front of you) while performing calf raises. It was originally created by F3 Knoxville''s Anchorman and is heavily used in F3 Knoxville JUCO.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["lower","upper"],"equipment":[],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-two-coupon-dip","name":"Two Coupon Dip","text":"A tricep exercise performed using two coupons (cinderblocks or similar) positioned parallel to each other at shoulder-width apart. Place one hand on top of each coupon and support your body weight with straight arms, legs extended in front or bent behind you. Lower your body by bending your elbows until you achieve full range of motion (upper arms parallel to ground or lower), then press back up to the starting position. The elevated hand position allows for deeper dips than floor-based variations, significantly increasing the challenge to your triceps, chest, and shoulders while engaging your core for stability","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["core","heavy","lower","mobility","upper"],"equipment":["coupon","weights"],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-tyfbaf-thank-you-for-being-a-friend","name":"TYFBAF (Thank You For Being A Friend)","text":"Play the Golden Girls theme song aka Thank You For Being a Friend. Every time the word friend is sung, you do a burpee. The rest of the time you should be doing side straddle hops or high knees. Can be done as a warmup.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["cardio","upper"],"equipment":["speaker"],"tags":["warmup"]},{"id":"x-uhaul","name":"UHaul","text":"UHaul Begin in a standing position, holding a kettlebell or coupon with both hands at chest level. The exercise is performed in cadence with the following movements: Count 1, chest press straight out (parallel to the ground). Count 2, return the kettlebell to the chest. Count 3, perform an incline chest press at a 45-degree upward angle. Count 4, return the kettlebell to the chest.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["heavy","upper"],"equipment":["coupon","weights"],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-ultimate-football","name":"Ultimate Football","text":"Played like Ultimate Frisbee but with a football. The scoring team calls out an exercise for the entire PAX, but the ''losing'' team has to do double the amount. For example, if the exercise is ''10 burpees,'' the scoring team does 10 burpees, while the losing team does 20 burpees. If one team scores three times in a row, that team has to run a lap around the field in addition to their exercises. Play for an hour, usually around the holidays.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["cardio","core","run","upper"],"equipment":["field"],"tags":["team"]},{"id":"x-ultimate-frisburpee","name":"Ultimate Frisburpee","text":"This game is similar to ultimate frisbee but includes penalty burpees. On the 1st turnover, all PAX do 5 burpees. On the 2nd turnover, it's 4 burpees; on the 3rd, 3 burpees; on the 4th turnover, 2 burpees; and on the 5th turnover, 1 burpee. If neither team has scored, the remainder of the point is played like regular ultimate frisbee. The burpee count resets after each point. You do not have to wait for all PAX to finish their burpees before beginning play (i.e., it is advantageous to finish your burpees quickly). The game is usually played for about 20 minutes and is a favorite in F3 Hampton Roads.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["cardio","core"],"equipment":[],"tags":["finisher","game","team"]},{"id":"x-uncle-mary","name":"Uncle Mary","text":"For the Mary, at the end of a workout, the Q leads an ab exercise, doing reps until a PAX calls \"Uncle\". Then they lead the next ab exercise until another PAX calls \"Uncle\". Rinse and repeat until the end.","kind":"thang","emphasis":[],"equipment":[],"tags":["mary","routine"]},{"id":"x-underdog","name":"Underdog","text":"A supine pull-up is performed while hanging below a swing. Lying horizontally on the ground with your arms extended and hanging below the swing, lift your chest up toward the swing (a supine pull-up). This exercise can also be performed on a fence, bench, bars, or similar structures.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["upper"],"equipment":["bench_wall","pull_up_bar","swing"],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-up-dog","name":"Up Dog","text":"A conscious effort to catch breath and slow breathing so the following exercises can be performed with good attention to form and effort.\nExample:\nQ: Next exercise is.... Up Dog!\nExhausted PAX: What's Up Dog?\nQ: Give us a 10 count, that's what's up.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":[],"equipment":[],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-up-downs","name":"Up downs","text":"Up downs Chop your feet or do high knees. On the Q''s signal, drop your chest to the ground and bounce back up, then resume chopping your feet or doing high knees.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["cardio","upper"],"equipment":[],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-up-straddle-hop","name":"Up Straddle Hop","text":"Side Straddle Hops performed using one leg. It's suggested to do 25-30 reps on each leg in cadence. I recently tore my calf and have been on injury reserve (IR) for a bit. Not wanting to miss our monthly convergence, I grabbed my kettlebell to use when the PAX were doing exercises I couldn't participate in and headed out to the beatdown. We circled up, and the first exercise called was SSH. Not wanting to put pressure on my torn calf, I started hopping on one leg in cadence while still doing the upper body motion. Apparently, it looked funny, as the PAX started laughing and then joined in. Forty-three men hopping on one leg and waving their arms would have looked awesome to any passersby! Doing 30 IC of those completely exhausted my right (good) leg, so I figured it might need a name. Let the PAX name it and do 25-30 IC with each leg. It burns! For good measure, the Q next called for 10 OYO burpees. I tried to do them one-legged, and after 2 burpees, I had absolutely no strength left in my good leg. So, doing burpees on one leg could be an interesting add-on to the exercise.","kind":"thang","emphasis":["cardio","core","heavy","lower","upper"],"equipment":["weights"],"tags":["routine"]},{"id":"x-upper-decker","name":"Upper Decker","text":"Best used with sturdy picnic table or stairs. PAX will step up to the tabletop (two steps) when on top perform one air squat and step down. In reference to the movie MaGruber","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["lower"],"equipment":["bench_wall","stairs"],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-upright-row","name":"Upright Row","text":"Upright Row Grab a rock, concrete block (coupon), log, kettle bell, or a small 2.0. Use a close overhand grip at waist level and lift the object up to your chin. (Thanks to Clark in NoCo.)","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["heavy","upper"],"equipment":["coupon"],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-uptown-50","name":"Uptown 50","text":"Uptown 50 There are 10 cones with the following exercises written on them: Burpee Broad Jump, Crab Walk, Partner Carry (P1), Partner Carry (P2), Alligator Crawl, Wheelbarrow (P1), Wheelbarrow (P2), Nur (Run Backwards), AYG (Sprint), and Bear Crawl. The cones are placed at the end zone and at the 50-yard line. PAX partner up and line up on the goal line. Start by doing 10 burpees, then travel to the 50-yard line using the method indicated on the first cone. Once you reach the 50-yard line, do 10 burpees and travel back using the method on the next cone. Repeat this process until you have used all the methods on the cones and completed your 100 burpees. Continue until audible swearing is heard or until time runs out.","kind":"thang","emphasis":["cardio","lower","run","upper"],"equipment":["cones","field"],"tags":["partner","routine"]},{"id":"x-v-up","name":"V-Up","text":"A challenging core exercise that targets the entire abdominal region. Lie flat on your back with arms extended overhead and legs straight. Simultaneously lift your legs and upper body off the ground, reaching your hands toward your toes to form a \"V\" shape with your body at the top of the movement. Keep your legs and arms as straight as possible throughout. Lower back down with control to the starting position and repeat. This exercise builds serious core strength, hip flexor endurance, and improves coordination while working both the upper and lower abs simultaneously.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["core","lower","upper"],"equipment":[],"tags":["mary"]},{"id":"x-v-up-roll-up","name":"V-Up Roll-Up","text":"Performed in a 4-count cadence, this exercise is best known from P90X''s Ab Ripper. Start by lying flat with your arms extended above your head. Perform a full sit-up and touch your toes. As you return to the starting position, when your mid-back touches the ground, begin to raise your legs to a 45-degree angle and hold them there. Then, crunch up and touch your toes while keeping your legs in position.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["cardio","core","lower","upper"],"equipment":[],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-vacuum-cleaners","name":"Vacuum Cleaners","text":"Vacuum Cleaners Partner work is done in the wheelbarrow position, ideally in a parking lot or a lined field. Starting at the first line, wheelbarrow to the second line and perform five Derkins. Reverse the wheelbarrow back to the first line for one rep. Flapjack after the agreed-upon number of reps have been completed.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["cardio","upper"],"equipment":["field"],"tags":["partner"]},{"id":"x-van-goghda","name":"Van Goghda","text":"Van Goghda Think of lying down like Abe Vigoda. On your back with your legs spread, sit up while reaching as high as possible with one hand. Once you reach the peak, lower your hand forward and cross over to touch the opposite foot, then reverse the motion back down. Flip to the other side and repeat. For a harder variation, cross your legs.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["core","lower"],"equipment":[],"tags":["mary"]},{"id":"x-vertigos","name":"Vertigos","text":"Vertigos Run across a field or any stretch of road or earth, but with each step, rotate so that you are constantly spinning as you move forward (clockwise or counter-clockwise, your choice). If this doesn''t make you dizzy, then not much will.","kind":"thang","emphasis":["cardio","mobility","run"],"equipment":["field"],"tags":["routine"]},{"id":"x-vicious-circle","name":"Vicious circle","text":"Vicious circle The PAX travel single-file around the bases of a baseball field. The last man (or last 2 men in larger groups) peels off, runs to the pitcher''s mound, performs 5 of an exercise, and then rejoins the PAX at the front. Repeat this for all PAX. Change the mode of travel and the exercises accordingly. For example: PAX bear crawl around the bases. The last man moseys to the pitcher''s mound for 5 Merkins and then returns to the front of the PAX. Or, PAX lunge walk around the bases. The last man moseys to the pitcher''s mound for 5 jump squats and then returns to the front.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["cardio","lower","upper"],"equipment":["field"],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-wake-up-chop-suey","name":"Wake Up! (Chop Suey!)","text":"Play System of a Down's \"Chop Suey!\"\nFast verses = High Knees / Fast Feet (Sprint in place). Slow melodic chorus (\"Father into your hands...\") = Slow, deep Sumo Squats.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["cardio","lower","run"],"equipment":[],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-walk-and-chew-gum","name":"Walk and Chew Gum","text":"Perform Overhead Press repeatedly while walking. Best performed at least 4 times as an MOT (mode of transportation) between other exercise sets at distances of at least 100 yards per movement.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["cardio","upper"],"equipment":[],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-walk-like-an-egyptian","name":"Walk Like An Egyptian","text":"Walk Like An Egyptian The PAX line up single-file, about an arm''s length apart. In unison, the entire PAX lunges forward with their right leg and holds the lunge, while the last PAX jailbreaks to the front of the line. The entire PAX then recovers and lunges forward with their left leg and holds the lunge, while the last PAX jailbreaks to the front. This process continues until all PAX have cycled through at least once. To add some extra core work, have the PAX rotate their torso (e.g., rotate the chest right while in the right leg lunge) and hold the rotation throughout.","kind":"thang","emphasis":["core","lower","upper"],"equipment":[],"tags":["routine"]},{"id":"x-walk-the-dog","name":"Walk The Dog","text":"Perform any carry with a coupon.\nExample carries: coupon on one shoulder, suitcase (one hand to your side), food baby (front near abdomen), binocular (front near face), rifle (above head), child (front on one hip, one arm).","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["heavy","upper"],"equipment":["coupon"],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-walkerstrong","name":"Walkerstrong","text":"Walkerstrong The PAX circles up and performs 2 minutes of Imperial Walkers, with the last 30 seconds as AMRAP. The exercise is named in honor of Walker Phillips, 2.0 of NailPop in Lexington. A variation of this exercise involves each PAX taking a turn praying aloud with the group while continuing the Imperial Walkers until everyone has prayed.","kind":"thang","emphasis":[],"equipment":[],"tags":["routine"]},{"id":"x-wall-conveyor","name":"Wall Conveyor","text":"Wall Conveyor All PAX line up against the wall of a building in the Balls to the Wall (BTTW) position. The first PAX at one end of the line drops down from BTTW, runs to the end of the line, and then returns to the BTTW position. The next PAX follows, and this process repeats until the Q says to stop or you run out of wall space.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["cardio","run"],"equipment":["bench_wall"],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-wall-worms","name":"Wall Worms","text":"Wall Worms Start in the Balls to the Wall (BTTW) position. Inch your way to the left or right by moving your hands on the ground and your feet on the wall. Alternatively, you can inch your hands out and your feet down the wall into a more horizontal position, and then move back up.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":[],"equipment":["bench_wall"],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-walls-of-jericho","name":"Walls of Jericho","text":"Walls of Jericho It''s Biblical and it will hurt... just as Joshua was instructed to do. Walls of Jericho (WOJ) is usually performed around a large building. Pick 7 different exercises, complete 7 reps of each, and then run one lap around the building. Repeat this process for 7 laps. For an extra challenge, you can have the PAX shout on the last set to pay homage to the story.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["cardio","run"],"equipment":[],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-walmart-burpee","name":"Walmart Burpee","text":"The burpee's discount-store cousin, where the fun is dialed back. Start by dropping into a squat like a normal burpee, but continue all the way down to your back, rolling onto your shoulder blades. Roll forward, and when your feet hit the ground, place your hands in front and jump back into a plank. The rest follows a standard burpee: perform a merkin, a thruster, and then jump with your hands overhead.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["cardio","core","lower","upper"],"equipment":[],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-war-hammer","name":"War Hammer","text":"War Hammer This exercise is a combination of a World War II sit-up and four American Hammer reps at the top of the sit-up. It is similar to Captain Thor but does not include an ascending count.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["core"],"equipment":[],"tags":["mary"]},{"id":"x-wave-of-merkins","name":"Wave of Merkins","text":"Wave of Merkins Circle up and get into plank position. The first person does one merkin, then the next person to the right does a merkin, creating a wave effect around the circle. When it reaches the first person again, they perform 2 merkins, and the wave continues. Repeat this pattern all the way up to 10 merkins and then back down. Stay in plank position the entire time.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["core","upper"],"equipment":[],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-we-re-not-worthy","name":"We're Not Worthy","text":"Everyone remembers Wayne and Garth from Wayne's World: \"We're not worthy, we're not worthy.\" With arms extended outward, lower and raise your arms. Okay, okay, it's a front raise. But this is F3! It's extremely effective when mixed with other arm exercises or by adding bricks or concrete blocks.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["upper"],"equipment":[],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-webbicide","name":"Webbicide","text":"Webbicide A standard suicide but instead of touching each line the pax does an increasing number of merkins at each line. Run to the first line, do one merkin, run back to start, run to next line, do two merkins, and so on until you get to 10. A running form of the Jack Webb usually done on a large parking lot.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["cardio","run","upper"],"equipment":[],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-weezy-jefferson","name":"Weezy Jefferson","text":"Weezy Jefferson Ab exercise performed lying on your back with hands under your bum and legs raised to a 90-degree angle. In cadence, lower your legs quickly toward the ground, stop them 6 inches above the ground without touching, and then move them back up to 90 degrees (like you''re \"movin'' on up\" like George & Weezy). This exercise can also be used in place of foot-push-downs during a Guantanamo by pushing the 90-degree legs from the head side. (Thanks to DÃ¶ner Kebab in Richmond.)","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["lower"],"equipment":[],"tags":["mary"]},{"id":"x-welcome-party","name":"Welcome Party","text":"Welcome Party Invite PAX to arrive 15 minutes before the workout. Any PAX can \"host,\" promising coffee, donuts, a safe space, etc., but instead, deliver pre-workout pain. For example, do rounds of burpees for 10 minutes, aiming for at least 100. Feel free to add burpee variations if desired. Bring some aggressive music to accompany the burpees.","kind":"thang","emphasis":["cardio"],"equipment":["speaker"],"tags":["routine"]},{"id":"x-welsh-dragons","name":"Welsh Dragons","text":"Welsh Dragons Stay in the plank position the entire time. Bear crawl forward 4 steps, then do 1 merkin, 1 plank jack, and tap the back of each shoulder once. Repeat, adding 1 rep to each exercise each timeâ€''bear crawl forward 4 steps, then do 2 merkins, 2 plank jacks, and 2 shoulder taps. Continue until you reach 10 reps of each exercise, have covered 30-50 feet, or until your arms give outâ€''whichever comes first.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["core","upper"],"equipment":["stairs"],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-wembys","name":"Wembys","text":"Inspired by a modern day sports moment and the famous F3 exercise, the @Nolan Ryan.\nPAX goes into a traditional plank position. Lifts one arm and punches under the body in a controlled manner. Flagrantly jerks elbow back with maximum force. Recommended in sets of 10 on each side.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["core","upper"],"equipment":[],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-werewolf","name":"Werewolf","text":"Werewolf Start in the downward-facing dog position (high plank), transition to a low plank, then to upward-facing dog, and back to downward-facing dog in one smooth motion. On the return to downward-facing dog, the PAX should push through the shoulders to really feel the burn. It kind of looks like you are going from downward dog to howling at the moon. The first time the Smokehouse men did it, there was a full moon over Batesburg-Leesville.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["core","upper"],"equipment":[],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-werkin","name":"Werkin","text":"A push-up variation with hands positioned wider than shoulder-width apart, emphasizing the chest and outer pectorals. Start in a plank position with your body straight and arms extended wider than your shoulders. Lower your body down by bending your elbows, keeping your core tight and back flat, then press back up to the starting position. The wider hand placement shifts more emphasis to the chest muscles compared to a standard merkin. Can be counted as 'down one' or '1, 2, 3' and can be modified by dropping to your knees if needed. This variation builds upper body strength with a focus on chest development and shoulder stability","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["core","upper"],"equipment":[],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-whamo-lunge-walks","name":"Whamo lunge walks","text":"Whamo lunge walks Named after the toy company Wham-O. One pax throws a frisbee. All pax sprint in that direction until frisbee lands. When it lands, all PAX stop and then lunge-walk until they get to the frisbee. Can be modified with duck walk, crab walk, whatever.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["cardio","lower","run","upper"],"equipment":[],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-wheel-of-animal-walk","name":"Wheel of Animal Walk","text":"Wheel of Animal Walk Essentially a Wheel of Merkin with Animal Walks between each stage. Find a parking lot 40-60 yards across, preferably with an incline (the steeper, the better). Begin at the bottom of the incline. Frog Hop across and do 10 merkins with both hands on the curb. Bear Crawl across and do 10 merkins with your left hand on the curb. Duck Walk across and do 10 merkins with your feet on the curb. Crab Walk across and do 10 merkins with your right hand on the curb. (North Augusta PAX LOVE this one.)","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["cardio","upper"],"equipment":["bench_wall"],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-wheel-of-merkin","name":"Wheel of Merkin","text":"Grab a piece of curb and start in an incline plank position. Perform a set number of reps in each merkin position before rotating to the next. Begin with an incline merkin. Then, rotate 90 degrees clockwise until your body is parallel to the curb, with your left hand and foot on the curb and your right hand and foot off it. Perform a merkin, then rotate another 90 degrees and perform a decline merkin. Rotate 90 degrees again and repeat, this time with your right hand and foot on the curb and your left hand and foot off it.","kind":"thang","emphasis":["core","upper"],"equipment":["bench_wall"],"tags":["routine"]},{"id":"x-when-animals-attack","name":"When Animals Attack","text":"Mark off an area (kill zone). All PAX must remain in the area at all times. One PAX (the attacker or \"it\") starts in one corner, while all the other PAX start in the opposite corner. Assume the bear crawl position and stay there. The attacker begins to chase the other PAX throughout the kill zone (in bear crawl mode). Once contact is made with a PAX (\"tag\"), the contacted PAX becomes the new attacker, returns to their corner, and the game starts over. Adjust the exercise based on the size of the kill zone and the number of people. Variation: Instead of tagging, you must take your prey down to the ground (F3 meets jiu-jitsu), which should be safe from your hands and knees.","kind":"thang","emphasis":[],"equipment":[],"tags":["game","routine"]},{"id":"x-wilt-chamberlains","name":"Wilt Chamberlains","text":"Wilt Chamberlains Named for Wilt Chamberlain''s NBA record 100-point game. Space the cones 100 feet apart, the length of a basketball court. Line up at the first cone, do 100 LBCs, then run to the second cone and do 100 squats. Return to the first cone to do 100 flutter kicks (each leg), and then finish at the second cone with 100 lunges (50 each leg). This is a nice ab and lower body routine.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["cardio","core","lower","run"],"equipment":["cones"],"tags":["game","mary"]},{"id":"x-windmill","name":"Windmill","text":"Standing windmill exercise: Stand with feet shoulder-width apart, one arm straight up, and the other hand inside the opposite leg. Rotate torso and push hips back. Eyes should follow the back hand.\nVariations:\nAbe Vigoda = Slow 4-count","kind":"thang","emphasis":["lower","upper"],"equipment":[],"tags":["routine","warmup"]},{"id":"x-windshield-wipers","name":"Windshield Wipers","text":"Windshield Wipers This is a 10-count exercise. Start on your six with legs together at 90 degree angle. First, move both legs together to the left, till they are 6 inches from the ground. Then go to the right till they are six inches from the ground all the way to the right. Finally, go back to the middle to end the 10-count. Rinse and repeat.","kind":"thang","emphasis":["lower"],"equipment":[],"tags":["mary","routine"]},{"id":"x-wing-nut","name":"Wing Nut","text":"Wing Nut Done in cadence. Start with sitting on a picnic table with your feet under the bench, lean back to approximately 15 degrees with your back and neck straight. With your fists touching in front of your chest and elbows pointing parallel with your shoulders, rotate your waist so that each elbow touches the tabletop. Complete in a 4-count cadence.","kind":"thang","emphasis":["upper"],"equipment":["bench_wall"],"tags":["routine"]},{"id":"x-wojo-squats","name":"Wojo Squats","text":"Named after Duke basketball player Steve Wojciechowski, who would slap the floor, these are squats where you slap the pavement at the bottom of each rep, just like an overly energetic Duke basketball player.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["cardio","lower"],"equipment":[],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-wood-chopper","name":"Wood Chopper","text":"Grab a sandbag (for the added instability) or a paver. Start in a crouch, twisted to the left, with the sandbag outside your left shin (1). Swing the sandbag up across your body to the right to a standing press position, with the weight outside your right shoulder (2). Swing back down to the left to the starting position (3). Back up (4). Swing vigorously enough to require deceleration at both the top and bottom really go for it, as if you were chopping wood. Perform this for a 20-count in cadence. Switch sides to start on the right and repeat. Intermingle with another exercise for recovery, and complete 3 sets for a true crowd-pleaser. Expect some serious soreness from hips to armpits. Disclaimer: Maintain good form and straight backs! Those with bad backs or unfit FNGs should modify to jumpies with the weight.","kind":"thang","emphasis":["heavy","lower","upper"],"equipment":["sandbag","swing","weights"],"tags":["routine"]},{"id":"x-wooly-worm","name":"Wooly Worm","text":"Place your feet on the swing seat while in a plank position. Bring your knees to your chest, pulling the swing with your feet for a suspended reverse crunch (inchworm movement). Introduced at SVU during the Wooly Worm Festival.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["cardio","core","upper"],"equipment":["swing"],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-world-war-i-sit-up","name":"World War I Sit-up","text":"World War I sit-up Starting on your six with arms fully extended above your head and legs straight, raise your upper body while keeping your arms straight above your head until you are upright. Then, bring your arms as far forward as possible, trying to touch your toes. Return to the starting position, flat on the ground.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["core","lower","upper"],"equipment":[],"tags":["mary"]},{"id":"x-world-war-i-snow-angel","name":"World War I Snow Angel","text":"World War I Snow Angel (Only to be called in the snow) Perform the same motion as a WW1 sit-up, but when you are in the extended position on your back, make motions to create a snow angel on counts 3 and 4.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["core"],"equipment":[],"tags":["mary"]},{"id":"x-world-war-ii-sit-up","name":"World War II Sit-up","text":"Done in cadence. Start on your back with knees bent, both arms extended above your head on the ground. On count one, Pax will move arms to bent knees while sitting up. On count two, PAX will return to the starting position with arms extended over the head on the ground. Counts 3 and 4 will repeat Counts 1 and 2. That is one rep.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["core","upper"],"equipment":[],"tags":["mary"]},{"id":"x-world-war-iii-sit-up","name":"World War III Sit-up","text":"The WW3 sit-up is a one-coupon exercise where, starting in the down position, you will execute a chest-press with the coupon and then bring the coupon to your knees on the up. Then execute a final shoulder press before the down, rinse and repeat.","kind":"thang","emphasis":["core","heavy","upper"],"equipment":["coupon"],"tags":["routine"]},{"id":"x-worst-merkin-ever","name":"Worst Merkin Ever","text":"Worst Merkin Ever Three merkins performed in succession with no break in form: 1 Wide Arm Merkin, 1 Regular Merkin, and 1 Diamond Merkin = 1 Worst Merkin Ever.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["upper"],"equipment":[],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-worst-merkin-ever-crawl","name":"Worst Merkin Ever Crawl","text":"WMD Crawl A Bear Crawl executed by performing 5 Werkins, then crawling 10 steps with hands set out wide, followed by 5 Regular Merkins and crawling 10 steps with hands in a normal position, and finishing with 5 Diamond Merkins and crawling 10 steps with hands set close. Rinse and repeat until the desired distance has been traveled.","kind":"thang","emphasis":["upper"],"equipment":["stairs"],"tags":["routine"]},{"id":"x-worst-worst-merkin-ever","name":"Worst Worst Merkin Ever","text":"That''s right, it can ALWAYS be worse! Done in cadence: start with a Crucible Merkin on 1, a Wercan on 2, a regular Merkin on 3, and a Diamond Merkin on 4. Do ten of these, and you''ll agree it''s the worst of the worst.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["upper"],"equipment":[],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-wounded-bear-crawl","name":"Wounded Bear Crawl","text":"Wounded Bear Crawl Using a curb, crawl along it with one arm and one leg on the curb and the other arm and leg on the asphalt or concrete next to it. You''ll feel like a wounded animal.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["lower","upper"],"equipment":["bench_wall"],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-x-gon-give-it-to-ya","name":"X Gon' Give It To Ya","text":"Play DMX's \"X Gon' Give It To Ya\"\nOn your six to perform \"X-Factors\": arms and legs wide forming an \"X\". Crunch up touching opposite hand to opposite foot. Keep the rhythm aggressive.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["cardio","core","lower","upper"],"equipment":[],"tags":["mary"]},{"id":"x-x-cross-sit-up","name":"X-Cross Sit-up","text":"Performed in slow cadence. Starting position: Lie on your back with your legs and arms extended in an ''X'' position. On count 1, simultaneously lift your left leg and right arm to meet above your core, keeping both as straight as possible while touching your right hand to your left leg. Return to the starting ''X'' position. On count 2, switch to lifting your right leg and left arm, again keeping both as straight as possible while touching your left hand to your right leg above your core. Return to the starting ''X'' position. On count 3, execute a knee-up by lifting your shoulders and legs off the ground and touching your toes as you bring your knees up, with only your lower back in contact with the ground. On count 4, extend your arms and legs and return to the starting ''X'' position. That completes one rep.","kind":"thang","emphasis":["core","lower","upper"],"equipment":[],"tags":["mary","routine"]},{"id":"x-x-factor","name":"X-Factor","text":"X-Factor Start on your back with your arms and legs spread out to resemble an X. Start the move with a V-up, with your right arm touching your left shin, then lower down and perform another V-up with your left arm touching your right shin. The opposite arm and leg stay down. That''s one rep. For a bonus, raise your arms and legs 6 inches off the ground and start the move from there, keeping the down arm and leg at 6 inches while performing the V-up.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["core","lower","upper"],"equipment":[],"tags":["mary"]},{"id":"x-xs-and-os","name":"Xs and Os","text":"Lie down on your six, with your arms and legs spread out into an X position. This is the 'X' in Xs and Os. Pull your arms and legs toward your body, curling up into a ball when the Q calls out 'O'. This is the 'O' in Xs and Os. Then move back into the X position when the Q calls out 'X' again.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["lower","upper"],"equipment":[],"tags":["mary"]},{"id":"x-xys","name":"XYs","text":"XYs 4-count hybrid of Rosalita with a Flutter Kick: Start with legs at a 45-degree angle. Counts 1 and 2 are the Rosalita, with Counts 3 and 4 going directly into the Flutter Kick.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["core","lower"],"equipment":[],"tags":["mary"]},{"id":"x-yoke-walk","name":"Yoke Walk","text":"Yoke Walk Many different variations with this one, but you''ll need something heavy to carry across your shoulders and behind your neck. Can involve a heavy bar for a single pax member or pax can team up with heavy objects like logs.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["upper"],"equipment":[],"tags":["team"]},{"id":"x-yul-brynner","name":"Yul Brynner","text":"Yul Brynner was an actor in the 1960s movie The Magnificent Seven . The Magnificent Seven Merkins involve progressing through seven different types of merkins without stopping or holding plank between each one: Carolina Dry Dock, Wide Merkin, Normal Merkin, Ranger Merkin, Diamond Merkin, Crucible Merkin, and Chuck Norris Merkin. Rinse and repeat on the Q''s call.","kind":"thang","emphasis":["core","upper"],"equipment":[],"tags":["routine"]},{"id":"x-yurpee","name":"Yurpee","text":"A Burpee variation in honor of the Ruskie (Yuri Verkhoshansky), who developed plyometrics to train Olympians: The merkin at the bottom of the burpee is a clap-merkin, and on the up portion, there are two tuck jumps per burpee. Basically, it's a Clurpee with two tuck jumps.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["cardio","lower","upper"],"equipment":[],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-yves-poll","name":"Yves Poll","text":"Yves Poll (pronounced \"eves pole\" in English) is a term for running backwards or backpedaling. He was a French marathon runner who ran backwards all the time. Submitted by SkyHook in Houston, whose father-in-law was an ultramarathoner and one of Yves'' running buddies.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["cardio","run"],"equipment":[],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-zebra-butt-kicks","name":"Zebra Butt-Kicks","text":"Ever seen a zebra launch another Savannah beast into the sky? If so, it was with that butt kick that they do so perfectly. Virtually no exercises wear out our glutes in F3. The zebra kick is all about the gluteus maximus. From plank, bend your knee to 90 degrees and kick skyward. High reps, imagine your heel busting up the chops of a lioness.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["core","lower"],"equipment":[],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-zig-zag-hops","name":"Zig-Zag Hops","text":"Find a beam, log, or other object even a PAX member or two (who has signed a disclaimer) to jump over. Start on one side and hop over in a zig-zag fashion from one end to the other. Added because we need something that begins with a Z.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["lower"],"equipment":[],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-zombie-crawl","name":"Zombie Crawl","text":"Start in a plank position and crawl with both legs dragging behind. For an added challenge, try a Zombie Crawl on an incline.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["core","lower"],"equipment":[],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-zombie-crunch","name":"Zombie Crunch","text":"LBC with both legs bent/laid to one side (like a dead zombie). Then repeat for other side.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["cardio","core","lower"],"equipment":[],"tags":["mary"]},{"id":"x-zombie-merkins","name":"Zombie Merkins","text":"A challenging push-up variation. With your hands shoulder-width apart, lower your body until your chest touches the ground, keeping your elbows close to your sides, then press back up to the starting position. At the top of the Merkin, raise one hand horizontally forward, then back down to the ground. At the top of the next Merkin, raise the alternate hand forward, then back down to the ground.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["upper"],"equipment":[],"tags":[]},{"id":"x-zombie-walk","name":"Zombie Walk","text":"A lunge walk over a long distance that causes the PAX to groan and stumble like the Walking Dead.","kind":"exercise","emphasis":["lower"],"equipment":[],"tags":[]}]};
